hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6601","6595 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Ibn al-Sammak narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muslim, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not leave the evening meal even with a handful of dry dates, for leaving it causes old age. This is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Ibn al-Sammak alone transmitted it."
"6602","6596 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril fed me harisah, strengthening my back with it for standing at night. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Muhammad ibn al-Hajjaj."
"6603","6597 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yunus informed me, from Ibn Shihab, that Ubaydillah ibn Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to him from Abdullah ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent the night at Dhu al-Hulayfah at the start of his journey, and prayed in its mosque. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus."
"6604","6598 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Bishr narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come to me a people from those who were with me, then when they are raised to me and I see them, they will be snatched away from me, so I will say: O Lord, my companions, my companions, so it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik; al-Hasan ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"6605","6599 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Masud, from his father, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Children of Israel appointed over them a caliph, so he stood praying in the moonlight upon the roof of Bayt al-Maqdis, and mentioned things he had done, then let himself down with a rope, and in the morning the rope was hanging from the mosque, while he had gone, so he went until he came to a people on the seashore, and found them about to make bricks, so he asked them: How do they take payment for these bricks? So they informed him, and he worked with them, and would eat from the work of his hand, until when prayer time came he purified himself and prayed, then that worker was reported to their chief, that among us is a man who does such-and-such, so he sent to him, but he refused to come to him. He said: Then he came himself, riding upon his mount, then when the other saw him, he fled, so he followed him, but he outran him, so he said: Wait for me to speak a word to you. So he stood until he spoke to him, and informed him that he had been a king, and that he had fled from fear of his sin, so he said: I shall join you. So he worshipped Allah at Rumaylat Misr. Abdullah ibn Masud said: Had I been in Egypt I would have shown you the place, by the description of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which he described to us. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Qays ibn al-Rabi."
"6606","6600 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Said ibn Sulayman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prophet from the prophets besieged the people of a city until he feared to conquer it, and feared the sun would set, so he said: O sun, you are commanded, and I am a commanded servant, I adjure you except that you stay still for me an hour of the day. He said: So Allah held it for him until he conquered the city. And when they captured their spoils they would bring them near for the offering, then fire would come and eat them, then when they captured what they captured and placed it, fire did not come to eat it, so they said: O Prophet of Allah, why are our offerings not accepted? He said: Among you is misappropriation. They said: O Prophet of Allah, how can we know with whom the misappropriation is? He said: You are twelve tribes, so the chief of each tribe shall pledge me. He said: So the chief of each tribe pledged him, and the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stuck to the hand of one of them, so he said: The misappropriation is among you. He said: How can I know with whom it is? He said: So he pledged them man by man, and did that, and his hand stuck to the hand of a man among them, so he said to him: The misappropriation is with you? He said: Yes. He said: What is that? He said: A bulls head of gold, it pleased me so I misappropriated it. So he brought it and placed it with the spoils, and fire came and ate it. Then Kab, while with Abu Hurayrah, said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, thus it is in the Book of Allah O Abu Hurayrah, did the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) tell you which prophet it was? He said: No. Kab said: Yusha ibn Nun, the companion of Musa, did he tell you which city it was? He said: No. He said: It is the city of Ariha. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah ibn Umar except Mubarak ibn Fadalah."
"6607","6601 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah informed me, that Abu al-Nadr narrated to him that he heard Qabisah ibn Dhuayb and Sulayman ibn Yasar both narrating, from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, she said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, then a man passed by us calling: They are days of eating and drinking and remembrance of Allah. So I stood to see who he was, and he was a man called Ibn Hudhafah. So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me with this. No one perfected this hadith among those who narrated it from Abu al-Nadr except Ibn Luhayah. And al-Thawri narrated it, from Abu al-Nadr, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Hudhafah, and al-Thawri did not include between Sulayman ibn Yasar and Abdullah ibn Hudhafah: Umm al-Fadl, nor did he mention Qabisah ibn Ruwaybah."
"6608","6602 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Bahir ibn Abdillah ibn Muawiyah ibn Bahir ibn Raysan al-Himyari al-Misri narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Umar narrated to me, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Ibrahim al-Nakhai, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and I did not find anyone following him, so Umar ibn al-Khattab was alarmed, and brought him a vessel for purification, and found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating in a chamber, so he withdrew from him from behind him, until the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head, so he said: You did well O Umar when you found me prostrating and withdrew from me. Jibril came to me and said: Whoever from your ummah sends one blessing upon you, Allah will send ten upon him, and raise him thereby ten degrees. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah ibn Umar except Yahya ibn Ayyub; Amr ibn al-Rabi ibn Tariq alone transmitted it."
"6609","6603 - Muhammad ibn Bahir narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Talhah ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr al-Siddiq narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, from his father Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The heat of Hell upon my ummah is like the heat of the bathhouse."
"6610","6604 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn al-Imam al-Dimyati narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Madini narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Umar narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, Urwah ibn al-Zubayr informed me that Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman informed him: That Aishah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would admit his head to me while he was in itikaf, and I would comb it, and he would not enter his house except for human need. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah ibn Umar except Anas ibn Iyad; Ali ibn al-Madini alone transmitted it."
"6611","6605 - Muhammad ibn Jafar, the Imam son of the Imam, narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn Ghanim narrated to us, Sawwar ibn Musab narrated to us, from Atiyyah al-Awfi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from Umm Salamah, she said: It was my night, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with me, then Fatimah came, and Ali preceded her, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Ali, you and your companions are in Paradise, you and your party are in Paradise, except that among those who claim they love you are peoples who spit out Islam, then cast it off, they recite the Quran not passing their throats, they have a nickname called al-Rafidah, so if you reach them, strive against them, for they are polytheists. So I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the sign among them? He said: They do not attend Friday nor congregation, and they revile the first predecessors. No one narrated this hadith from Atiyyah, from Abu Said, from Umm Salamah, except Sawwar ibn Musab."
"6612","6606 - Muhammad ibn Jafar, son of the Imam, narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya Abu al-Sukayn al-Tai narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad al-Muharibi narrated to us, from Muqatil ibn Dawal Dawz, from Shurahbil ibn Sad, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the Quran, or said: Whoever compiles the Quran, will have with Allah an answered supplication, if He wills He hastens it for him in this world, and if He wills He delays it for him in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Shurahbil, and none narrated it from Shurahbil except Muqatil ibn Dawal Dawz; al-Muharibi alone transmitted it, and Muqatil narrated no other musnad hadith."
"6613","6607 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Yusuf al-Shair narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Saad ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah narrated to me, from his father, that he entered upon Ali, so he called for his sword, and brought out from the belly of the sword an Arab leather, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left with us nothing except the Book of Allah which was revealed except what I conveyed, other than this. So he read it, and in it was: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Every prophet has a sanctuary, and my sanctuary is Madinah, so whoever innovates in it an innovation or shelters an innovator, Allah will not accept from him any obligatory nor voluntary deed. No one narrated this hadith from Saad ibn Sulayman except Sahl ibn Hammad."
"6614","6608 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, that Umar assigned for Usamah ibn Zayd three thousand five hundred, and assigned for his son three thousand, so Abdullah said to his father: Why did you prefer Usamah over me, when by Allah he never preceded me to a battle? He said: Because Zayd was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than your father, and Usamah was more beloved to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than you, so I preferred the beloved of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over my beloved. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Muhammad ibn Bakr al-Bursani; Sufyan ibn Waki alone transmitted it."
"6615","6609 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Waki narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, al-Hasan ibn al-Hasan ibn Ali narrated to me, that Umar ibn al-Khattab proposed to Ali for Umm Kulthum, so he said: She is too young for that. So Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every سبب and نسب will be cut off on the Day of Resurrection, except my سبب and نسب, so I loved that I have from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a سبب and نسب. So Ali said to al-Hasan and al-Husayn: Marry your uncle. So they said: She is a woman among women who chooses for herself. So Ali stood while angry, and al-Hasan seized his garment, and said: There is no patience upon your desertion O father. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Rawh; Sufyan ibn Waki alone transmitted it."
"6616","6610 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Yunus narrated to us, Fudayl ibn Iyad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Salih al-Hanafi, from Bukayr al-Jazari, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We were in a house, a group of the Ansar and the Muhajirin, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, and every man began making room hoping he would sit beside him, then he turned toward the door, seized its two posts, and said: The Imams are from Quraysh, and I have over you a great right, and they have that so long as they do three things: when they are asked for mercy they show mercy, and when they judge they are just, and when they covenant they fulfill. So whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah and the angels and all people. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Iyad except Ahmad ibn Yunus."
"6617","6611 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Subayh narrated to us, Salim ibn Abd al-Ala Abu al-Fayd narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Spread peace, for it is pleasing to Allah."
"6618","6612 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd al-Ala, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught al-Hasan ibn Ali, when he enters the mosque, to send blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and say: O Allah, forgive us our sins, and open for us the doors of Your mercy, and when he exits, he sends blessings upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and says: O Allah, open for us the doors of Your bounty. No one narrated these two hadiths except Abu al-Fayd; Ismail ibn Subayh alone transmitted them."
"6619","6613 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Mutamir ibn Sulayman saying: Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting in circles on Friday before the Imam comes out. I said to Abu Hafs: Did you hear this from Yahya? He said: More than a hundred times. Abu Hafs said: I saw Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi come to the circle of Yahya ibn Said, and Muadh ibn Muadh, and sit outside the circle on Friday before the prayer, so Yahya said to him: Enter the circle. So Abd al-Rahman said to him: You narrated to me from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting in circles on Friday before the Imam comes out. So Yahya said to him: I saw Habib ibn al-Shahid, and Hisham ibn Hassan, and Said ibn Abi Arubah sitting in circles on Friday before the Imam comes out. So Abd al-Rahman said: These were informed that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sitting in circles on Friday, then they sat in circles. So Yahya fell silent. No one narrated this hadith from Mutamir, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi, from Yahya ibn al-Qattan, except Abu Hafs."
"6620","6614 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Qatadah, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, he said: I used to ask people about Adi ibn Hatim while he was beside me in Kufah, so I came to him, and said: What hadith has reached me from you? So he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, I was among the people most hateful of him, until I went fleeing, until I joined the land of Sham, then while I was thus, it reached us that Khalid ibn al-Walid had been directed toward us, so I went fleeing until I joined the land of Rome, then while I was thus sitting in the shade of a wall, I saw a covered woman coming, so I stood to her, and she was my paternal aunt, so she said: O Adi ibn Hatim, you fled and left me, no sooner had you left us than Khalid ibn al-Walid came upon us in the morning, took the offspring captive, and killed the fighters. So we went until we came to Madinah. Then while I was one day sitting, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by me, intending prayer, so I said: O Muhammad, the father has perished, and the delegate has fled, free me, may Allah free you. He said: And who is your delegate? I said: Adi ibn Hatim. He said: The one fleeing from Allah and His Messenger? And he went on. Then on the second day he passed by me intending prayer, so I said: O Muhammad, the father has perished, and the delegate has fled, free me, may Allah free you. He said: And who is your delegate? I said: Adi ibn Hatim. He said: The one fleeing from Allah and His Messenger. And he went on and did not return anything to me. Then on the third day he passed, and I was shy to say anything to him, so Ali ibn Abi Talib nudged me, so I said: O Muhammad, the father has perished and the delegate has fled, free me, may Allah free you. He said: And who is your delegate? I said: Adi ibn Hatim. He said: The one fleeing from Allah and His Messenger. I said: Yes. He said: Allah has freed you, so stay and do not leave until something comes to us and we equip you. So I stayed three days, then a caravan came from Sarh carrying food, so he mounted me upon this camel and provisioned me. O Adi ibn Hatim, come to him, come to him and take your share from him before one comes to him who is not like you from your people. So I came until I reached Madinah, and the people looked at me, and said: Adi ibn Hatim has come. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: O Adi ibn Hatim, are you the one fleeing from Allah and His Messenger? I said: I have a religion. He said: I know your religion better than you: Are you not a Rakusi, are you not a chief of your people, do you not take the quarter? So I felt shame at that. He said: It does not prevent you from accepting Islam except that you see around us poverty, and you see people united against us. O Adi, soon you will see the covered woman depart from al-Hirah until she comes to the House without protection, and soon the treasures of Kisra will be opened upon us. He said: I said: Kisra ibn Hurmuz? He said: Kisra ibn Hurmuz, and soon a man will take out charity from his wealth and find none to accept it from him. He said: So I was among the first cavalry that raided the treasures of Kisra, and I saw the covered woman depart from al-Hirah until she came to Makkah without protection, and by Allah the third will surely be, for the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is true. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Hisham al-Dastuwai; his son Abdullah alone transmitted it."
"6621","6615 - Muhammad ibn Jafar son of the Imam narrated to us, Abu al-Sukayn al-Tai Zakariyya ibn Yahya narrated to us, the uncle of my father Zahr ibn Hisn narrated to us, from his grandfather Humayd ibn Munhib, he said: It reached Muawiyah that Ibn al-Zubayr reviles Abu Sufyan. He said: Evil, by Allah, is what he says regarding his uncle, but I do not say regarding Abu Abdillah except good, may Allah have mercy on him, he was a righteous man. Abu Sufyan went out to a desert land of his, mounting Hind behind him, and I went out walking before her, while I was a boy upon a she-donkey of mine, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) caught up with us. So Abu Sufyan said: Dismount O Muawiyah until Muhammad rides. So I dismounted from the she-donkey, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) rode it, and traveled before them a while, then turned to them, and said: O Abu Sufyan ibn Harb, and O Hind bint Utbah, by Allah you shall die, then you shall be resurrected, then the doer of good shall enter Paradise, and the doer of evil the Fire, and what I say to you is true, and you are the first I warned. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited: Ha Mim, a revelation from the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate, until he reached: They both said: We come willingly. So Abu Sufyan said to him: Have you finished O Muhammad? He said: Yes. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dismounted from the she-donkey, and I rode it. Then Hind turned to Abu Sufyan, and said: For this sorcerer liar did you dismount my son? He said: By Allah, he is neither sorcerer nor liar. This hadith is not narrated from Muawiyah except with this chain; Abu al-Sukayn alone transmitted it."
"6622","6616 - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Adam ibn Abi Iyas al-Asqalani narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather Adam ibn Abi Iyas, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran is a thousand thousand letters, and twenty-seven thousand letters, so whoever recites it patiently seeking reward will have for every letter a wife from the houris. This hadith is not narrated from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain; Hafs ibn Maysarah alone transmitted it."
"6623","6617 - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is granted good, let him reward for it, and whoever does not find what to reward with, let him thank him. Whoever does so has thanked, and whoever leaves has disbelieved. And whoever adorns himself with what he was not given is like one wearing two garments of falsehood."
"6624","6618 - And with the same chain, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: What is the righteousness of Hajj? He said: Feeding food, and good speech. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Awzai except Ayyub ibn Suwayd."
"6625","6619 - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Amr ibn Bakr al-Saksaki narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Abdah ibn Riyah al-Ghassani narrated to us, from his father Abdah ibn Riyah, from Munib ibn Abdillah al-Azdi, from his father Abdillah ibn Munib, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited to us: Every day He is in a matter. So we said: O Messenger of Allah, what is that matter? He said: To forgive a sin, and relieve distress, and raise a people, and lower others. This hadith is not narrated from Abdillah ibn Munib al-Azdi except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi alone transmitted it."
"6626","6620 - Muhammad ibn Ubayd ibn Adam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Amr ibn Bakr narrated to us, Abu Bakr Muhammad ibn Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays narrated to me, from his father Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays, he said: I heard Abu Umamah al-Bahili saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: For a man is what he intends, and upon him is what he earns, and every man is with whom he loves. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi alone transmitted it."
"6627","6621 - Muhammad ibn Abdah al-Missisi narrated to us, Abu Tawbah al-Rabi ibn Nafi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ubaydillah, from Karimah bint al-Hashas, she said: Abu Hurayrah narrated to us in the house of this woman, meaning: Umm al-Darda, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah says: I am with My servant so long as he remembers Me, and his lips move with Me. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Muhajir except Abu Tawbah."
"6628","6622 - Muhammad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Jumahi narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever cups on the morning of the seventeenth, it will be a cure for him from every disease. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Said ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abu Tawbah alone transmitted it."
"6629","6623 - Muhammad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The womb is a branch hanging from the Throne, and the joiner is not the recompenser, but the joiner is one who, when his kinship is cut, joins it. No one narrated this hadith from Fitr, from Abu al-Tufayl, except Isa ibn Yunus; Abu Tawbah alone transmitted it. And al-Thawri and others narrated it, from Fitr, from Mujahid, from Abdullah ibn Amr."
"6630","6624 - Muhammad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim, from Abu Umamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two and more are a congregation. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn al-Harith except Maslamah; Abu Tawbah alone transmitted it."
"6631","6625 - Muhammad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Abu Tawbah narrated to us, Bashir ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Durayk, from Yala ibn Munabbih, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had dispatched a detachment, so I bid farewell to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a man riding upon a saddle said to me: I will not go out unless you give me three dinars. So I disliked to return to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after I had bidden him farewell, so I gave them. Then when I finished my expedition I informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Give it to him, it is his share of his expedition in his world and his Hereafter. This hadith is not narrated from Yala ibn Munabbih except from the hadith of Bashir ibn Talhah."
"6632","6626 - Muhammad ibn Hisn ibn Khalid al-Uwaysi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Azhar ibn Sad narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Imran al-Khayyat, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is upon the people of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith as musnad from Imran al-Khayyat except Ibn Awn, and none from Awn except Azhar; Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan alone transmitted it."
"6633","6627 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Hammad ibn Sulayman ibn al-Hasan ibn Aban ibn al-Numan ibn Bashir ibn Sad al-Ansari narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seeks goodness through istikhara will not be disappointed, and whoever consults will not regret, and whoever is moderate will not be poor."
"6634","6628 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Abd al-Salam ibn Abd al-Quddus narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we not command good until we act upon it, and not forbid evil until we avoid it all? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather command good, even if you do not act upon all of it, and forbid evil, even if you do not avoid all of it. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Hasan except Abd al-Quddus ibn Habib; his son alone transmitted them from him."
"6635","6629 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Amir al-Nahwi al-Suri narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Ammar al-Duhni, Ibrahim narrated to me, from the daughter of Maqil ibn Yasar, from her father Maqil, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever governs an ummah from my ummahs, few or many, and does not act justly among them, Allah will throw him upon his face into the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar al-Duhni except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn; Hisham alone transmitted it."
"6636","6630 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Amir al-Nahwi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Abu Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you is called and comes with the messenger, that is his permission. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Khilas, well-perfected, except Shuayb ibn Ishaq; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"6637","6631 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Knowledge is in Quraysh, and trustworthiness in al-Azd. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn al-Harith except Yazid ibn Abi Habib; Ibn Luhayah alone transmitted it."
"6638","6632 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Amir al-Nahwi narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hashim ibn Abi Hurayrah al-Himsi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would complete the bowing and prostration, and lighten the standing and sitting in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Hashim ibn Abi Hurayrah; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"6639","6633 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Musa ibn Isa al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever drags his garments, Allah will not look at him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except Musa ibn Isa; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"6640","6634 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim Abu Amir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu al-Muhazzam narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: My believing servant is more beloved to Me than some of My angels."
"6641","6635 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abu al-Muhazzam narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The first to enter the Fire from this ummah are the whip-bearers. No one narrated these two hadiths from Hammad ibn Salamah except al-Walid ibn Muslim; Hisham alone transmitted them."
"6642","6636 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abdillah, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a day comes upon me in which I do not increase in knowledge, there is no blessing in the rising of the sun of that day. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Hakam ibn Abdillah al-Ayli; Baqiyyah alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"6643","6637 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Abdullah ibn Saydan who said: I was with Ibn Masud at Arafah, then Uthman prayed Zuhr four and Asr four, so Ibn Masud said: Here I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and with Abu Bakr and Umar, and they prayed only two. I said: Will you not stand to him? He said: Be silent, for dissension is evil. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Saydan except Maymun ibn Mihran; Jafar ibn Burqan alone transmitted it."
"6644","6638 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Ruasi narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Ibn Abi Awfa who said: It was said to him: Did you see Ibrahim the son of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? So he said: Yes, he died while small, the most resembling of people to him (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and had it been decreed that there be a prophet after him, his son Ibrahim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would have lived. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Ruasi except Ubayd ibn Jannad."
"6645","6639 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Bazigh ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The travel of a woman with her servant is waste. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Bazigh ibn Abd al-Rahman; Ismail ibn Ayyash alone transmitted it."
"6646","6640 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, from Ibn al-Suddi, from his father, from Rifah al-Bajali, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever grants a man safety upon his blood, then kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the killed is a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Suddi except Ata ibn Muslim; Ubayd ibn Jannad alone transmitted it."
"6647","6641 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ishaq, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas saying: We heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever guards these prescribed prayers in congregation will be the first to cross the Sirat like flashing lightning, and Allah will resurrect him among the first group of the followers, and for every day and night he guarded them he will have like the reward of a thousand martyrs killed in the path of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Abi Aishah except Ammar Abu Ishaq; Baqiyyah alone transmitted it."
"6648","6642 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Said ibn Zayd, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Usamah ibn Zayd, he said: Ali said to me: O Usamah, why do you not go out with us, you are a man from the household? He said: I said: You spoke truly, none is more entitled that I go out with than you, but by Allah I will not fight those who pray after the word of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did you not leave him, or did you split his heart and look into it. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Said ibn Zayd, and none from Said except Ata ibn Muslim; Ubayd ibn Jannad alone transmitted it."
"6649","6643 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kulthum, from al-Awzai, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mustahadah bathes from menstrual period to menstrual period. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Salamah ibn Kulthum, and none from Salamah except Baqiyyah; Ubayd ibn Jannad alone transmitted it."
"6650","6644 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Amr ibn Qust narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Junadah, from Makhul, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever walks in the darkness of the night to the mosques, Allah will grant him light on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Junadah; Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah alone transmitted it."
"6651","6645 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Amr ibn Qist narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ate from a sheeps shoulder, then prayed and did not perform wudu. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ishaq ibn Rashid, and none from Ishaq except Ubaydillah ibn Amr."
"6652","6646 - Muhammad ibn Jafar al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Hibban, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a ring of gold, so he discarded it among his Companions, then said: I shall never wear it. So the people discarded their rings. Then he took a ring of silver, with which he would seal documents, until it fell into the well of Aris, and was lost. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Layla except Zayd ibn Hibban; Mamar ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"6653","6647 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Hibban, from Asim, from al-Harith, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Bring a quarter of a tenth: when it reaches two hundred dirhams, in it are five dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud except Zayd ibn Hibban; Mamar ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"6654","6648 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Hibban, from Umar ibn Yahya, from his father, from Abu Said who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no charity in less than five awsuq, and there is no charity upon less than five dhawd, and there is no charity upon less than five awaq. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Hibban except Mamar ibn Sulayman."
"6655","6649 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Fuhayr ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There are no people with whom there is a dog, except a hunting dog, and Abu Hurayrah claimed: or a farming dog, except that it decreases from their rewards every night two qirats."
"6656","6650 - And with the same chain, from Ibn Jurayj, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A child does not repay his father, except that he finds him enslaved, so buys him and frees him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Jurayj except Fuhayr."
"6657","6651 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Amr ibn Qist narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabir, from Salim, from Ibn Umar who said: I would often go with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Fitr and Adha, and he would not pray before them nor after them."
"6658","6652 - And with the same chain, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Yazid ibn al-Bara ibn Azib, from his father who said: I met my uncle with the banner with him, so I said: Where do you intend? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to a man who married the wife of his father, and commanded me to kill him, and take his wealth. No one narrated these two hadiths from Zayd except Ubaydillah ibn Amr."
"6659","6653 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Amr ibn Qist narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not listen like His listening to a prophet chanting the Quran."
"6660","6654 - And with the same chain, from al-Zuhri, that Salim ibn Abdillah informed him from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: Allah hears whoever praises Him, our Lord, to You is praise. Then he would say before prostrating: O Allah, curse so-and-so and so-and-so. Then he would say takbir and prostrate, until Allah revealed: You have nothing of the matter, the verse. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ishaq ibn Rashid except Ubaydillah ibn Amr."
"6661","6655 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Sufyan al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad al-Halabi narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Ibn al-Suddi, from his father, from Rifah al-Bajali, from Amr ibn al-Hamiq, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever a man trusts upon his blood and he kills him, I am free of the killer, even if the killed is a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Suddi except Ata ibn Muslim; Ubayd ibn Jannad alone transmitted it."
"6662","6656 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Jannad narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ammar Abu Ishaq, from Musa ibn Abi Aishah, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, that he heard Abu Hurayrah and Ibn Abbas saying: They both heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the last of his sermon saying: Whoever guards these prescribed prayers in congregation will be the first to cross the Sirat like flashing lightning, and Allah will resurrect him among the first group of the followers, and for every day and night he guarded them he will have like the reward of a thousand martyrs killed in the path of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Abi Aishah except Ammar Abu Ishaq; Baqiyyah alone transmitted it."
"6663","6657 - Abu Hasin Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Dimashqi narrated to us: My father narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said and Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb and Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that they heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying the talbiyah with both together: Labbayk Umrah and Hajj. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari except Hushaym and Abu Yusuf the judge; Ismail ibn Muhammad al-Dimashqi alone transmitted it from Hushaym, and from Abu Yusuf: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi."
"6664","6658 - Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Yusuf al-Umawi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would find a mans shoulder protruding from his companions shoulder, so he would straighten it, and say: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Hafs ibn Ghiyath and Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri; his son Umar ibn Hafs alone transmitted it from Hafs, and Hisham ibn Khalid alone transmitted it from Khalid ibn Yazid."
"6665","6659 - Muhammad ibn Bishr ibn Yusuf al-Umawi al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Qays al-Mulai, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would recite in the dawn prayer on Friday: Alif Lam Mim, the revelation, al-Sajdah, and: Has there come upon man. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Qays except Thawr ibn Yazid, and none from Thawr except al-Walid; Duhaym alone transmitted it."
"6666","6660 - Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, he said: al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam al-Sanani used to narrate from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever prays one rakah of the dawn prayer, then the sun rises, let him pray another to it."
"6667","6661 - Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Abd al-Samad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not say salam in the two rakahs of witr. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam except Muhammad ibn Shuayb; Hisham ibn Ammar alone transmitted them."
"6668","6662 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sariyah al-Ukkawi al-Muqri narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mouse is transformed, and the sign of that is that it drinks sheeps milk, and does not drink camels milk. No one narrated this hadith as marfu from Ibn Awn except Ismail ibn Ayyash, and none from Ismail except Baqiyyah; Musa ibn Ayyub alone transmitted it."
"6669","6663 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Mansur ibn Safiyyah, from his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, she said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw what he loves, he said: Praise be to Allah by Whose blessing good deeds are completed, and when he saw what he dislikes, he said: Praise be to Allah in every condition."
"6670","6664 - Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would see semen in the garment of one of us, then rub it off. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Jafar ibn Burqan."
"6671","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Sariyah narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Amr ibn Uthman ibn Hani, he said: Asim ibn Amr ibn Uthman informed me, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to me, and I recognized in his face that something had occurred, and he did not speak until he performed ablution, then he went out and ascended the minbar, and I clung to the chamber, and he praised Allah and extolled Him, then he said: O people, indeed Allah says: Enjoin good and forbid evil before you supplicate Me and I do not answer you, and you ask Me and I do not give you, and you seek My help and I do not help you. And he did not add to them until he returned. No one narrated this hadith from Asim ibn Amr except Amr ibn Uthman; Ibn Abi Fudayk is alone in transmitting it."
"6672","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us, Musa ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Ghusn narrated to us, from al-Amash and Husayn, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) continue saying the talbiyah until he stoned Jamrat al-Aqabah. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except al-Qasim ibn Ghusn; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"6673","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah al-Asqalani narrated to us, Isa ibn Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Umawi al-Asqalani narrated to us, Muadh ibn Khalid narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi Salih narrated to me that he heard Nafi ibn Jubayr ibn Mutim narrating from his father, he said: While I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Hijr, al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As passed by, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Woe to my ummah because of what is in the loins of this man. This hadith is not narrated from Jubayr ibn Mutim except with this chain; Zuhayr ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"6674","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani narrated to us, Habib, the scribe of Malik, narrated to us, Shibl ibn Abbad narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you touches his private part with his hand, let him perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Shibl except Habib, the scribe of Malik."
"6675","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Habib narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him not enter the bathhouse except with a waist-wrapper. No one narrated this hadith from Malik except Habib."
"6676","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Rushdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes to a soothsayer and believes him in what he says has disavowed what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and whoever goes to him without believing him, his prayer is not accepted for forty days. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Jarir ibn Hazim, nor from Jarir except Rushdin; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"6677","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Maqdisi narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Indeed the angels curse one of you when he points at his brother with a piece of iron, even if he is his full brother through his father and mother. No one narrates this hadith from Ibn Shawdhab except Damrah."
"6678","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab al-Ramli narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Shuayb narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Said al-Maqburi, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ruined are those who make themselves filthy. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it."
"6679","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yazid ibn Iyad informed me, from Abu Adi al-Fadaki, from al-Qasim Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Thawban, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things do not break the fast of the fasting person: cupping, vomiting, and nocturnal emission. This hadith is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it."
"6680","And with the same chain, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to him that Yazid ibn Abi Ubayd, the freed slave of Salamah ibn al-Akwa, narrated to him that he heard Salamah ibn al-Akwa saying: When we saw a man cursing his brother, we considered that he had committed one of the major sins. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah except Yazid, nor from Yazid except Bukayr; Amr ibn al-Harith is alone in transmitting it."
"6681","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Khalaf al-Ramli narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No flesh that grew from unlawful earnings shall enter Paradise; the Fire is more deserving of it. No one narrates this hadith from Sufyan except Ayyub ibn Suwayd; Ibrahim ibn Khalifah is alone in transmitting it."
"6682","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Asim al-Nabil narrated to us, Abu Amir al-Aqadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Taifi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever is strictly reckoned for his deed will perish. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Zubayr except Amr ibn Dinar, nor from Amr except Muhammad ibn Muslim; Abu Amir is alone in transmitting it."
"6683","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Isa ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque on Friday, he would greet those seated near his minbar, and when he ascended the minbar he would turn to the people and greet them. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Isa ibn Abdullah; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"6684","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Isa ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Aishah, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man's mouth changes in odor; should he use the siwak? He said: Yes. I said: How should he do it? He said: He inserts his finger into his mouth. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Isa ibn Abdullah; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain."
"6685","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah al-Sanani narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sulayman Abu Sulayman al-Madani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I wish to go out to fight in the path of Allah. He said: Keep to al-Sham, then keep to Asqalan from al-Sham; for when the millstone turns against my ummah, its people will be in ease and well-being. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Yahya ibn Sulayman; Hafs ibn Maysarah is alone in transmitting it."
"6686","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those before you perished only because they glorified their kings by standing and sitting. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except al-Awzai, and no one narrated it from al-Awzai except Suwayd."
"6687","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan narrated to us, Maqil ibn Ubaydullah narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade mutah marriage. No one narrated this hadith from Maqil ibn Ubaydullah except al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn Ayan."
"6688","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no jizyah upon a Muslim. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Yahya ibn Isa; Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ghazzi is alone in transmitting it."
"6689","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Amr ibn Khulayf Abu Salih narrated to us, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Hafs ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three men from among those before you went out seeking provisions for their families, and rain befell them, so they took refuge in a cave, and he mentioned the hadith of the cave."
"6690","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf al-Asqalani narrated to us, Adam ibn Abi Iyas narrated to us, Abu Shaybah Shuayb ibn Ruzyaq narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from his father, he said: I was keen to find someone who would inform me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the Duha prayer, but I found no one to inform me except Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, for she informed me, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me after the day had risen on the day of the conquest, the conquest of Makkah, and he ordered a garment and it was screened for him, and he bathed, then he stood and prayed eight rakahs; I do not know whether his standing in them was longer or his bowing or his prostration; all of that in them was close together, and I never saw him pray before it nor after it. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except Shuayb ibn Ruzyaq; Adam is alone in transmitting it."
"6691","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad Abu Utbah al-Khawwas narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Ubaydullah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is two-faced in this world will have two tongues of fire on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Abbad ibn Abbad; Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah is alone in transmitting it."
"6692","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalaf narrated to us, Rawwad narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Khalid ibn al-Lajlaj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's nobility is his piety, his manliness is his intellect, and his lineage is his character. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Abu Ghassan."
"6693","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Musa ibn Sahl al-Ramli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Ghusn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Suqah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Abi Talhah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to the sky and said: The stars are a security for the people of the sky, and I am a security for my Companions, and my Companions are a security for my ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Suqah except al-Qasim ibn Ghusn; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"6694","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, Musa ibn Sahl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Ramli narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Ghusn narrated to us, Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon the peak of the hump of every camel there is a devil, so make use of them. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Muhammad except al-Qasim ibn Ghusn; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"6695","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Amr ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to us, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An angel came to me who had never descended to the earth before with a message from my Lord, and he placed one foot above the lowest heaven and one foot on the earth, which bore it. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Sadaqah; Amr ibn Abi Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"6696","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Zayd al-Kharraz al-Ramli narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Hakim, from Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed Safiyyah and made her freedom her dowry. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abi Arubah except Asim ibn Hakim; Ayyub ibn Suwayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6697","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Nawfal ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: One of the sons of Jafar ibn Abi Talib came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah, send with me someone to buy for me sandals and a ring. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Bilal ibn Rabah and said: Go to the market and buy for him sandals, and make them new, and let them not be black, and buy for him a ring, and let its stone be aqeeq. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim except Nawfal, and no one narrated it from Nawfal except Ayyub ibn Suwayd; his son is alone in transmitting it."
"6698","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Ali ibn Said al-Muqri al-Akkawi narrated to us, Yala ibn Ubayd al-Tanafisi narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Wabarah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Indeed Allah has placed the truth upon the tongue of Umar and his heart; he speaks by it. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Yala ibn Ubayd; Ali ibn Said is alone in transmitting it."
"6699","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sulayman narrated to us, Yusuf al-Abdi narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from Misar, from Abu Farwah, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in the Fajr prayer on Friday Alif Lam Mim, the Revelation, and Has there come upon man. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Abu Ishaq."
"6700","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Rushdin ibn Sad narrated to us, Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: To You all hopes end, O Possessor of well-being. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl except Musa ibn Jubayr, nor from Musa except Rushdin; Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari is alone in transmitting it."
"6701","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari narrated to us, Rawwad ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Abbad, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Saybani, from Abu Walah, from Kurayb al-Sahuli, from Murrah al-Bahzi, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Al-Ramlah is al-Rabwah. This hadith is not narrated from Murrah except with this chain; Abbad ibn Abbad is alone in transmitting it."
"6702","Muhammad ibn Sinan al-Shayzari narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah al-Hawti narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no days in which deeds are more virtuous than the ten of Dhu al-Hijjah. They said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah? He said: Not even jihad in the path of Allah, except one whose horse is hamstrung and whose blood is shed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except al-Walid; al-Hawti is alone in transmitting it."
"6703","Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab ibn Najdah narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from al-Amash, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abdullah ibn Salamah, from Ali, he said: Nothing would prevent the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from reciting the Quran except janabah."
"6704","And with the same chain: from Jafar ibn al-Harith, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi, al-Bara narrated to us, he said: When we prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and he said: Allah hears whoever praises Him, none of us would bend his back until he settled prostrating. No one narrated these two hadiths from Jafar ibn al-Harith except Ismail; al-Hawti is alone in transmitting them."
"6705","Muhammad ibn Sinan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, may one of us pray in a single garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"6706","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sadaqah al-Missisi narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Muradi, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Thawban, he said: When: And those who hoard gold and silver was revealed, they said: O Messenger of Allah, then what wealth should we hoard? He said: A grateful heart, a remembering tongue, and a righteous wife. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Muradi except Sharik; Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa is alone in transmitting it."
"6707","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa ibn Imran narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Jabir, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir, that a man made a conditional manumission of a slave boy after his death, and he was needy, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sold him. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Sharik; Abd al-Kabir ibn al-Muafa is alone in transmitting it."
"6708","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan al-Missisi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These privies are attended, so when one of you enters them, let him say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from male and female devils. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar; Ibrahim ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6709","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Abu al-Tayyah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Salim ibn Hayyan except Habban ibn Hilal."
"6710","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Habban narrated to us, from Salim ibn Hayyan, he said: I heard Qatadah narrating from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, that Umar said: Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us last year and said: Nothing better than well-being after certainty has been apportioned among people; indeed righteousness and truthfulness are in Paradise, and indeed lying and wickedness are in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except Habban ibn Hilal."
"6711","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Muti ibn Maymun al-Anbari narrated to us, from Safiyyah bint Ismah, who is his mother, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the going out of secluded maidens on the two Eids? He said: They go out. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, if she has no garment? He said: She wears her companion's garment. Have you not heard that Allah says: And to complete the number and to glorify Allah for having guided you."
"6712","And with the same chain, from Safiyyah, from Aishah, that a woman extended her hand with a letter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he withheld his hand from her, so she said: Why did you withhold your hand from me? He said: Is it a man or a woman? She said: A woman. He said: If you were a woman you would have changed your nails with henna. No one narrated these two hadiths from Safiyyah bint Ismah except Muti ibn Maymun."
"6713","Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Kaysan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Ghudani narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Israil narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Bashir, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from his father, that he said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): If there is over us a ruler who acts without obedience to Allah, shall we listen and obey? He turned away from him, then he repeated to him, and he turned away from him, then he said: Upon them is what they were burdened with, and upon you is what you were burdened with. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abi Israil except Hammam, and no one narrated it except Abdullah ibn Raja and Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri."
"6714","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid al-Baghdadi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi al-Sari al-Asqalani narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ibn Aqil, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed the aqeeqah for al-Hasan and al-Husayn and circumcised them at seven days. No one among the narrators said in this hadith: and circumcised them at seven days, except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad."
"6715","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Said ibn al-Arkun al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Khulayd ibn Dalaj narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The security of the earth from drowning is the rainbow, and the security of my ummah from disagreement is allegiance to Quraysh; Quraysh are the people of Allah, three times; and if a tribe of the Arabs opposes them, they become the party of Iblis. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Khulayd ibn Dalaj; Ishaq ibn Said is alone in transmitting it."
"6716","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Abi Usamah al-Halabi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed over a dead person after he had been buried. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Jafar ibn Burqan; Abu Usamah Zayd ibn Ali is alone in transmitting it."
"6717","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Farwah narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not that I would cause hardship for my ummah, I would have made the time of Isha until midnight. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ishaq ibn Abdullah."
"6718","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Makhul, that Qaysar narrated to him, from Ibn Umar, that he used to pray upon his mount wherever it turned with him, and he was asked: Is it a sunnah? He said: It is a sunnah. They said: Did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He smiled and said: I heard it. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir."
"6719","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that he entered ihram for Hajj when his mount rose with him, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entering ihram when his mount rose with him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"6720","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Marzuq ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said during his illness in which he was ill: Pour over me from seven waterskins whose ties have not been untied, so that I may give counsel to the people. Aishah said: So we seated him in a washtub belonging to Hafsah, and we poured over him water from those skins. No one narrated this hadith from Marzuq ibn Abi al-Hudhayl except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"6721","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Sanani narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Amili narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Aktham ibn Abi al-Jawn al-Khuzai: Campaign with other than your people; your character will improve and you will be honored among your companions. O Aktham, the best of companions are four, the best of advance scouts are forty, the best of detachments are four hundred, and the best of armies are four thousand, and twelve thousand shall never be defeated due to fewness. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Anas, except Abu Salamah al-Amili; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6722","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Utaybah informed me, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym al-Juhani, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to us while we were in Juhaynah: Do not make use of the carcass by skin or sinew. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, except Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"6723","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban, from Salim ibn Abdullah, that he heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril came to me with in his hand something like a white mirror in which there was a black speck, and I said: What is this, O Jibril? He said: This is Friday; your Lord sent it to you to be a festival for you and for your ummah after you. I said: What is in it for us? He said: Much good for you; you are the last, the foremost on the Day of Resurrection, and in it there is an hour which no Muslim servant coincides with while praying and asking Allah for something except that He gives it to him. I said: What is this black speck? He said: This is the Hour; it will come on Friday, and it is the master of days, and we call it the Day of Increase. I said: O Jibril, what is the Increase? He said: Your Lord has taken in Paradise a wide valley of white musk, and when Friday comes in the days of the Hereafter, the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, descends from His Throne to His Kursi, and the Kursi is surrounded with pulpits of light upon which the prophets sit, and the pulpits are surrounded with chairs of gold upon which the martyrs sit, and the people of the chambers descend from their chambers and sit upon dunes of musk, and they do not see the people of the chairs and pulpits as having any superiority over them in seating, and the Possessor of Majesty and Honor manifests Himself to them and says: Ask Me. They say: We ask You for pleasure, O Lord. He says: My pleasure has settled you in My abode and bestowed My honor upon you. Then He says: Ask Me. They all say together: We ask You for pleasure. So He makes them witnesses to the pleasure. Then He says: Ask Me. So they ask Him until every servant among them finishes. Then He confers upon them what no eye has seen, no ear has heard, and what has never occurred to a human heart. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"6724","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that Hakim ibn Hizam bought provision-food and sold it before taking possession of it, so Umar forbade him and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade selling food until it is taken possession of, so he returned his capital to him. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abdullah ibn Umar, nor from Abdullah ibn Umar except Muammal; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6725","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from his father, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On the night I was taken by night journey, I saw written upon the gate of Paradise: Charity is ten times its like, and a loan is eighteen times. I said: O Jibril, why is a loan better than charity? He said: The beggar asks while he has, and the borrower does not borrow except out of need."
"6726","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid ibn Abi Malik narrated to us, from his father, he said: Anas ibn Malik used to place his hands upon his ears and say: May they be deaf if they did not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Perform ablution because of what fire has touched. No one narrated these two hadiths from Yazid ibn Abi Malik except his son Khalid ibn Yazid."
"6727","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Halbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, from his brother Isa, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the fetus? He said: Its slaughter is the slaughter of its mother. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abi Layla except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6728","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wailing women shall wear garments of tar. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"6729","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, Talhah ibn Musa narrated to me, from his uncle Ishaq ibn Talhah, from Talhah ibn Ubaydullah, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Hajj is jihad, and Umrah is voluntary. It is not narrated from Talhah except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6730","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: I heard Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan narrating from Zurarah ibn Awfa, from Abu Umayyah, he said: I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating, and he said: Come. I said: I am fasting. He said: Come, I shall tell you: Allah has lifted from the traveler fasting and half the prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except al-Khalil; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6731","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salamah al-Nasri al-Kufi narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, he said: Abdullah ibn Umar accompanied me and a companion of mine when I was setting out from Madinah to Iraq, and when he wanted to leave he said: I have nothing with me to give you, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When Allah is entrusted with something, He preserves it. And I entrust to Allah your religion, your trusts, and the outcomes of your deeds. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Salamah except Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6732","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Abu Sad, the servant of al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan, from al-Hasan, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hates Umar has hated me, and whoever loves Umar has loved me. Allah boasted to the people on the evening of Arafah generally, and boasted of Umar specifically. No prophet was sent except that there was among his ummah one spoken to, and if there is any of them among my ummah, it is Umar. They said: O Messenger of Allah, how is one spoken to? He said: The angels speak upon his tongue. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Said except al-Hasan, nor narrated it from al-Hasan except Abu Sad his servant, nor narrated it from Abu Sad except Muhammad ibn Muhajir; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"6733","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, from Qatadah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar prostrated in Sad. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Abu Bakr al-Hudhali; Ismail ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"6734","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I have wealth and children, and my father wants to consume my wealth? He said: You and your wealth belong to your father. No one narrated this hadith from Yusuf except Isa ibn Yunus."
"6735","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: I heard Sulayman ibn Abi Muslim al-Ahwal saying: I asked al-Minhal about currency exchange, and he said: I and a partner of mine bought hand to hand and deferred for deferred, and we mentioned that to al-Bara ibn Azib, and he said: I and my partner Zayd ibn Arqam did it, and we mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: What is hand to hand, take it, and what is deferred, leave it. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn al-Aswad except Sadaqah ibn Khalid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6736","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ata ibn Yasar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the prayer is established, there is no prayer except the obligatory one. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Husayn except Hisham ibn Ammar."
"6737","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Abu Taybah and he cupped him at sunset at the fasting person's breaking of fast, then he asked him and said: How much is your tax? He said: Two saas, so he reduced a saa from him. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Burqan except Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6738","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Abu al-Asbat al-Harithi, from Ismail ibn Sharwas al-Sanani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the funeral for which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood was the funeral of a Jew, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Its odor offended me. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Sharwas except Abu al-Asbat; Hatim ibn Ismail is alone in transmitting it."
"6739","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, my father Ammar ibn Nusayr narrated to me, from Amr ibn Said al-Khawlani, from Anas ibn Malik, that Salamah, the nurse of Ibrahim the son of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), said: O Messenger of Allah, you give glad tidings to men of every good and you do not give glad tidings to women? He said: Did your companions put you up to this? She said: Yes, they ordered me. He said: Is not one of you pleased that when she is pregnant by her husband and he is pleased with her, she has the reward of one fasting and standing in the path of Allah, and when labor befalls her, neither the people of heaven nor the people of earth know what is hidden for her of delight of eyes, and when she gives birth, no sip of her milk comes out and no suck is sucked except that she has for every sip and every suck a good deed, and if it keeps her awake a night, she has the reward of seventy necks she frees in the path of Allah. O Salamah, do you know for whom I mean this? For the chaste, righteous women, obedient to their husbands, who do not deny the companionship. This hadith is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6740","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Qatadah ibn Diamah al-Sadusi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the call was made for the Maghrib prayer, the people would hasten to the pillars, praying two rakahs, two rakahs, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among them. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Anas, except al-Hakam ibn Hisham."
"6741","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Nistas al-Madani narrated to us, Mirba narrated to me, from Umm Sulaym, the mother of Anas ibn Malik, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, advise me. He said: Abandon disobedience, for it is the best emigration; guard the obligatory duties, for they are the best jihad; and remember Allah much, for you shall not come to Allah with anything more beloved to Him than much remembrance of Him. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Sulaym except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6742","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salih al-Madani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Part of honoring the majesty of Allah is honoring the gray-haired Muslim, the just ruler, and the bearer of the Quran who neither exceeds bounds in it nor turns away from it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Muhammad ibn Salih al-Madani, who is al-Tammar; Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn is alone in transmitting it."
"6743","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Abu Abd al-Aziz Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Azdi narrated to us, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: We campaigned with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we seized sheep, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed a portion of them among us and placed the remainder in the spoils. No one narrated this hadith from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, nor from Abd al-Rahman except Ubadah ibn Nusayy, nor from Ubadah except Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz; Yahya ibn Hamzah is alone in transmitting it."
"6744","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Urdunni narrated to us, that Abdullah ibn Nuaym al-Azdi narrated to him, from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ashari, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, he said: When Allah defeated the polytheists on the day of Hawazin, the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) put Abu Amir al-Ashari in command of the cavalry of pursuit, and he pursued them, and there came to him among those who pursued them Ibn Durayd ibn al-Simmah, and Ibn Durayd turned toward him and killed Abu Amir and took the banner, and I charged upon Ibn Durayd and killed him and took the banner, then I returned to find the people gathered, and when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me carrying the banner, he said: Has Abu Amir been killed? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his hands supplicating for Abu Amir and said: O Allah, grant Your servant Abu Amir, and place him among the most numerous on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from al-Dahhak ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Musa, except with this chain; Yahya ibn Hamzah is alone in transmitting it."
"6745","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, Musa ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Makhul, from Junadah ibn Abi Umayyah, he said: We encamped at Dabiq with Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah over us, and it reached Habib ibn Maslamah that the master of Cyprus had set out heading toward the road of Adharbayjan, with emeralds, rubies, pearls, gold, and brocade with him, so he went out with cavalry and killed him and brought what was with him, and Abu Ubaydah wanted to take a fifth of it, and Habib said: Do not deprive me of it, a provision Allah has provided me, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) assign the spoils to the killer. Muadh said: Wait, O Habib, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A man has only what his imam willingly allows him. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Musa ibn Yasar; Amr ibn Waqid is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Muadh and Habib ibn Maslamah except with this chain."
"6746","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon in two sermons, sitting between them. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Hatim ibn Ismail; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6747","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn Malih al-Bahrani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from Luqman ibn Amir al-Wasabi, from Abd al-Ala ibn Adi al-Bahrani, from Thawban, the freed slave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two groups of my ummah Allah has protected from the Fire: a group that campaigns in India, and a group that will be with Isa son of Maryam. This hadith is not narrated from Thawban except with this chain; al-Zubaydi is alone in transmitting it."
"6748","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Yazid ibn Ubaydah narrated to me, Abu Ubaydullah Muslim ibn Mishkam narrated to me, from Awf ibn Malik, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Dreams are of three kinds: among them are frights of Satan to grieve the son of Adam, and among them is what a man occupies himself with in his wakefulness and then sees in his sleep, and among them is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood. I said to him: Did you hear this from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: I heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Awf ibn Malik except with this chain; Yazid ibn Ubaydah is alone in transmitting it."
"6749","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Yazid narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhuayb al-Khuzai and Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The farthest outposts of the Muslims are about to be arms, and arms near Khaybar. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Said ibn Yahya; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6750","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Mukhays ibn Tamim narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar narrated to me, Ibrahim ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Moderation in spending is half of livelihood, affection toward people is half of intellect, and asking well is half of knowledge. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it. Hafs ibn Umar is Hafs ibn Umar ibn Abi al-Attaf al-Madani, and Ibrahim ibn Abdullah is Ibrahim ibn Abdullah ibn Qariz."
"6751","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Shaybah Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, from Musa ibn Talhah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is Greatest, and there is no power nor strength except through Allah, an angel folds his wing over them and does not return with anything until he bears them to the Throne, and he does not pass by anything except that it invokes blessings upon them and upon their sayer. And tasbih is declaring Allah free of every evil. And whoever says: There is no power nor strength except through Allah, the Most High, the Most Great, Allah says: My servant has submitted and surrendered. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Talhah except Uthman ibn Abdullah ibn Mawhab, and no one narrated it from Uthman except Abu Shaybah; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"6752","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Sanani narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give a single salutation facing forward. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad."
"6753","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Waqid, from Bishr ibn Ubaydullah, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Awf ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, I shall inform you about leadership. They said: What is it? He said: Its beginning is blame, its second is regret, and its third is punishment on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who acts justly. This hadith is not narrated from Awf ibn Malik except with this chain; Zayd ibn Waqid is alone in transmitting it."
"6754","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa al-Kufi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Ibn Abi Mulaykah narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out for his Hajj pilgrimage while joyful and happy with his ummah because of what he saw of their unity and their great number, then he returned grieving. I said: O Messenger of Allah, you left me joyful with your ummah and returned to me grieving? He said: I entered the Kabah, and I wish I had not entered it; I fear lest I burden my ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Musa except Hisham ibn Ammar."
"6755","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa narrated to us, from Muzahir ibn Aslam, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The divorce of a slave woman is two divorces, and her waiting period is two menstrual cycles. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Musa except Hisham ibn Ammar, and no one narrated it from Muzahir ibn Aslam except Ibn Jurayj, Sulayman ibn Musa al-Kufi, and Abu Asim."
"6756","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Salamah al-Nasri al-Kufi narrated to me, from al-Mughirah ibn Abdullah al-Yashkuri, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith, from Abu Kathir al-Zubaydi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: Beware of injustice, for injustice is darkness on the Day of Resurrection; beware of obscenity, for Allah does not love obscenity nor indulging in it; beware of miserliness, for miserliness destroyed those before you: it commanded them to sever their kinship ties and they severed them. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: That your blood be shed and your horse hamstrung. He said: Which emigration is best? He said: That you abandon what your Lord dislikes. They are two emigrations: an emigration of the settled and an emigration of the nomad. As for the emigration of the nomad, when he is called he answers and when he is commanded he obeys; as for the emigration of the settled, it is the more severely tried of the two and the greater in reward. No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Salamah al-Nasri except Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay; Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"6757","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Yunus al-Kufi narrated to me, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Aishah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A prayer in the Sacred Mosque is better than a hundred prayers elsewhere. No one narrates this hadith from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq except Suwayd; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6758","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The two sons of al-As are believers, and Amr ibn al-As is in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman except al-Muttalib, nor narrated it from al-Muttalib except Kathir ibn Zayd, nor narrated it from Kathir except Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6759","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri narrated to us, Abu Hamzah al-Thumali narrated to us, from Abu Jafar Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she said: O Messenger of Allah, the women of Banu al-Mughirah have held their mourning gathering for al-Walid ibn al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, so he gave her permission, and she stood while saying. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ali except Abu Hamzah, nor from Abu Hamzah except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Qasri; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6760","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Abu Hujayyah al-Kindi informed me, from Ubayd ibn Abi al-Jad, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, that while he was governor over Hims he summoned Kab ibn Murrah and said: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and be cautious. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim person, Allah frees for every limb of him a limb of him from the Fire. Then he said: Narrate to us from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and be cautious. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicated against Mudar, and years befell them that took away wealth, or what Allah willed of it, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, Mudar has been destroyed, so supplicate to Allah for them. He said: You are bold toward me. Then he said to him concerning that, then he stood on Friday and said: O Allah, give us a rescuing rain, wholesome, copious, widespread, swift without delay, beneficial without harm. And they were given rain. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd ibn Abi al-Jad except al-Ajlah, nor from al-Ajlah except Shayban, nor from Shayban except Muhammad ibn Shuayb; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it. Al-Ajlah is Abu Hujayyah Yahya ibn Abdullah."
"6761","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, Ali ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah narrated to us, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered the expulsion of Banu al-Nadir, some people among them came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have ordered our expulsion, and we have debts owed by people that have not yet fallen due. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reduce them and hasten their collection. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Yazid ibn Rukanah except Muslim ibn Khalid."
"6762","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from al-Zuhri, from al-Saib ibn Yazid, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar did not appoint a judge. And the first to appoint judges was Umar; he said: Keep the people away from me concerning a dirham and two dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yazid ibn Abi Habib, nor from Yazid except Ibn Lahiah, nor from Ibn Lahiah except al-Walid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6763","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Masruq al-Kindi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydullah al-Arzami narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah and Yunus ibn Khabbab, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Judges are three: two in the Fire and one in Paradise. A man who sat for the people and judged between them with no knowledge of judging, destroying their rights; a man who knew and acted unjustly while knowing; and a man who knew and judged by his knowledge with the truth, so this one is in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah except al-Arzami, and no one narrated it from al-Arzami except Muhammad ibn Masruq; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6764","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah narrated to us, from his uncle Musa ibn Talhah, Abu Waqid al-Laythi narrated to me, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), my knee touching his knee, when someone came to him and took hold of his ear, and the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) changed and blood rushed to his features. Then he said: This is the messenger of Amir ibn al-Tufayl threatening me and threatening those near me, and Allah sufficed me against him through my two sons from the children of Ismail, through the two sons of Qaylah. Hisham said: Meaning the Ansar. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Waqid except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6765","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Kathir ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Muttalib ibn Abdullah ibn Hantab, from Ibn Umar, he said: I never saw anyone among people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more generous than Muawiyah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muttalib except Kathir, nor from Kathir except Abdullah ibn Yazid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6766","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Abi Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Ala ibn Abi Amrah, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Muadh ibn Jabal, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The Milky Way in the sky is the sweat of the serpent that is beneath the Throne. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6767","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Dawud ibn Qays al-Madani narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Saib ibn Yazid saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me refuge with the Opening of the Book, spitting. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Qays except Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri; Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"6768","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Rafi ibn Khadij, he said: Nuayman said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a severe feverish illness. He said: Where are you, O Nuayman, from Mahyaah? And it was an unhealthy land. This hadith was not narrated from Rafi except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6769","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Kab ibn Alqamah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Hubuli, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that a man complained to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of poor livelihood, and he said: Raise a young one. So he asked him and he said: A foal, or a slave girl, or a boy. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn al-Harith except Abdullah ibn Yazid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"6770","And with the same chain: Abdullah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from Tufayl ibn Sinan, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, he said: I heard a man saying to Ibn Umar: Did you not hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I jest, but I speak only the truth? He said: Yes. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd ibn Umayr except Tufayl ibn Sinan, nor narrated it from Tufayl except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, nor from Sulayman except Abdullah ibn Yazid; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"6771","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Muhammad al-Sanani narrated to us, Abu Salamah al-Amili narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Urwah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said on the day of Hunayn at al-Jiranah: Ten things are permitted for Muslims in their campaigns: honey, water, oil, vinegar, salt, dust, stones, unshaped wood, fresh skins, and food one takes out with him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abu Salamah al-Amili; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6772","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Shubrumah narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Zura ibn Amr ibn Jarir, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing transmits infection to anything. A Bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, camels are in the sands like gazelles, then a camel comes with on its lip or at the root of its tail something like a speck of mange, and no camel remains among them except that it becomes mangy? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A defect, and decree. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abdullah ibn Shubrumah except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"6773","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Mahmud ibn Khalid narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Nafi narrated to us, he said: I was riding behind Ibn Umar when a shepherd playing a flute passed by, and he struck the she-camel's face and turned it away from the road, then he placed his two fingers in his ears and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) doing it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam except Khalid ibn Abi Khalid; his son Mahmud is alone in transmitting it."
"6774","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to me that he heard Ibn Jurayj narrating from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells fruit and it is struck by a calamity, let him not take anything from his brother; for what does one of you take the wealth of his Muslim brother? No one narrated this hadith from Thawr ibn Yazid except Yahya ibn Hamzah; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6775","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, that Hisham ibn Abd al-Malik paid seven thousand dinars on behalf of al-Zuhri, then Hisham said to al-Zuhri: Do not return to its like. Al-Zuhri said: O Commander of the Believers, Said ibn al-Musayyib narrated to me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from one hole twice. Then al-Zuhri returned and borrowed again, and Hisham spoke to him about that, and he said: O Commander of the Believers, experiences do not benefit the generous. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz except al-Walid ibn Muslim; Hisham ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it."
"6776","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam is founded upon five: testifying that there is no god but Allah, alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger; establishing prayer; giving zakat; performing Hajj to the House; and fasting Ramadan. And a man kept repeating them, saying: Fasting before Hajj, while Abdullah would say: And Hajj to the House, and fasting Ramadan. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydullah except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"6777","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, Dawud ibn Isa al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubaydullah, from Salim, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever buys a sheep whose udder has been tied up and milks it for three days has the choice: if he wishes he keeps it, and otherwise he returns it with a saa of dates. No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Dawud ibn Isa; Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz is alone in transmitting it."
"6778","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever honors a person of innovation has helped in demolishing Islam. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani."
"6779","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ali ibn Sulayman al-Kalbi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I served the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for ten years, and he never said to me for something I did: Why did you do such and such? Nor for something I did not do: Why did you not do such and such? No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Ali ibn Sulayman; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6780","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off a thief. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi."
"6781","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Hiql ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let one of you eat with his right hand and drink with his right hand, for Satan eats with his left, takes with his left, and gives with his left. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except al-Hiql; Hisham is alone in transmitting it."
"6782","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid narrated to us, Abu Khulayd Utbah ibn Hammad narrated to us, from al-Awzai and Ibn Thawban, from his father, from Makhul, from Malik ibn Yakhamir, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah looks upon His creation on the night of the middle of Shaban and forgives all His creation, except a polytheist or one harboring rancor. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai and Ibn Thawban except Abu Khulayd Utbah ibn Hammad; Hisham ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it from al-Awzai."
"6783","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa al-Zuhri narrated to us, Muzahir ibn Aslam al-Makhzumi narrated to us, Said al-Maqburi informed me, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite ten verses from the end of Surah Al Imran every night. No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except Muzahir ibn Aslam, nor from Muzahir except Sulayman ibn Musa; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6784","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Khushani narrated to us, Umar ibn Abdullah, the freed slave of Ghufrah, narrated to me, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There shall be in this ummah a people who say there is no decree; they are the Magians of this ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Umar, the freed slave of Ghufrah, except al-Hasan ibn Yahya; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6785","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from his father, he said: Ali ibn Abi Talib wrote a letter for me and said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me with it. He said: When you take your bed, say: I seek refuge in the Noble Face of Allah and His perfect words from the evil of what You seize by its forelock. O Allah, You remove debt and sin. O Allah, do not defeat Your troops, do not break Your promise, and the wealth of the wealthy does not avail against You. Glory be to You and with Your praise. Abu Ishaq said: I mentioned it to Abu Maysarah al-Hamdani, and he narrated to me the like of it from Abdullah ibn Masud, except that he said: From the evil of what You grasp by its forelock."
"6786","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, he said: I heard Dawud ibn Farahij saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: By Allah, Allah never beautified a man's creation and character and then the Fire ever consumes him. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Farahij except Abu Ghassan, nor from Abu Ghassan except Abdullah ibn Yazid al-Bakri; Hisham ibn Ammar is alone in transmitting it."
"6787","Muhammad ibn Abi Zura al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Amr ibn Waqid narrated to us, Yunus ibn Maysarah ibn Halbas narrated to us, from Abu Idris, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my speech and does not add to it. Many a bearer of a word to one more comprehending of it than him. Three things the heart of a believer never holds deceit over: sincerity to Allah, sincere counsel to those in authority, and holding fast to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses those behind them. This hadith is not narrated from Muadh ibn Jabal except with this chain; Amr ibn Waqid is alone in transmitting it."
"6788","Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar ibn Bilal al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, Abu Maryam narrated to me that he heard Hisham ibn Abi Ruqayyah saying: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever wears silk in this world is forbidden it in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd."
"6789","Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu Qilabah, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Humran, from Uthman, that he performed ablution three times three times and said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution like this ablution of mine, thus. No one included between Qatadah and Muslim ibn Yasar, Abu Qilabah, in this hadith except Said ibn Bashir; Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari is alone in transmitting it."
"6790","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said narrated to me, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No newborn is born except that Satan touches him when he is born, so he begins crying loudly from its touch, except Maryam and her son. Then Abu Hurayrah says: Recite if you wish: And I seek refuge for her with You and her offspring from Satan, the accursed. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Zuhayr ibn Muhammad; Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay is alone in transmitting it."
"6791","And with the same chain: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to the people and said: While a man was driving a cow and wanted to ride it, it turned to him and said: We were not created for this; we were created for plowing. Those around him said: Glory be to Allah, a cow spoke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in it, I, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, though they were not there. Then he said: A man said: While I was among sheep of mine pasturing them, a wolf came and seized a sheep, and I pursued it and took it from him, and it said: How will you be on the day of the beast of prey when there is no shepherd for it but me. They said: Glory be to Allah, a wolf spoke. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in it, I, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, though they were not there. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay."
"6792","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, Sad ibn Ubaydah narrated to me, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Judges are three: two judges in the Fire and one judge in Paradise. A judge who abandoned the truth while knowing; a judge who judged without the truth while not knowing, destroying people's rights; these two are in the Fire. And a judge who judged with the truth, so this one is in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ubaydah except Yahya ibn Hamzah; Muhammad ibn Bakkar is alone in transmitting it."
"6793","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Rabah ibn al-Walid al-Dhimari narrated to us, al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, he said: I heard Ata ibn Abi Rabah saying: I heard Jabir ibn Abdullah saying: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the prayer times. When the sun declined, Bilal called the adhan for Zuhr, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he established the prayer, and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Asr when we thought a man's shadow was longer than him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he established the prayer, and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun had set, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he established the prayer, and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Isha when the whiteness of day had gone, which is the twilight, then he ordered him and he established the prayer, and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Fajr when dawn rose, and he ordered him and he established the prayer, and he prayed. Then Bilal called the adhan the next day for Zuhr when the sun declined, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed it until the shadow of everything was like it, and he established and prayed. Then he called the adhan for Asr, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed it until the shadow of everything was twice it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he established and prayed. Then he called the adhan for Maghrib when the sun set, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delayed it until the whiteness of day almost disappeared, which is the beginning of twilight as it appears. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered him and he established the prayer, and he prayed. Then he called the adhan for Isha when the twilight had gone, and we slept then rose repeatedly, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: No one among people awaits this prayer but you, and you shall remain in prayer as long as you await it. Were it not that I would cause hardship for my ummah, I would have ordered delaying this prayer until midnight and near midnight. Then he called the adhan for Fajr, and he delayed it until the sun almost rose, and he ordered him and he established the prayer and he prayed. Then he said: The time is between these two times. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mutim ibn al-Miqdam except Rabah ibn al-Walid; Marwan ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"6794","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Marwan narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Musa al-Kufi narrated to us, from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No people withhold zakat except that Allah tries them with years of drought. No one narrated this hadith from Fudayl ibn Ghazwan except Sulayman ibn Musa; Marwan ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"6795","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have a right over Quraysh, and they have a right over you: as long as they covenant and fulfill, and when asked for mercy they show mercy, and when they judge they are just, and when entrusted they deliver. Whoever among them does not do that, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir."
"6796","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adam is in the lowest heaven, Isa and Yahya in the second, Yusuf in the third, Idris in the fourth, Harun in the fifth, Musa in the sixth, and Ibrahim in the seventh. No one narrated this hadith in this order from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir; Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6797","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Nawf al-Bikali, from Abdullah ibn Amr ibn al-As, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There shall be an emigration after an emigration; the best of the people of earth shall be toward the emigration place of Ibrahim, upon him be peace. The worst of its people shall remain in it; the earth ejects them and the soul of Allah finds them loathsome. Allah shall send upon them a fire that gathers them with monkeys and pigs; it rests at midday when they rest and moves in the evening when they move, and it consumes whoever lags behind. And a people shall be spread in the east; whenever a generation arises, a generation is cut off; the Dajjal emerges among their flanks. No one included between Shahr ibn Hawshab and Abdullah ibn Amr anyone among those who narrated it from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir; al-Walid ibn al-Walid is alone in transmitting it."
"6798","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abdullah ibn Sarjis, he said: I came to pray Fajr while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in prayer, so I prayed two rakahs then entered the prayer. When he finished, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With which of the two did you reckon: the first two or the latter two? No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir, nor from Said except Marwan ibn Muhammad; al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal is alone in transmitting it."
"6799","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Mughaffal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a man to urinate in his bathing place, and said: It brings about whisperings. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, except Said ibn Bashir; Marwan ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it. And Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated it from Qatadah, from Said ibn Abi al-Hasan."
"6800","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muawiyah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir; Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6801","Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us, from Said ibn Bashir, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not curse night and day, nor the sun, nor the moon, nor the winds, for they are a mercy to some people and a punishment to others. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Said ibn Bashir."
"6802","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Umar ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir, from Makhul, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, that he asked Aishah: Are women permitted to pray upon riding animals? She said: They were not permitted that, in hardship nor in ease. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except al-Numan ibn al-Mundhir."
"6803","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Zayd ibn Yahya ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, Makhul narrated to me, from Salamah ibn Abi Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Ibn Umar, that he proposed to Nuaym ibn Abdullah al-Adawi al-Nahham for his daughter, and she was a virgin, and Nuaym said to him: I have an orphan whom I do not prefer anyone over. So the girl's mother, the wife of Nuaym, went out until she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that, and informed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of her and her daughter's dislike of the orphan. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her father and said: Please her and please her daughter. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Muhammad ibn Rashid."
"6804","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Maslamah al-Muaddil, from the people of Dariyya, narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Hani, from Abu al-Adhra, from Umm al-Darda, from Abu al-Darda, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Revere Allah and He will forgive you, meaning: Submit to Allah. No one said in this hadith, from Abu al-Adhra: from Umm al-Darda, among those who narrated it from Umayr ibn Hani, except Maslamah al-Muaddil, and no one narrated it from Maslamah except Marwan. And Ibn Thawban narrated it from Umayr ibn Hani, from Abu al-Adhra, from Abu al-Darda."
"6805","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Utbah narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri and Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Abdullah ibn Maqil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Remorse is repentance. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except al-Walid ibn Muslim; al-Walid ibn Utbah is alone in transmitting it."
"6806","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, al-Walid ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise was adorned for Ramadan from the beginning of the year to the year. When the first day of Ramadan comes, a wind blows from beneath the Throne, and the leaves of Paradise rustle before the wide-eyed maidens, and they say: O Lord, appoint for us husbands among Your servants whose eyes find delight in them and whose eyes find delight in us. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except al-Walid ibn al-Walid."
"6807","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Let none of you come to me on the Day of Resurrection carrying a camel upon his neck that bellows, saying: O Muhammad. And I say: I own nothing for you; you were informed. Let none of you come to me on the Day of Resurrection carrying a sheep upon his neck that bleats, saying: O Muhammad. And I say: I own nothing for you; you were informed. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay."
"6808","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Muallim al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Dawud Sulayman ibn Musa al-Kufi narrated to me, Dalham ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Masruq, that he entered upon Aishah on the day of Arafah and said: Give me drink. Aishah said: O boy, give him honey to drink. Then she said: Are you not fasting, O Masruq? He said: No, I fear it may be the day of sacrifice. Aishah said: It is not that; the day of Arafah is the day the imam recognizes, and the day of sacrifice is the day the imam sacrifices. Did you not hear, O Masruq, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to equate it with fasting a thousand days? No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Dalham ibn Salih, nor from Dalham except Sulayman ibn Musa; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"6809","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Muallim narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Shayban Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Mihran al-Amash, from Abu Qays Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abdullah ibn Masud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed concerning a daughter, a son's daughter, and a full sister: the daughter gets half, the son's daughter gets a sixth, and the sister gets what remains. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Shayban and Ali ibn Mushir; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it from Shayban."
"6810","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ismail al-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), concerning an ostrich egg: Fasting a day or feeding a poor person, meaning the one in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Ibn Jurayj; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"6811","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Uthman al-Muallim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shuayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Isa ibn Abdullah informed me, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Zuhri, from Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdullah, from his father Ibn Umar, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he used to send collectors for charities, he would order them that what they took of charities be placed first among the relatives of those from whom it was taken, then the first nearest; if he had no relatives, then to the members of the clan, then to the needy among neighbors and others. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Waqqasi, and no one narrated it from Uthman except Isa ibn Abdullah; Muhammad ibn Shuayb is alone in transmitting it."
"6812","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hamzah narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does good in what remains is forgiven for what has passed, and whoever does evil in what remains is seized for what has passed and what remains. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except Yahya ibn Hamzah."
"6813","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Dubarah ibn Abdullah ibn al-Salil narrated to me, from Duwayd ibn Nafi, from Ibn Shihab, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that Abu Qatadah ibn Ribi informed him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah said: I have obligated upon you five prayers, and I have made a covenant with Myself that whoever guards them at their times, I shall admit him into Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Duwayd ibn Nafi, nor from Duwayd except Dubarah; Baqiyyah is alone in transmitting it."
"6814","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Umar ibn Salih al-Azdi narrated to us, Abu Jamrah Nasr ibn Imran narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to a tribe of Arabs inviting them to Islam, and they did not accept the letter, and they returned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him. He said: Had I sent it to a people on the shore of Oman from Azd Shanuah and Aslam, they would have accepted it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to al-Julanda inviting him to Islam, and he accepted it and embraced Islam, and he sent to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a gift, and it arrived after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had passed away, so Abu Bakr made the gift an inheritance and divided it between Fatimah and al-Abbas."
"6815","And with the same chain: from Ibn Abbas, he said: Four hundred men of Daws came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Welcome to the people of best faces, sweetest mouths, and greatest trustworthiness. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Jamrah except Umar ibn Salih."
"6816","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from Abu Ishaq, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr. No one reported this hadith from Abu Ishaq except his son Yunus; Ismail ibn Ayyash alone transmitted it."
"6817","Muhammad ibn Harun ibn Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Maymun, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to give salam to his right and to his left until the whiteness of his cheek could be seen. No one reported this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, except Khalid ibn Maymun, and no one reported it from Khalid ibn Maymun except Said ibn Abi Arubah; Shu'ayb ibn Ishaq alone transmitted it."
"6818","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Hassan al-Jurashi narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Ma'dan, from Amr ibn al-Aswad al-Ansi, from Umm Haram bint Milhan, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I saw the first army of my ummah riding upon the sea have made Paradise obligatory for themselves, so I said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah that I be among them. He said: O Allah, place her among them. No one reported this hadith from Thawr ibn Yazid except Ayyub ibn Hassan; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"6819","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay' narrated to us, Thawr ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, that Amrah bint Abd al-Rahman reported to him, that Aishah said: Had the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seen what women have newly introduced after him, he would have barred them from attending the mosques, just as the women of the Children of Israel were barred. No one reported this hadith from Thawr ibn Yazid except Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay'."
"6820","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Kathir al-Tawil narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, al-Zuhri reported to me, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man and I fear hardship for myself, and I do not possess the means to marry women; do you permit me to castrate myself? He remained silent toward me. Then I repeated: O Messenger of Allah, I am a young man and do not have the means to marry women; do you permit me to castrate myself? And I said the same a third time, whereupon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abu Hurayrah, the Pen has dried upon what you shall meet, so undergo castration despite that, or leave it. No one reported this hadith from al-Awzai, from Yunus, except Abdullah ibn Kathir; al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal alone transmitted it."
"6821","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, from Urwah ibn Ruwaym, from Abdullah ibn al-Daylami, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Sulayman ibn Dawud asked Allah for three things; He granted him two, and I hope He granted him the third. He asked Him to judge with a judgment coinciding with His judgment, and it was granted; he asked Him for a dominion befitting no one after him, and it was granted; and he asked that any servant who comes to Bayt al-Maqdis seeking nothing but prayer therein emerge from his sins like the day his mother bore him. No one reported this hadith from Urwah ibn Ruwaym except Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb."
"6822","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Walid al-Khallal narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muhammad al-Tatari narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been favored over mankind by four things: generosity, courage, frequency of marital intercourse, and strength of grip."
"6823","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from al-A'mash, from Ribi ibn Hirash, from Abu al-Abyad, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray Asr while the sun was white and high. No one reported this hadith from al-A'mash except Abd al-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, and no one from Abd al-Aziz except Ismail ibn Ayyash; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"6824","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Said ibn Yahya narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, from Amr ibn Sulaym al-Zuraqi who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib say: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until when we were at the watering place that belonged to Sa'd, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, Ibrahim is Your servant and intimate friend; he supplicated to You for blessings for the people of Makkah, and Muhammad is Your servant and Messenger, and I supplicate to You for the people of Madinah that You bless them in their sa' and their mudd as You blessed the people of Makkah, and along with the blessing two further blessings. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar except Sa'dan ibn Yahya; Sulayman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from Ibn Umar except through this chain."
"6825","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Said ibn Mansur al-Judhami narrated to us, from his grandfather Malik ibn Ahmar, that when news of the arrival of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached him, he came as a delegate to him, and he accepted his Islam, and he asked him to write for him a document with which to call to Islam. So he wrote for him on a piece of leather: In the name of Allah, the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; this is a document from Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, to Malik ibn Ahmar and those Muslims who follow him: security for them so long as they establish prayer, give zakat, follow the Muslims, shun the polytheists, pay the fifth of the spoils, the share of the debtors, and such-and-such share and such-and-such share; they are secure under the security of Allah and the security of Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not reported from Malik ibn Ahmar except through this chain; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone transmitted it."
"6826","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Khalid al-Azraq narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came from one of the outskirts of Madinah intending to pray, and found the people had already prayed, so he went to his house, gathered his household, then led them in prayer. No one reported this hadith from Khalid al-Hadhdha except Muawiyah ibn Yahya, and no one reported it from Muawiyah except al-Walid ibn Muslim; Hisham ibn Khalid alone transmitted it."
"6827","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham narrated to us, Hatim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdullah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adhere to night prayer, even if only one rak'ah. One day he came out for Fajr and found a man performing supererogatory prayer, and said: Will you not desist? Two prayers together? No one reported this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Hatim; Hisham ibn Ammar alone transmitted it."
"6828","Muhammad ibn Harun narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Nastas narrated to us, Mirba' reported to me, from Umm Anas ibn Malik, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, counsel me. He said: Abandon acts of disobedience, for it is the best emigration; guard the obligatory duties, for they are the best jihad; and remember Allah abundantly, for you will bring nothing to Allah more beloved to Him than abundant remembrance of Him. This hadith is not reported from Umm Anas the Ansari woman, who is not Umm Sulaym the mother of Anas ibn Malik but another Ansari woman. This hadith was reported only through this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar alone transmitted it."
"6829","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bakkar al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, that his father Yazid ibn Jabir reported to him, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he forbade eating the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, and nabidh in earthen jars, and visiting graves; then afterwards the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you the meat of sacrificial animals after three days, so eat as you wish; I had forbidden you nabidh in jars, so drink, but every intoxicant is unlawful; and I had forbidden you visiting graves, so visit them but do not say what angers Allah. No one reported this hadith from Yazid ibn Jabir except Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, and no one from Abd al-Rahman except Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb; Abd al-Hamid alone transmitted it."
"6830","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid al-Bayruti narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Bakkar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu Ghalib, from Abu Umamah, that a man confronted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which jihad is best? He said: A word of truth before an unjust ruler. No one reported this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"6831","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Rahabi, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari who said: I asked Aishah what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in Witr. She said: He used to recite in the first rak'ah the Mother of the Book and Say: He is Allah, the One, in the second rak'ah the Mother of the Book and Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of the daybreak, and in the third rak'ah the Mother of the Book and Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of mankind. This hadith is not reported from Abu Musa, from Aishah, except through this chain; Ismail ibn Ayyash alone transmitted it."
"6832","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, Abu al-Zubayr informed me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The leg of a wild donkey at Kura' al-Ghamim was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he returned it to its owner and apologized to him, saying: We are in ihram. No one reported this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Said ibn Bashir and Hammad ibn Shu'ayb."
"6833","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey when a man in ihram fell and died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Wash him and shroud him in his garment, do not cover his head, for he will be raised on the Day of Resurrection reciting the talbiyah. No one reported this hadith from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"6834","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Khulayd ibn D'alaj narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: I said to Ali ibn Abi Talib: The people claim concerning the saying of Allah, Exalted be His mention: And a witness from him follows him, that you are the one following? He said: I wish I were he, but it is the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one reported this hadith from Qatadah, from Urwah, except Khulayd ibn D'alaj; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone transmitted it."
"6835","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying, Exalted be He: Until when he attains his full strength, he said: Thirty-three, and it is the age at which Isa son of Maryam (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was raised up. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except Sadaqah ibn Yazid; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone transmitted it."
"6836","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd ibn Abi Ghaniyyah narrated to us, Asim ibn Abi al-Najud informed me, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The world shall not end until a man from my household rules, whose name coincides with my name. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"6837","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Humayd narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wrote to us while we were in the land of Juhaynah: Do not benefit from carrion by using its sinews or its hide. No one reported this hadith from al-Hakam, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, except Ibn Abi Ghaniyyah; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone transmitted it. The people reported it from al-Hakam, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym."
"6838","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Labid narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Said ibn Bashir, from Matar al-Warraq, that he reported to him, from Abu Qilabah, from al-Ash'ath al-San'ani, that Abu Jandal ibn Suhayl and al-Harith ibn Muawiyah passed by Bilal, the mu'adhdhin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while he was performing ablution at the ablution area of the Damascus mosque, and asked him about wiping over the leather socks. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wipe over the leather socks and the head covering. No one reported this hadith from Matar al-Warraq except Said ibn Bashir."
"6839","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi, Durran, narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail Abu Salamah al-Tabudhaki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Abu Hurayrah who said: We were forbidden to drink from the broken edge of the vessel. No one reported this hadith from Jafar ibn Burqan except Ma'mar, and no one from Ma'mar except Ibn al-Mubarak; Musa ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"6840","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja al-Ghudani narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Qays ibn Sa'd reported to me, from Yazid ibn Hurmuz who said: Najdah wrote to Ibn Abbas asking him about certain matters, and I witnessed Ibn Abbas when he read the letter and when he wrote its reply. Ibn Abbas said: Were it not to turn him back from a misguidance he had fallen into, I would not have written to him, nor for the comfort of an eye. So he wrote to him: You asked about the share of the near kindred whom Allah mentioned, and we considered ourselves, the kin of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to be them, but our people denied us that. You asked about the orphan, when his orphanhood ends: when he reaches marriageable age and sound judgment is perceived in him, his wealth is handed to him and his orphanhood ends. You asked whether the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to kill any of the children of the polytheists: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never killed any of them. And you asked about the woman and the slave, whether they have a fixed share when present: they have no fixed share except to be given something from the spoils of the people. No one reported this hadith from Qays ibn Sa'd except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"6841","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim al-Makki narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah who said: A man passed by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw in his strength and vigor what amazed them, and said: O Messenger of Allah, if only this were in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If he went out striving for his small children, he is in the path of Allah; if he went out striving for two aged elderly parents, he is in the path of Allah; if he strives for himself to keep it chaste, he is in the path of Allah; but if he went out for show and boasting, he is in the path of Satan. No one reported this hadith from al-Hakam except Ismail ibn Muslim, and no one reported it from Ismail except Hammam; Muhammad ibn Kathir alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from Ka'b ibn Ujrah except through this chain."
"6842","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Qays ibn Sa'd narrated to us, Ata ibn Abi Rabah reported to me, from Umm Uthman bint Khuthaym, from Umm Kurz, that she heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked about the aqiqah, and he said: For the boy two sheep, and for the girl one sheep. No one reported this hadith from Qays ibn Sa'd except Jarir ibn Hazim."
"6843","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: As for the Fire, people will be cast into it and it will say: Is there more? Until its Lord, Blessed and Exalted be He, comes to it and places His Foot upon it, whereupon it will contract and say: Enough, enough. As for Paradise, Allah will create for it a creation as He wills. No one reported this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6844","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, that the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Messenger of Allah, this salam upon you we know; how then do we send blessings upon you? He said: Say: O Allah, send blessings upon Muhammad and upon the family of Muhammad as You sent blessings upon Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious; and bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed Ibrahim, indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. No one reported this hadith from Qays ibn Sa'd except Hammad ibn Salamah."
"6845","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Razin, from his brother, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has forbidden the singing slave-girl, her sale, her price, teaching her, and listening to her. This hadith is not reported from Ibn Sabit, from Aishah, except through this chain; Muhammad ibn Kathir alone transmitted it."
"6846","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Nuh ibn Qays al-Tai narrated to us, from Yazid al-Raqashi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Blessed and Exalted be He, will grant intercession on the Day of Resurrection to Adam for all his progeny, concerning one hundred million and ten million. This hadith is not reported from Anas except through this chain; Musa ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"6847","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Ibn Tawus, from his father, from Safwan ibn Umayyah, that it was said to him: None shall enter Paradise except one who emigrated. So I said: I shall not go to my dwelling until I go to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and ask him. So I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: This man with him stole a cloak of mine, so he ordered his hand cut. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have gifted it to him. He said: Why not before you brought him to me? I said: O Messenger of Allah, they say none shall enter Paradise except one who emigrated? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no emigration after the conquest of Makkah, but jihad and intention; and when you are called to march forth, march forth. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Tawus except Wuhayb; Musa ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"6848","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Abdi narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to us, from Kahmas ibn al-Hasan, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from Aishah who said: A woman came seeking the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not find him, so she sat until he came. When he came I said: O Messenger of Allah, this woman has a need of you. He said: What is your need? She said: O Messenger of Allah, my father married me to a son of his brother to raise his lowliness, without consulting me; do I have any say over myself? He said: Yes. She said: I would never reject anything my father did, but I wished the women to know whether they have any say over themselves or not. None perfected this hadith from Kahmas except Jafar ibn Sulayman and Waki' ibn al-Jarrah."
"6849","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Umm Muhammad, from Aishah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not sleep by night or day then wake except that he used the siwak before performing ablution. No one reported this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Hammam."
"6850","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed in the house of Umm Sulaym upon a green mat, and they prayed behind him. No one reported this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Sulayman ibn Kathir and Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"6851","And with the same chain: Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar reported to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar who said: Whenever it was a cold night or a rainy night, the caller of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would call: Pray in your dwellings. No one reported this hadith from Sulayman ibn Kathir except his brother Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"6852","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Hammam narrated to us, from Layth, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever says I am learned is ignorant. This hadith is not reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain; Muhammad ibn Kathir alone transmitted it."
"6853","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to present himself to the people at the standing place: Is there no man to carry me to his people, for Quraysh have prevented me from conveying the speech of my Lord? Then a man from Hamdan came to him and he said: From whom are you? He said: From Hamdan. He said: Do you have protection? He said: Yes. Then the Hamdani man feared his people would betray him, so he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I shall go to them, then meet you next year. He said to him: Go forth. And the delegations of the Ansar came in Rajab. No one reported this hadith from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah except Israil."
"6854","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Ja'd Abu Uthman, from Anas ibn Malik, from Jabir ibn Abdullah, that the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complained to him of thirst, so he called for a large cup and called for water and poured it into it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his palm in the cup and said: Draw water. So I saw the water gushing forth like springs from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until the people all drank. This hadith is not reported from Anas, from Jabir, except through this chain; Jafar ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"6855","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Ziyad Abu Hamzah al-Habati narrated to us, Abu Shaddad, a man from Dama, a village of the villages of Oman, reported to me, saying: The letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us, to the people of Oman: Peace; as for what follows: affirm the testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, pay zakat, mark out mosques, otherwise I shall raid you. Abu Shaddad said: We found no one to read the letter to us until we found a black boy who read it to us. I said to Abu Shaddad: Who was then over Oman administering their affairs? He said: A Persian commander of the commanders of Kisra called Sahan. This hadith is not reported from Abu Shaddad except through this chain; Musa ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"6856","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Shaddad ibn Said narrated to us, Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of the youth of Quraysh, guard your private parts; indeed whoever guards his private part shall have Paradise. No one reported this hadith from al-Jurayri except Shaddad; Muslim alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from Ibn Abbas except through this chain."
"6857","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh al-Halabi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Maslamah al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mu'adhdhins shall have the longest necks of people on the Day of Resurrection, and nothing hears him but will testify for him on the Day of Resurrection. No one reported this hadith from Khalid ibn Abi al-Salt except al-Qa'nabi."
"6858","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, Umm Hakim reported to me, saying: I heard Umm Ishaq say: I emigrated with my brother to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah, and when I was partway along, my brother said to me: Stay here, O Umm Ishaq, for I forgot my provisions in Makkah. I said: I fear for you from my wicked husband. He said: No, Allah willing. She said: So I stayed for days, then a man I knew but shall not name passed by me and said: What keeps you seated here, O Umm Ishaq? I said: I am waiting for Ishaq; he went for provisions of his in Makkah. He said: You have no Ishaq; your wicked husband caught up with him and killed him. So I arrived and entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was performing ablution. I said: O Messenger of Allah, Ishaq has been killed. And I was weeping, and he would look at me, and when I looked at him he would lower his gaze in ablution, then took a handful of water and sprinkled it on my face. Bashshar said: My grandmother said: Great calamities would befall us, and we would see tears on her eyes but none touching her cheek. This hadith is not reported from Umm Ishaq except through this chain; Musa ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"6859","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Zaynab bint Nubayt, the wife of Anas ibn Malik, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr, that she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he ordered her to make a stipulation. No one reported this hadith from Humayd except Sulayman ibn Kathir; Muhammad ibn Kathir alone transmitted it."
"6860","Muhammad ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Abu al-Attuf narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever arrives as a pilgrim should circumambulate between al-Safa and al-Marwah before going to Mina."
"6861","And with the same chain: from Abu al-Attuf, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from Ibn Umar who said: I prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed two rak'ahs before Zuhr and two after it, two rak'ahs after Maghrib, two rak'ahs after Isha, and two rak'ahs before Fajr. No two hadiths were reported from Abu al-Attuf except by Yazid ibn Harun."
"6862","And with the same chain: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Jarrah ibn al-Minhal narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the jamarat at the decline of the sun with pebbles like those used for flicking, while upon his mount. No one reported this hadith from al-Jarrah ibn al-Minhal except Yazid ibn Harun."
"6863","Muhammad ibn Yasir al-Hadhdha al-Dimashqi al-Jubayli narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abu Ghanim al-Kalai, from Abu Ghassan al-Dabbi who said: I went out walking with my father in the outskirts of al-Harrah, and Abu Hurayrah met me and said to me: Who is this? I said: My father. He said: Do not walk in front of your father, but walk behind him or beside him; do not let anyone come between you and him; do not walk above a roof under which your father is; and do not eat a bone your father has looked at, for perhaps he desired it. Then he said: Do you know Abdullah ibn Khidash? I said: No. He said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: His thigh in Hell shall be like Uhud, and his molar like al-Bayda. Abu Hurayrah said: I said: And why is that, O Messenger of Allah? He said: He was disobedient to his parents. No one reported this hadith from Abu Ghassan al-Dabbi except Abu Ghanim al-Kalai; al-Walid alone transmitted it."
"6864","Muhammad ibn Yasir al-Hadhdha narrated to us, Duhaym narrated to us, Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Khuzai, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Four enter the morning in the anger of Allah and enter the evening in the wrath of Allah. I said: And who are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The men who imitate women, the women who imitate men, the one who goes to beasts, and the one who goes to men. No one reported this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Khuzai except Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"6865","Muhammad ibn Yasir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abu Shaybah Yahya ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kindi narrated to us, from Hibban ibn Abi Jabalah, from Amr ibn al-As who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not equate anyone of his companions with me and Khalid ibn al-Walid since we embraced Islam. This hadith is not reported from Amr ibn al-As except through this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar alone transmitted it."
"6866","Muhammad ibn Yasir narrated to us, Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, Sadaqah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah shall be in the shade of Allah on a day when there is no shade but His shade. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid ibn Jabir except Sadaqah ibn Khalid; Hisham ibn Ammar alone transmitted it."
"6867","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azraq al-Antaki narrated to us, Sahl ibn Salih al-Antaki narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Nafi' and Ata, from Ibn Umar: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray in his sandals. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ubaydullah ibn Musa; Sahl ibn Salih alone transmitted it."
"6868","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Azraq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Idris al-Shafii narrated to us, Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, that Ibn Umar used to wipe over the leather socks and would command wiping over the leather socks, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded that. No one reported this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ma'mar, and no one from Ma'mar except Abd al-Razzaq; Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn Idris alone transmitted it."
"6869","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, with a gap in the chain, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When it is the middle of Sha'ban, no fasting except Ramadan. No one reported this hadith from al-Zubaydi except Baqiyyah."
"6870","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Mubashshir ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn Abi Hamzah, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among the signs of the Hour is the swelling of the crescents, until the crescent is seen for one night and it is said: It is two nights old. No one reported this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Shu'ayb; Mubashshir ibn Ismail alone transmitted it."
"6871","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Musafir al-Antaki narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nasr al-Antaki narrated to us, Salm ibn Salim narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Mus'ab, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah laughs at the despair and despondency of the servants, while His mercy is near to them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be ransomed for you, and does our Lord laugh? He said: Yes, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, He indeed laughs. No one reported this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Kharijah ibn Mus'ab; Muslim ibn Salim alone transmitted it."
"6872","Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn al-Yaman al-Jabali narrated to us at Jabalah, Yazdad ibn Jamil narrated to us, Rughayn ibn Isa narrated to us, Artah ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) invoked blessing upon three things: suhur, tharid, and measurement. No one reported this hadith from Dawud, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, except Artah, and no one from Artah except Rughayn; Yazdad alone transmitted it."
"6873","Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Jubayli narrated to us, Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Hamzah al-Nasibi, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever forgets to mention Allah at the beginning of his meal should mention the name of Allah at its end and recite: Say: He is Allah, the One. No one reported this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Hamzah al-Nasibi."
"6874","Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Jubayli narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-A'la al-Sulami narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A dirham spent with understanding is dearer to me than a hundred spent otherwise. No one reported this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abdullah except Abd al-Samad; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone transmitted it."
"6875","Muhammad ibn al-Harith al-Jubayli narrated to us, Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr and said: Will you not perform Hajj? She said: I am weak and unable. He said: Perform Hajj, and stipulate that my place of release is where You detained me."
"6876","And with the same chain: from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a slave is jointly owned by partners and one of them frees him, he is valued at the highest price, so he pays his price and the slave is freed. No two hadiths were reported from Amr ibn Shu'ayb except by al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah."
"6877","And with the same chain: from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father and Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not grant umra or ruqba; if you do, it belongs to the one granted the umra and the one granted the ruqba. I said: And how is that? He said: Umra is to say: It is yours for your lifetime; ruqba is to say: It belongs to whichever of us survives the other. No one reported this hadith from Said ibn al-Musayyib except Amr ibn Shu'ayb; al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah alone transmitted it."
"6878","And with the same chain: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, concerning the saying of Allah: And remember your Lord when you forget, he said: When you forget the exception, make the exception when you remember. He said: It is exclusive to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); none of us may make the exception except by joining it to the oath. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone transmitted it."
"6879","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Anbasah al-Bazzar al-Massisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Kathir al-Massisi narrated to us, al-Awzai narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at Abu Bakr and Umar and said: These two are the masters of the elderly people of Paradise. No one reported this hadith from al-Awzai except Muhammad ibn Kathir, and no one reported it from Qatadah except al-Awzai."
"6880","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Samad ibn Abi al-Jarrah al-Massisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Wazir al-Dimashqi narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Raja ibn Abi Salamah, from al-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade secret marriage. No one reported this hadith from al-Zuhri except Raja ibn Abi Salamah, and no one reported it from Raja except Damrah; Muhammad ibn al-Wazir alone transmitted it."
"6881","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi al-Tarsusi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Aishah who said: I would cover my lower part while menstruating, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fondle me. No one reported this hadith from Nafi' except al-Hajjaj, and no one reported it from al-Hajjaj except Amr ibn Abi Qays al-Razi; Harun ibn al-Mughirah alone transmitted it."
"6882","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Nu'aym ibn Maysarah al-Razi narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A red velvet cloth was placed in the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one reported this hadith from Yunus except Abu Jafar al-Razi, and no one from Abu Jafar except Nu'aym ibn Maysarah al-Razi; his son Abdullah ibn Nu'aym alone transmitted it."
"6883","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Said al-Qadi, from Abu Hamzah, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from Aishah who said: It is as though I am looking at the yellowness of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while in ihram, from the oil he applied at his ihram."
"6884","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn Said, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to sacrifice a ram. No one reported this hadith from al-Zubayr ibn Adi except Anbasah."
"6885","And with the same chain: Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I am pleased for my ummah with what the son of Umm Abd is pleased with for it. No one reported this hadith from Mansur except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"6886","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Atiyyah, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Each of you is a shepherd, and each of you is responsible for his flock. No one reported this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Abu Hafs al-Abbar; Yahya ibn Main alone transmitted it."
"6887","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, Abu Hafs al-Abbar narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to have his lifespan extended and his term deferred, let him fear Allah and uphold his kinship. No one reported this hadith from Mansur except Abu Hafs al-Abbar."
"6888","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from al-Zubayr ibn Adi, from Umayr ibn Said, that Ali gathered the people in al-Rahbah while I was present, and said: I adjure by Allah any man who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whomsoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla. So eighteen men stood and testified that they heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that. No one reported this hadith from al-Zubayr ibn Adi except Amr ibn Abi Qays."
"6889","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Mani' narrated to us, Abu al-Ahwas Muhammad ibn Hayyan narrated to us, Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, Ya'la ibn Ata narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Hadid, from Sakhr al-Ghamidi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bless my ummah in its early mornings. No one reported this hadith from Malik except Abu al-Ahwas; Ahmad ibn Mani' alone transmitted it."
"6890","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi al-Dunya al-Nasibi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One Who sent me with the truth, if the drop upon which Allah took the covenant were cast upon a rock, Allah would create a human being from it. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Abi al-Dunya; Muhammad ibn Mihran alone transmitted it."
"6891","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Bakr narrated to us, Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qays, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from Aishah who said: I would cover my lower part while menstruating, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would fondle me. No one reported this hadith from Nafi' except al-Hajjaj, and no one reported it from al-Hajjaj except Amr ibn Abi Qays and Hafs ibn Ghiyath."
"6892","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Zunayj Abu Ghassan narrated to us, Bahz ibn Asad narrated to us, Harun ibn Musa narrated to us, from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from miserliness. No one reported this hadith from Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab except Harun ibn Musa; Bahz ibn Asad alone transmitted it."
"6893","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Main and Ibrahim ibn Musa al-Farra narrated to us, both saying: Ibrahim ibn Khalid al-San'ani narrated to us, Rabah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken between my breast and my collarbone, and I had him leaning upon my chest. Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Bakr came with a siwak, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) beckoned to him, so he took the siwak from him and tried to use it but could not. So I took the siwak from him, softened it, then handed it to him, and he began brushing with it. Then his hand grew heavy, and I heard him saying: In the Highest Companionship. Then he was taken while I was unaware. No one reported this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ma'mar; Rabah ibn Zayd alone transmitted it."
"6894","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Razi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Mu'addib narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Isa ibn Musa al-Ghunjar, from Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from al-A'mash, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not call grapes karm. No one reported this hadith from al-A'mash except Abu Hamzah; al-Ghunjar alone transmitted it."
"6895","And with the same chain: from Abu Hamzah al-Sukkari, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you is invited, let him accept. No one reported this hadith from Raqabah except Abu Hamzah."
"6896","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Awn al-Nasai narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It suffices a man as evil that people point at him with fingers, in religion or worldly matters, except one whom Allah protects. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn; Ali ibn Hujr alone transmitted it."
"6897","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Awn narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid al-Hilali narrated to us, from Said ibn Abi Iyas al-Jurayri, from Abu al-Salil Durayb ibn Nuqayr, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I heard your supplication last night, and what reached me of it is that you say: O Allah, forgive me my sin, widen my dwelling for me, and bless for me in what You have provided me. He said: Do you see that they left anything out? No one reported this hadith from Said al-Jurayri except Abd al-Hamid al-Hilali; Ali ibn Hujr alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from Abu Hurayrah except through this chain."
"6898","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Ali ibn Hujr al-Marwazi narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about kalalah, and said: The summer verse suffices you. No one reported this hadith from al-Hajjaj except Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman."
"6899","Muhammad ibn al-Khuzz ibn Amr al-Tabarani narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Wasiti narrated to us, Yahya ibn Isa al-Ramli narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: (gap in the printed text) and al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me there shall be matters and favoritism. They said: What do you command, O Messenger of Allah, one who lives to see that? He said: You shall render the duty incumbent upon you, and ask Allah for what is yours. No one reported this hadith from al-A'mash, from Abu Hazim, except Yahya ibn Isa; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Aziz alone transmitted it. The hadith of Zayd ibn Wahb is with al-Thawri and the people."
"6900","Muhammad ibn al-Khuzz al-Tabarani narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Walid ibn Salamah al-Tabarani narrated to us, my father al-Walid narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Hearts develop rust. They said: And what polishes them, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Their polish is seeking forgiveness. No one reported this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except al-Nadr ibn Muhammad; al-Walid ibn Salamah alone transmitted it."
"6901","Muhammad ibn al-Khuzz ibn Amr narrated to us, Salih ibn Bishr al-Tabarani narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdullah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah sent me with the perfection of noble character and the completion of excellent deeds. No one reported this hadith from Yusuf ibn Muhammad except Umar ibn Ibrahim; Salih ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"6902","Muhammad ibn al-Khuzz ibn Amr narrated to us, Salih ibn Bishr narrated to us, Umar ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated to us, Miswar ibn al-Salt narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whatever a man spends upon himself, his child, his family, his kin and relatives is charity for him. No one reported this hadith in this complete wording from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Miswar ibn al-Salt, and no one from Miswar except Umar ibn Ibrahim; Salih ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"6903","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam al-Bayruti, Mak'hul, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah ibn Yazid al-Qurduwani al-Harrani narrated to us, my father reported to me, Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Mak'hul, from Raja ibn Haywah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept charity from misappropriated spoils, nor prayer without purification. No one reported this hadith from Mak'hul except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud; Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah ibn Yazid alone transmitted it, from his father."
"6904","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam al-Bayruti narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ayshun al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, my father reported to me, from Mak'hul, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The dust in the path of Allah and the smoke of Hell shall never combine in the belly of a Muslim man. No one reported this hadith from Mak'hul except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud; his son alone transmitted it from him."
"6905","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki narrated to us, Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade every beast with fangs and every bird with talons. No one reported this hadith from Sufyan except Abu al-Jawwab; Muhammad ibn Ghalib alone transmitted it."
"6906","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki narrated to us, Ghusn ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from his father, from Mak'hul, from Kurayb, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you doubt in your prayer, let the doubt be whether it is the fifth or the fourth. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Ghusn ibn Ismail; Muhammad ibn Ghalib al-Antaki alone transmitted it."
"6907","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam al-Bayruti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ghalib narrated to us, Ghusn ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Ibn Thawban, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the expedition of Tabuk, and he would combine Zuhr and Asr, praying Zuhr at the end of its time and Asr at the beginning of its time; then he would travel and pray Maghrib at the end of its time so long as the twilight had not disappeared, and pray Isha at the beginning of its time when the twilight disappeared. Then he said when we drew near: Tomorrow, Allah willing, we shall alight at Tabuk; let none of you precede us to the water. Mu'adh said: I was the first to precede to the water, and two men had already reached the water, drawing in two skins with them and muddying the water. I said: After the prohibition of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did you precede and draw water? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: Did I not forbid you that any of you should precede us to the water? So he called for the two skins and they were emptied into the water; he performed ablution, rinsed his mouth in the water, and supplicated to Allah, and the water flowed abundantly. He said: O Mu'adh, if your life is prolonged you shall see what is here filled with gardens. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Thawban except Ghusn ibn Ismail; Muhammad ibn Ghalib alone transmitted it."
"6908","Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Said al-Massisi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Himyar narrated to us, from Khalid ibn Humayd al-Mahri, from Khayr ibn Nu'aym, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A gift to the ruler is misappropriation. No one reported this hadith from Khayr ibn Nu'aym except Khalid ibn Humayd; Muhammad ibn Himyar alone transmitted it."
"6909","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abd al-Salam al-Bayruti narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Said al-Massisi narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Minhal ibn Khalifah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays who said: Abu Rimthah led us in prayer; he said: I witnessed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray, then give salam to his right and to his left until we saw the brightness of his cheeks. This hadith is not reported from Abu Rimthah except through this chain; Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah alone transmitted it."
"6910","Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, al-Yaman ibn Said narrated to us, Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah narrated to us, Warqa narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la al-Tha'labi, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, concerning His saying: Say: I ask of you no reward except love for kinship, he said: There was no clan among the clans of Quraysh but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had close kinship among them, so he said to him: Say: I ask of you no reward except that you love me for my kinship among you. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-A'la except Warqa; Ash'ath ibn Shu'bah alone transmitted it."
"6911","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Abi Hanzalah al-Saydawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sadaqah al-Jublani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Said, raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: In this ummah there shall be collapse of the earth, pelting, and transformation, among those who take singing girls, wear silk, and drink wines. No one reported this hadith from Ziyad al-Jassas except Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Wahbi; Muhammad ibn Sadaqah alone transmitted it."
"6912","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'afa ibn Abi Hanzalah narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said al-Saydawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman ibn Abi al-Jawn narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Salih al-Madani, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah is Beautiful and loves beauty, loves lofty matters, and dislikes trivial ones. No one reported this hadith from Muhammad ibn Salih al-Tammar except Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman."
"6913","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'afa narrated to us, Uthman ibn Said al-Saydawi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb ibn Shabur narrated to us, Isa ibn Abdullah narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Mak'hul, from Wathilah ibn al-Asqa' who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man should not wipe his forehead of dust until he finishes prayer, but there is no harm in wiping sweat from his temples. No one reported this hadith from Mak'hul except Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman; Muhammad ibn Shu'ayb alone transmitted it, from Isa ibn Abdullah."
"6914","Muhammad ibn al-Mu'afa narrated to us, Zakariyya ibn Yahya al-Waqar narrated to us, saying: It was read to Abdullah ibn Wahb while I listened: al-Thawri said: Mujalid said: Abu al-Waddak said: Abu Said al-Khudri said: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My brother Musa (peace be upon him) said: O Lord, show me the one You showed me in the ship. So Allah revealed to him: O Musa, you shall see him. Only a short while passed until al-Khidr came to him, sweet-smelling, with bright white garments, and said: Peace be upon you, O Musa son of Imran; your Lord conveys to you peace and the mercy of Allah. Musa said: He is Peace, and from Him is peace, and to Him is peace; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds, Whose blessings I cannot enumerate nor thank except by His aid. Then Musa said: I wish you would counsel me with counsel by which Allah will benefit me after you. Al-Khidr said: O seeker of knowledge, the speaker tires less than the listener, so do not bore your companions when you address them; know that your heart is a vessel, so see what you fill your vessel with; turn away from the world and cast it behind you, for it is not your abode nor your place of residence, but was made as provision for servants to take provision from it for the Return. O Musa, accustom yourself to patience and you shall receive wisdom; clothe your heart with piety and you shall attain knowledge; train yourself in patience and you shall be freed from sin. O Musa, devote yourself to knowledge if you seek it, for knowledge belongs to one who devotes himself to it; do not be excessive in speech and babbling, for much speech disgraces scholars and reveals the faults of fools, but adhere to moderation, for that is of success and rectitude. Turn away from the ignorant and forbear the foolish, for that is the merit of the wise and the adornment of scholars. If the ignorant reviles you, remain silent toward him in peace and avoid him prudently, for what remains of his ignorance against you and his reviling of you is greater and graver. O son of Imran, do you not see that you have been given but little of knowledge; over-eagerness and rashness stem from venturing and affectation. O son of Imran, do not open a door whose closing you do not know, nor close a door whose opening you do not know. O son of Imran, one whose craving for the world never ends and whose desire for it never ceases, how can he be a worshipper? One who belittles his state and accuses Allah of what He decreed for him, how can he be ascetic? Shall one restrain his desires when his caprice has overcome him, and shall knowledge benefit him when ignorance has encompassed him? For his journey is to his Hereafter while he advances toward his world. O Musa, learn what you learn in order to act upon it, and do not learn it to be talked about, lest its ruin be upon you and its light for others. O Musa son of Imran, make asceticism and piety your garment, knowledge and remembrance your speech, increase in good deeds, for you will commit misdeeds; shake your heart with fear, for that pleases your Lord; do good, for you must do other than it. You have been admonished, if you preserve it. Then al-Khidr departed, and Musa remained sorrowful and distressed."
"6915","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Taraifi al-Raqqi narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Said ibn Maslamah al-Umawi narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Tariq, from Abu Hazim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: My ummah is a ummah shown mercy; punishment has been lifted from them, except their own punishment by their own hands. No one reported this hadith from Sa'd ibn Tariq except Said ibn Maslamah."
"6916","Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun narrated to us, Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mughith, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: After me there shall be leaders who dispense wisdom upon their pulpits, but when they descend it is stripped from them; their hearts and bodies are worse than carrion. No one reported this hadith from Mughith, who is Ibn Sumayy, except Layth; Said ibn Maslamah alone transmitted it."
"6917","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Massisi narrated to us, from Mughirah ibn Abi Mughirah al-Ramli, from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Barirah, the freedwoman of Aishah, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applying ithmid while fasting. No one reported this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except Mughirah ibn Abi Mughirah, and no one from Mughirah except Muhammad ibn Mihran; Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from Barirah except through this chain."
"6918","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Umar ibn Rashid ibn Abi al-Uyun narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Mansur ibn Said, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off the hands and branded the eyes of those who drove away the grazing camels of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah. No one reported this hadith from Mansur ibn Said except Jafar ibn Burqan; Umar ibn Rashid ibn Abi al-Uyun alone transmitted it."
"6919","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Fuhayr Yahya ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no vow in disobedience. No one reported this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Fuhayr; Ayyub al-Wazzan alone transmitted it."
"6920","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sabur al-Raqqi narrated to us, Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Hazim, from Sahl ibn Sa'd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a rolling place of musk like the rolling places of your beasts in this world. No one reported this hadith from Abu Hazim except Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman; Muhammad ibn Sabur alone transmitted it."
"6921","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Adam al-Massisi narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Aishah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is gentle with my ummah, be gentle with him; whoever causes them hardship, cause him hardship. No one reported this hadith from Sufyan except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"6922","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Kalbi al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Nasibi wrote to me, mentioning that Abd al-Aziz ibn Suhayb reported to him, from Khabbab, the freedman of al-Zubayr, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, when we rise from your presence we fall into the talk of Jahiliyyah. He said: When you sit in those sittings in which you fear for yourselves, say upon rising: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; there is no god but You; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You; what you committed therein shall be expiated for you. This hadith is not reported from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam except through this chain; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Kalbi alone transmitted it."
"6923","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Ali ibn Maymun al-Raqqi narrated to us, Said ibn Maslamah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married Maymunah while in ihram. No one reported this hadith from Said ibn al-Musayyib except Ismail ibn Umayyah; Said ibn Maslamah alone transmitted it."
"6924","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Ruzayq ibn al-Ward narrated to us, Salm al-Khawwas narrated to us, Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Sahl ibn Abi Hathmah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: When I die, and Abu Bakr, and Umar, if you are able to die, then die. No one reported this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar; Salm al-Khawwas alone transmitted it."
"6925","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Manbiji narrated to us, Abu Nu'aym narrated to us, Talhah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you look at his shadow in the water. No one reported this hadith from Talhah except Abu Nu'aym; Muhammad ibn Sallam alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"6926","Muhammad ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Hunayni narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer is not stung from the same hole twice. No one reported this hadith from Kathir ibn Abdullah except Ishaq al-Hunayni."
"6927","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahim ibn Kardam narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Aishah, a house with no dates in it, its people are hungry. No one reported this hadith from al-Zuhri except Abd al-Rahim ibn Kardam; Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi alone transmitted it."
"6928","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Khalid ibn Ismail al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Yusuf ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Adhere to contentment, for contentment is wealth that never depletes. No one reported this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except his son Yusuf, and no one from Yusuf except Khalid ibn Ismail; Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani alone transmitted it, and it is not reported from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except through this chain."
"6929","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Walid al-Harrani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from his father, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have been commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah; when they say it, their blood and wealth are protected from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud; Muhammad ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"6930","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Makhlad ibn Yazid narrated to us, Mis'ar narrated to us, from Jabalah ibn Suhaym, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: As for me, I do not eat reclining. None introduced Jabalah ibn Suhaym between Mis'ar and Ali ibn al-Aqmar in this hadith except Makhlad ibn Yazid."
"6931","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib al-Taraifi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam al-Manbiji narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Azwar, from Hisham al-Qurdusi, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Brevity in prayer is the rest of the people of the Fire. No one reported this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Abdullah ibn al-Azwar; Isa ibn Yunus alone transmitted it."
"6932","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sallam narrated to us, Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Urayf ibn Dirham, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Juhayfah, from Ali who said: The best of this ummah after its Prophet is Abu Bakr, then Umar. No one reported this hadith from Urayf ibn Dirham except Isa ibn Yunus."
"6933","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Ali ibn Jamil al-Raqqi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and two witnesses. No one reported this hadith from Jafar ibn Burqan, from Hisham ibn Urwah, except al-Husayn ibn Ayyash; Ali ibn Jamil alone transmitted it."
"6934","Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan narrated to us, Ma'mar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Furat ibn Sulayman, from al-Zuhri, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the grandmother one-sixth. No one reported this hadith from Furat ibn Sulayman except Ma'mar ibn Sulayman."
"6935","Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Saydalani narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Idris al-Kufi, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ablution except from sound or wind. None among those who reported this hadith from Shu'bah introduced Idris between Shu'bah and Suhayl except Yahya ibn al-Sakan."
"6936","Muhammad ibn Suhayl ibn al-Muhajir al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from Sulayman ibn Buraydah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr. No one reported this hadith from Sufyan except Mu'ammal ibn Ismail."
"6937","Muhammad ibn Suhayl ibn Hammad ibn al-Muhajir al-Raqqi narrated to us, Mu'ammal ibn Ismail narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his brother, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever remembers Allah abundantly is absolved of hypocrisy. No one reported this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Mu'ammal ibn Ismail."
"6938","Muhammad ibn al-Bustanban narrated to us at Surra man ra'a: al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, Sa'dan ibn al-Walid, the seller of sabiri cloth, narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jafar ibn Abi Talib passed with Jibril and Mikail; he has two wings with which Allah compensated him for his hands, so he greeted, then informed me how his affair was when he met the polytheists; for that he was called the Flyer in Paradise."
"6939","And with the same chain: from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is put in charge of ten and judges among them by what they love or hate, he shall be brought on the Day of Resurrection with his hand bound to his neck; if he judged by other than what Allah revealed, a shackle is added to his shackle; if he judged by what Allah revealed, did not deviate in judgment, and did not take bribes therein, his right hand shall be released. One of Ata's companions said: O Abu Muhammad, must there be a shackle? He said: Yes, by the Lord of this Structure, pointing to the Ka'bah."
"6940","And with the same chain: from Ibn Abbas who said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, and he was hungry. She said to him: O Messenger of Allah, I have in-laws who sought refuge with me, and Ali ibn Abi Talib is not deterred by any blame in the cause of Allah, and I fear that if he learns of them he will kill them; so grant security to whoever enters my house until they hear the speech of Allah. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted them security. Then he said: Do you have any food for me to eat? She said: I have only stale crumbs, and I am shy to present them to you. He said: Bring them. So she brought them, and brought him salt. He said: O Umm Hani, is there any condiment? She said: I have nothing but some vinegar. He said: Bring it. When she brought it he touched it to his food, then ate from it, then praised Allah, then said: What an excellent condiment is vinegar; O Umm Hani, no house with vinegar in it shall be poor."
"6941","And with the same chain: from Ibn Abbas who said: When Fatimah, the mother of Ali ibn Abi Talib, died, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) removed his shirt and clothed her in it, and lay with her in her grave. When the dust was leveled over her, some of them said: O Messenger of Allah, we saw you do something you never did for anyone. He said: I clothed her in my shirt that she may be clothed with garments of Paradise, and I lay with her in her grave that the constriction of the grave may be lightened for her; she was the kindest of Allah's creation to me in deed after Abu Talib."
"6942","And with the same chain: from Ibn Abbas who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was seated with Asma bint Umays near him, he returned the greeting of salam, then said: O Asma, this is Jafar ibn Abi Talib with Jibril and Mikail, upon them be peace; they passed and greeted us, and I returned the greeting upon them. He informed me that he met the polytheists on such-and-such day, and I was struck on the front of my body with seventy-three wounds between thrust and blow; then I took the banner in my right hand and it was cut off, then I took it in my left hand and it was cut off, so Allah compensated me for my hands with two wings with which I fly with Jibril and Mikail in Paradise, descending wherever I wish and eating of its fruits whatever I wish. Asma said: Glad tidings to Jafar for what Allah has granted him of good, but I fear the people will not believe me; so ascend the pulpit and inform the people, O Messenger of Allah. So he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: O people, Jafar ibn Abi Talib passed with Jibril and Mikail; he has two wings with which Allah compensated him for his hands, with which he flies in Paradise wherever he wishes, and he greeted me. And he informed them how his affair was when he met the polytheists, so it became clear to the people after that day that Jafar had met them, and he was called Jafar the Flyer in Paradise."
"6943","And with the same chain: from Ibn Abbas who said: One day the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with Jibril (peace be upon him) upon al-Safa, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: O Jibril, by the One Who sent you with the truth, no handful of flour nor cup of sawiq remained by evening for the family of Muhammad. His speech was no sooner finished than he heard a crash from the sky that startled him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Has Allah commanded the Hour to rise? He said: No, but Allah commanded Israfil, who descended to you when he heard your speech. So Israfil came to him and said: Allah heard what you mentioned, and sent me to you with the keys of the treasuries of the earth, commanding me to present them to you: if you wish that I make the mountains of Tihamah move with you as emerald, ruby, gold and silver, I shall do so; if you wish a prophet-king, and if you wish a prophet-servant? Jibril signaled to him to be humble, so he said: Rather a prophet-servant, three times. None reported these hadiths from Ata except Sa'dan ibn al-Walid; al-Hasan ibn Bishr alone transmitted them."
"6944","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid Abu Ali al-Hanafi narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Some people of my ummah shall come after me; one of them would wish to purchase the sight of me with his family and wealth. No one reported this hadith from Amr ibn Abi Amr except Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"6945","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Jarrah al-Adhani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Azdi narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Umm Salamah: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was shrouded in three garments. No one reported this hadith from Shu'bah except Muhammad ibn al-Qasim."
"6946","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn al-Faraj al-Riyashi narrated to us, Zufar ibn Hubayrah narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah who said: I never saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) honor anyone as he honored al-Abbas. No one reported this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Ibn Abi al-Zinad."
"6947","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Uthman narrated to us, saying: I found in the book of my father and my uncle, from my grandfather, from Shu'bah, from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn Ar'arah, from Ali, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Tranquility is a swift wind. No one reported this hadith from Shu'bah except Uthman ibn Jabalah; his son alone transmitted it from him."
"6948","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, saying: I found in the book of my father and my uncle, from my grandfather, from Shu'bah, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and prayer is established, begin with supper. No one reported this hadith from Shu'bah except Uthman ibn Jabalah; his son alone transmitted it from him."
"6949","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Marzuq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah al-Ansari narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Thumamah, from Anas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A report is not like eyewitnessing. This hadith is not reported from Anas except through this chain; Muhammad ibn Marzuq alone transmitted it."
"6950","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abdan ibn Uthman narrated to us, my father informed me, from Shu'bah, from Muhammad and Yahya, from Amrah, from Aishah who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeing it as nothing but Hajj. No one reported this hadith from Shu'bah except Abdullah ibn Uthman; Abdan alone transmitted it. Muhammad is Ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Sa'd ibn Zurarah, and Yahya is Ibn Said."
"6951","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Abdi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father reported to me, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Mujahid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ka'b ibn Ujrah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him with lice from his head falling upon his face, and said: Do your lice trouble you? He said: Yes. He said: Then shave your head, and sacrifice a sheep, or fast three days, or feed six poor persons. No one reported this hadith from Qays ibn Sa'd except Jarir ibn Hazim; Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6952","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Abdi narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Adi narrated to us, from Mis'ar ibn Kidam, from Adi ibn Thabit, from al-Bara ibn Azib, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the Ansar: None loves them but a believer, and none hates them but a hypocrite; whoever loves them, Allah loves him, and whoever hates them, Allah hates him. No one reported this hadith from Mis'ar except al-Haytham ibn Adi; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim alone transmitted it."
"6953","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayyah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Bakrah, that he entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was bowing, so he bowed before reaching the row. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: O Abu Bakrah, may Allah increase you in eagerness, but do not repeat it. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Abu Hamzah; Ali ibn al-Hasan alone transmitted it."
"6954","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, Abu Hamzah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A Bedouin man died with no agnatic relatives, but he had a freedman whom he had manumitted, so the matter was raised to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Would he not anger at his anger and be pleased at his pleasure? They said: Yes indeed. So he gave him the inheritance of the wealth of his freedman. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Abu Hamzah; Ali ibn al-Hasan alone transmitted it."
"6955","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Abdi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Qays ibn Sa'd, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn al-Arqam who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When one of you needs to relieve himself and prayer arrives, let him begin with relieving himself. No one reported this hadith from Qays ibn Sa'd except Jarir ibn Hazim, and no one from Jarir except his son Wahb; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim alone transmitted it."
"6956","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, Kharijah ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Sa'd, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather: that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It costs none of you, when he wishes to give charity, to make it on behalf of his parents, without anything diminished from their rewards. No one reported this hadith from Uthman ibn Sa'd except Kharijah ibn Mus'ab, and no one from Kharijah except Ali ibn al-Hasan; Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh alone transmitted it."
"6957","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Abu al-Wazir Muhammad ibn A'yan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he prayed Fajr on a journey would walk. No one reported this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Sulayman ibn Bilal, and no one from Sulayman except Ibn al-Mubarak, and no one from Ibn al-Mubarak except Muhammad ibn A'yan; Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh alone transmitted it."
"6958","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Khalaf ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Uthman ibn Jabalah ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from my grandfather, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Nadrah, from his father, from Abu Said al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Has your Haruri liar not come to you with it; how often we heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention him, meaning the Dajjal. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Nadrah except Uthman ibn Jabalah; his son alone transmitted it from him."
"6959","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Sayyar al-Marwazi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Kashghari al-Marwazi narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar al-Saigh narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Jabir, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade dubba vessels, naqir, and muzaffat. No one reported this hadith from Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar except Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Kashghari; Ahmad ibn Sayyar alone transmitted it."
"6960","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Kashghari narrated to us, Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar al-Saigh narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Sabii narrated to us, Sulayman al-A'mash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdullah who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey, and water ran short, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called for a vessel and placed his hand in it, and I saw the water gushing forth from between the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one reported this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Abd al-Kabir ibn Dinar; Yahya ibn Ishaq al-Kashghari alone transmitted it."
"6961","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah ibn Yazid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Saj, from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from Sumayy, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Umrah to Umrah is expiation for what is between them, and the accepted Hajj has no reward except Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah ibn Said ibn Abi Hind except al-Walid ibn Amr ibn Saj; Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Harrani alone narrated it from his father."
"6962","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Hurayth narrated to me: Ishaq ibn Mansur al-Kawsaj narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) picked up meat from a shoulder blade, then prayed and did not perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind except Abd al-Warith, nor from Abd al-Warith except Abd al-Samad, nor from Abd al-Samad except Ishaq ibn Mansur; Abu Bakr ibn Hurayth alone narrated it."
"6963","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim al-Abdi narrated to us: Bakr ibn Yunus narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr who said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me when I was six years old, and I was taken to his house when I was nine years old, and I stayed with him nine years; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when I was eighteen years old."
"6964","And with the same chain: from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and left nothing in my house except a small measure of barley; I ate from it until I grew tired of it, then I measured it and it ran out — would that I had not measured it."
"6965","And with the same chain: from Urwah who said: Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me in Shawwal and consummated the marriage with me in Shawwal, so which of his wives was more fortunate with her husband than I? No one narrated these hadiths from Abi al-Zinad except his son, nor from his son except Bakr ibn Yunus; Muhammad ibn Abd al-Karim alone narrated them."
"6966","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Sad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to me: my father narrated to me: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to use the siwak so much that I feared for my teeth. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"6967","And with the same chain: my father al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: If man had two valleys of wealth he would seek a third, and nothing fills the belly of man except dust; then Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except al-Husayn ibn Waqid; his son alone narrated it from him."
"6968","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Sulayman narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Iyad ibn Abd Allah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Faith has seventy-odd branches, the highest of which is: there is no god but Allah, and the lowest of which is removing harm from the path."
"6969","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Khalaf ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Uthman ibn Jabalah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather: Ali ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, that al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh ibn Afra informed him that Thabit ibn Qays ibn Shammas struck his wife and broke her hand — she was Jamilah bint Abd Allah ibn Ubayy ibn Salul — so her brother came complaining to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent for Thabit ibn Qays and said: Take what she owes you and release her. He said: Yes. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered her to wait one menstrual period and join her family."
"6970","And with the same chain: from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir: Abu Qilabah narrated to me that Abu Idris al-Khawlani informed him that Amr ibn Abasah informed him that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which part of the night is best for supplication? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The last part of the night. Then he said: Pray as you wish until you pray the dawn prayer, then refrain until the sun rises, for it rises between the two horns of Satan and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it. Then pray as you wish until midday, then refrain, for Hell is kindled at that time; when the shadow turns, pray as you wish until you pray Asr, then refrain, for the sun sets between the two horns of Satan and at that time the disbelievers prostrate to it. He said: And I asked him about purification, and he said: When you rinse your mouth you expel its sins, when you wash your hands you wash away the sins of your hands, nails and fingertips, when you wash your feet you wash away your sins from the soles of your feet, and when you pray and turn to Allah with your heart it is an expiation; and if you sit, your reward becomes due. No one narrated these two hadiths from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Ali ibn al-Mubarak; Uthman ibn Jabalah ibn Abi Rawwad alone narrated them."
"6971","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abu Farwah Yazid ibn Muhammad ibn Yazid ibn Sinan al-Ruhawi narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from al-Awzai, that Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to him, that al-Hasan al-Basri narrated to him: a son of Abu Thalabah al-Khushani narrated to me, from his father who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying, he heard a man supplicating: Praise be to Allah, abundant, good and blessed praise, as befits the nobility of our Lord's countenance and the might of His majesty. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) finished, he said: Which of you said such-and-such? I saw twelve angels racing to take it up. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) lifted his gaze until it was veiled from him. He said: It is yours with its seal on the Day of Resurrection, and the like thereof. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Yazid ibn Sinan; his son alone narrated it from him."
"6972","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Kathir al-Harrani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Yazid ibn Mardanbah narrated to us, from Raqabah ibn Masqalah, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It is as if I am looking at the glitter of the ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came out to us in the last third of the night and said: The people have prayed and slept, and you remain in prayer as long as you wait for it."
"6973","And with the same chain: from Anas ibn Malik who said: I never saw a lighter prayer than that of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), complete in bowing and prostration. No one narrated these two hadiths from Raqabah except Ibrahim ibn Yazid; Muhammad ibn Musa ibn Ayan alone narrated them."
"6974","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Amr al-Usfuri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Muadh Abu Muadh narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Amir ibn Rabiah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The injury caused by a stray beast is not compensated, the well is not compensated, the mine is not compensated, and on buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah except Muadh Abu Bakr; his son alone narrated it from him."
"6975","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Sahl ibn Ammar al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Razin narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah: Musa ibn Talhah narrated to me that he presented himself to Umar ibn al-Khattab while he was serving food to the people, and a man passed by him — or greeted him — and Umar said to him: Come. He said: I am fasting. He said: Which month do you fast? He said: The beginning, middle and end of every month. Umar said: Call Abd Allah ibn Masud and Ubayy ibn Kab for me, and he named men among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they came. He said: Do you remember the day the man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a rabbit in such-and-such valley on such-and-such day? They said: Yes. Umar said: Then tell the man. So they began telling the man. They said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such-and-such valley on such-and-such day, when a shepherd brought him a roasted rabbit as a gift. The shepherd said: I saw blood on it. So he ordered the people to eat but did not eat himself, and said to the shepherd: Sit and eat with them. He said: I am fasting. He said: How do you fast? He said: I fast three days of every month. He said: Which three do you fast? He said: The middle of it and the end, and so on. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fast the white days. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Sufyan ibn Husayn; Umar ibn Abd Allah ibn Razin alone narrated it."
"6976","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Hatim ibn Yusuf al-Jallab narrated to us: Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, from Abd Allah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: Vile matters spread in Kufa, so the reciters of Kufa gathered and went out to Umar. Umar said: What have I done that the reciters of Kufa march to me? Abd Allah ibn Amr said: Vile matters have spread among them. He said: I adjure you by Allah, O Abd Allah ibn Amr, do you obey Allah in what you were commanded regarding your hearing? He said: No. He said: And regarding your sight? He said: No. He said: Then how shall I establish the affair of the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upon what you yourself cannot uphold regarding your hearing and sight? We only require of people what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: there is no god but Allah, establish prayer and give zakat; if they do that, they protect their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Abd Allah ibn Amr, from Umar, except with this chain; Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"6977","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Layth Abu al-Sabbah al-Haddadi narrated to us: Abu Nuaym al-Fadl ibn Dukayn narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Jami ibn Abi Rashid, from Abi al-Zubayr, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered on the day of the conquest of Mecca wearing a black turban. No one narrated this hadith from Jami ibn Abi Rashid except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Abu Nuaym; Muhammad ibn al-Layth alone narrated it."
"6978","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah narrated to us, from Bashir ibn Salman, from Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Mujalid, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Umar who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoining the neighbor until we thought he would make him an heir. No one inserted Abd Allah ibn Abi al-Mujalid between Bashir ibn Salman and Mujahid in this hadith except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rizmah."
"6979","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Mutahhar ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father: Matar al-Warraq narrated to me, from Umm al-Saib, that she entered upon Aishah, Mother of the Believers, with a stick with which she followed geckos and killed them. I said: O Mother of the Believers, what is the matter with this gecko? She said: When Ibrahim was thrown into the fire, everything repelled it except this, so we were ordered to kill it. I said: O Mother of the Believers, may a woman enter the bathhouse? She said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any woman who removes her clothes outside her husband's house has torn the veil between her and her Lord."
"6980","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Mutahhar ibn al-Hakam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, from Matar: al-Hasan narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, regarding His saying: Indeed We granted you a clear victory — that it was revealed to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from Hudaybiyah, while his Companions were overcome with grief and gloom, barred from their rites, having sacrificed the sacrificial animals at Hudaybiyah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A verse has been revealed to me that is dearer to me than the whole world. He recited it to them to its end. A man among the people said: Congratulations to you, O Messenger of Allah, from Allah for what He will do for you — but what will He do for us? So Allah revealed on that day: That He may admit the believing men and believing women into gardens beneath which rivers flow, to the end of the verse."
"6981","And with the same chain: from Matar al-Warraq, from Abd Allah ibn Babah who said: While I was circumambulating the House with Abd Allah ibn Umar, a man confronted him and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say about the private converse? He said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, Allah calls His servant and places His covering over him, saying to him: Did you not do on such-and-such day such-and-such sin? The servant says: Yes, my Lord. He says: I concealed it for you in the world, and I forgive it for you today. No one narrated these hadiths from Matar al-Warraq except al-Husayn ibn Waqid."
"6982","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Said ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Khilas ibn Amr, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My close friend (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me three things I never abandon, in travel or at home: sleeping upon witr, fasting three days of every month, and two rakahs after Friday prayer. Then Abu Hurayrah later made, in place of two rakahs after Friday, the two rakahs of Duha. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah, from Khilas, except Said ibn Abi Arubah, nor from Said except Abd al-Wahhab; Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh alone narrated it."
"6983","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from al-Zuhri, from al-Rabi ibn Sabrah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage with women. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"6984","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kept reciting talbiyah in Umrah until he touched the Black Stone. Ibrahim ibn Tahman said: And Ayyub ibn Musa narrated to me, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, the same. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Hafs ibn Abd Allah alone narrated it."
"6985","And with the same chain: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you goes to Friday prayer, let him bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"6986","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Salamah ibn Sulaym narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Umar ibn Salamah ibn Abi Mazyad al-Madini narrated to us, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution in a basin, so I took it and poured it into a well of ours. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain; Ibn al-Mubarak alone narrated it."
"6987","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade, on the day of Hunayn, selling spoils before they are divided, and having intercourse with pregnant captives until they deliver what is in their wombs, and said: Would you irrigate another man's crop? And he forbade the meat of domestic donkeys and the meat of every fanged beast of prey. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb except Yahya ibn Said, nor from Yahya except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Hafs ibn Abd Allah alone narrated it."
"6988","And with the same chain: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from al-Walid ibn Zarwan, from Maymun ibn Mihran, from Yazid ibn al-Asamm, from Maymunah, that she informed him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married her while in the lawful state, consummated the marriage with her while in the lawful state, and married her at Sarif."
"6989","And with the same chain: Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Abi al-Khalil, from Abd Allah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr who said: We were discussing, while with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), which is better: the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) or Bayt al-Maqdis? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than four prayers therein, yet what an excellent place of prayer it is; and it will soon be that a man having land the size of his bowstring from which he can see Bayt al-Maqdis will be better for him than the whole world. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except al-Hajjaj and Said ibn Bashir; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it from al-Hajjaj. And Ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud alone narrated it from Said."
"6990","And with the same chain: Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid, from al-Hasan, from Sasaaah ibn Muawiyah, from Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim spends two pairs of his wealth in the path of Allah except that the keepers of Paradise call him: Come, this is good. No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Abd al-Wahid except al-Hajjaj; Ibrahim ibn Tahman alone narrated it."
"6991","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Munayyib Abu al-Darda al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah ibn Kaysan narrated to us, from his father, from Ikrimah who said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah was named Abd Kallub, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named him Abd al-Rahman. He passed by him while he was performing ablution and said: Come, O Abd al-Rahman. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do not seek positions of authority, for if you seek them and are given them you will be left to them, but if you do not seek them you will be helped in them. No one narrated this hadith from Ikrimah except Abd Allah ibn Kaysan, nor did anyone narrate it from Abd Allah except his son Ishaq; Abu al-Darda alone narrated it."
"6992","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Abd Allah al-Khushk narrated to us: Hafs ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Hakim ibn Abbad ibn Hunayf, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Report is not like eyewitness. No one narrated this hadith from Hakim ibn Hakim except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad except Hafs ibn Abd al-Rahman; Ishaq ibn al-Khushk alone narrated it."
"6993","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Shuayb al-Naysaburi narrated to us: Husayn ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Usamah, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man who swears an oath about something, then regrets it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears an oath, then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and expiate for his oath. This hadith is not narrated from Muawiyah ibn al-Hakam except with this chain; Husayn ibn al-Walid alone narrated it."
"6994","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Quhzadh narrated to us: Hatim ibn Yusuf narrated to us: Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Buraydah narrating from Yahya ibn Yamar, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said in his sermon: I am about to be called and I will answer; after me, officials will rule you who do what you know and do what you recognize, and obedience to them is obedience. You will remain so for a time, then after them officials will rule you who do what you do not know and do what you do not recognize. Whoever flatters them and advises them falsely, those have perished and caused ruin. Mix with them in body but separate from them in deeds, and testify that the good-doer is good and the evil-doer is evil. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Yamar except Abd Allah ibn Buraydah, nor did anyone narrate it from Abd Allah except Abd al-Mumin ibn Khalid; Hatim ibn Yusuf alone narrated it."
"6995","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ubayd Allah al-Qarduwani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim, from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam, from Hammad, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Abi Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr Abu Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr at the beginning of the night, in its middle, and at its end, so that the Muslims would follow his example; whichever of that is acted upon is correct, Allah willing. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Abi Maryam except Abd al-Karim; Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud alone narrated it."
"6996","And with the same chain: from Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud, from Abd al-Karim, from Ziyad ibn Said, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Abi Abd Allah al-Jadali, from Uqbah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would perform witr at the beginning of the night, in its middle, and at its end. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Said except Abd al-Karim; Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud alone narrated it."
"6997","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn Khashram narrated to us: al-Fadl ibn Musa narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad ibn Abi al-Jad, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Samurah ibn Jundub who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not name anyone Aflah, nor Najih, nor Yasar, and do not add upon me. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ziyad except al-Fadl ibn Musa."
"6998","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Umayr al-Yafuni narrated to us: Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Murashshal narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Hayyan Abu Khalid al-Ahmar narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Sawwar, from Abi Bishr, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina while the Jews were fasting Ashura. He asked them, and they said: This is a day on which Musa prevailed over Pharaoh. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have more right to Musa, so fast it. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath ibn Sawwar except Abu Khalid al-Ahmar; Yazid ibn Khalid ibn Murashshal alone narrated it."
"6999","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Ibrahim ibn Umayr al-Yafuni narrated to us: Imran ibn Harun al-Ramli narrated to us: Ayyub ibn Suwayd narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Suraqah ibn Malik ibn Jushum who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and said: The best of you is the one who defends his clan, so long as he does not sin."
"7000","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Umayr narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah gave me the choice between forgiveness for half my ummah or my intercession, so I chose my intercession, hoping it would be more comprehensive for my ummah. Were it not for what the righteous servant beat me to, I would have hastened my supplication. When Allah relieved Ishaq of the distress of sacrifice, it was said to him: O Ishaq, ask and you shall be given. He said: By Allah, I shall hasten it before the whisperings of Satan: O Allah, whoever dies not associating anything with You and does good, forgive him and admit him to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abd al-Rahman; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone narrated it."
"7001","Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Jarir al-Ramli narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Hisham al-Halabi narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, that he heard Muawiyah on the pulpit on the day of Ashura saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanding fasting this day. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Ubayd Allah ibn Amr; Ubayd ibn Hisham alone narrated it."
"7002","Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Jarir al-Ramli narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Yazid ibn Yusuf al-Sanani narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, from Makhul, from Umm al-Darda, from Abi al-Darda, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding His saying: And beneath it was a treasure belonging to them — he said: Gold and silver. No one narrated this hadith from Makhul except Yazid ibn Yazid ibn Jabir, nor did anyone narrate it from Yazid except Yazid ibn Yusuf; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone narrated it."
"7003","Muhammad ibn Sufyan ibn Jarir narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: Marwan ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Said ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Kab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding His saying: And he began striking their shanks and necks — he said: He cut their necks and shanks. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Said ibn Bashir."
"7004","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub al-Nasibi narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us: Umar ibn Muhammad narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would lighten the two rakahs of Fajr until I would say: He does not complete the Fatihat al-Kitab. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Muhammad except al-Walid ibn Muslim. And the well-known version is from the hadith of Muhammad ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amrah, from Aishah."
"7005","Muhammad ibn Abdus ibn Jarir al-Suri narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Zuhayr ibn Muhammad: Mansur ibn Safiyyah narrated to me, from his mother Safiyyah bint Shaybah, from Aishah, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw something he loved he said: Our Lord, by Your blessing righteous deeds are completed, to You be praise; and when he saw something he disliked he said: Praise be to Allah in every circumstance. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Zuhayr; al-Walid ibn Muslim alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain."
"7006","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us, saying: I read to al-Jarrah ibn Malih, from al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is tested with daughters and treats them well, they will be a shield for him from the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zubaydi except al-Jarrah ibn Malih."
"7007","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayyub narrated to us: Baqiyyah narrated to us, from Thabit ibn Ajlan, from Ata, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not fear mistakes for you, but I fear deliberate sins for you."
"7008","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us: Safwan ibn Salih narrated to us: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out visiting Sad ibn al-Rabi al-Ansari, whose house was in al-Aswaq. His wife spread for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a mat beneath a cluster of palm trees, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat and we sat with him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: A man of Paradise will now appear before you. Then Abu Bakr appeared. Then he said: A man of Paradise will appear before you. Then Umar appeared. Then he said: A man of Paradise will appear before you. Then Uthman appeared. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except al-Walid ibn Muslim."
"7009","Muhammad ibn Abdus narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Hisham narrated to us: Yahya ibn Yahya al-Ghassani narrated to us: Said ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Amr ibn Qays, from Adi ibn Adi, from Abi al-Darda who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: No guardian of three but will meet Allah with his right hand chained; his justice will free him or his injustice will bind him. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Abd al-Aziz except Ibrahim ibn Hisham."
"7010","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan al-Hamdani narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Shihab ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Mujahid, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: May Allah brighten a man who hears a saying from us and retains it, for many a carrier of knowledge has no understanding, and many a carrier of knowledge carries it to one more learned than he. This hadith is not narrated from Umayr ibn Qatadah al-Laythi except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar alone narrated it."
"7011","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Qattan narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Sumay narrated to us, from al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah, from Ata, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever builds a mosque seeking thereby neither show nor reputation, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Muthanna except Muhammad ibn Isa; Hisham ibn Ammar alone narrated it, and none narrated it from Ata, from Aishah, except Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi and al-Muthanna ibn al-Sabbah."
"7012","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us: Nafi al-Sulami narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who is the master? He said: That is Yusuf ibn Yaqub ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim. They said: Is there no master among your ummah? He said: Yes, a man given lawful wealth and granted generosity, who draws the poor near and complains little among people. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abbas except Ata, nor did anyone narrate it from Ata except Nafi Abu Hurmuz; Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi alone narrated it."
"7013","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn al-Durays al-Faydi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Fudayl ibn Ghazwan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Amr ibn Salamah who said: We were at a watering place by the road, and riders would pass us who had met the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so I memorized Quran from them until I had learned much Quran. My father went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of our tribe, and when they returned they said: We were ordered such-and-such and ordered such-and-such, and ordered that the one with the most Quran lead us. They looked at the people of the watering place, and I had the most Quran among them, so they put me forward, wearing a cloak that when I prostrated nearly reached my buttocks. A woman of the tribe said: Cover from us the backside of this reciter of yours. So they bought me a garment from this yarn, and a woman of the tribe cut it into a shirt for me and dressed me in it, and I rejoiced with it as I never rejoiced with anything. I used to lead them while I was eight years old. No one narrated this hadith from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym except Muhammad ibn Fudayl; Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Durays alone narrated it."
"7014","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Abu al-Khattab Hammad al-Dimashqi narrated to us, from Ruzayq Abu Abd Allah al-Alhani, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer in his house equals one prayer, his prayer in the mosque of the tribes equals twenty-five prayers, his prayer in the congregational mosque equals five hundred prayers, his prayer in al-Masjid al-Aqsa equals fifty thousand prayers, his prayer in the mosque of the Kabah equals one hundred thousand prayers, and his prayer in this mosque of mine equals fifty thousand prayers. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar alone narrated it."
"7015","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us: Maslamah ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri who said: Abd Allah ibn Kab ibn Malik said: My father said: When Allah accepted my repentance, I said: O Messenger of Allah, I know of no one whom Allah has blessed in truthfulness as He has blessed me, and part of my repentance is never to speak but truth as long as I live, and to give up all my wealth to Allah and His Messenger, for what He bestowed upon me. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A third of your wealth suffices you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Maslamah ibn Ulayy; Muhammad ibn Rumh alone narrated it."
"7016","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Muslim ibn Yahya al-Tai narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Nuh ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abi al-Zinad, from Ghalib, from Jabir who said: I entered upon Aishah while she wore a patched woolen wrap, and I said: Why do you not cast off this garment? She said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If it pleases you to meet me, do not cast off a garment until you patch it, and do not store food for a month. And I shall not change what he commanded me until I join him, Allah willing. This hadith is not narrated from Jabir ibn Abd Allah, from Aishah, except with this chain; Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it."
"7017","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Dhakwan al-Dimashqi narrated to us: Salm al-Khawwas narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Idris al-Khawlani, from Abi Thalabah al-Khushani who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade killing women and children. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; Salm al-Khawwas alone narrated it."
"7018","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us: Yaqub ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Abi Hurayrah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a platter steaming hot; he hastened his hand into it, then raised his hand and said: Allah has not fed us fire. This hadith is not narrated from Bilal, from Abu Hurayrah, except with this chain; Hisham ibn Ammar alone narrated it."
"7019","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abd al-Salam ibn Asim al-Razi narrated to us: al-Sabbah ibn Muharib narrated to us: Abu Abd Allah al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Abi al-Ahwas, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The ring of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was worn during the rule of Abu Bakr, during the rule of Umar, and during part of the rule of Uthman. It was over a well called Bir Aris when the ring fell into it; they drained the well but did not find it. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Masud except with this chain; al-Sabbah ibn Muharib alone narrated it."
"7020","Muhammad ibn Nasr al-Hamdani narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said al-Qattan narrated to us: Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir ibn Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), regarding His saying: And glorify the praise of your Lord before sunrise and before sunset — he said: Before sunrise is the dawn prayer, and before sunset is the Asr prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan, nor from Dawud except Yahya ibn Said; Muhammad ibn Musaffa alone narrated it."
"7021","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Abd al-Hamid ibn Issam al-Jurjani narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Sayf narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Ata, from Abd Allah ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: May Allah curse whoever reviles my Companions. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except Abd Allah ibn Sayf; Abd al-Hamid ibn Issam alone narrated it."
"7022","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj informed me, from Ata, that he heard Ibn al-Zubayr saying on the pulpit: When one of you enters the mosque while the people are bowing, let him bow when he enters, then walk bowing until he enters the row, for that is the Sunnah. Ata said: I saw him doing that. Ibn Jurayj said: And I saw Ata doing that. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ibn Wahb; Harmalah alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except with this chain."
"7023","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya al-Lakhmi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ayyub ibn Bashir who said: I heard Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pour over me water from seven skins from different wells until I go out to the people and entrust them. He said: So he came out with his head bound, until he ascended the pulpit, praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: A servant among the servants of Allah was given the choice between the world and what is with Allah, and he chose what is with Allah. None understood it except Abu Bakr, so he wept and said: We ransom you with our fathers, mothers and children. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Gently; the best of people to me in companionship and wealth is Ibn Abi Quhafah. Look at these doors opening into the mosque and close them, except the door of Abu Bakr, for I saw light upon it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Said ibn Yahya alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Muawiyah except with this chain."
"7024","Muhammad ibn Nasr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hafs al-Awsabi narrated to us: Said ibn Musa al-Azdi narrated to us: Rabah ibn Zayd al-Sanani narrated to us, from Mamar, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever persists in reciting Ya Sin every night, then dies, dies a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Mamar, nor from Mamar except Rabah, nor from Rabah except Said ibn Musa; Ibn Hafs alone narrated it."
"7025","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Habab al-Jallab al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Muhajir al-Marwazi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajjib narrated to us: Warqa ibn Umar ibn Kulayb narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Thawban who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Be upright though you cannot encompass all, and know that the best of your deeds is prayer, and none preserves ablution except a believer. No one narrated this hadith from Warqa except Yahya ibn Nasr ibn Hajjib."
"7026","Muhammad ibn Hammad ibn al-Jawzajani narrated to us: Said ibn Abd Allah Abu Salih al-Hamdani narrated to us: Abu Muadh al-Nahwi narrated to us: Hatim ibn Ismail narrated to us, from Bukayr ibn Mismar, whom I know only from Amir ibn Sad, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May Allah brighten a servant who hears my saying and retains it, for many a carrier of knowledge is not learned, and many a carrier of knowledge carries it to one more learned than he. This hadith is not narrated from Said except with this chain; Abu Muadh al-Nahwi alone narrated it."
"7027","Muhammad ibn Hammad narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Hafs narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abi Salih, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not engage in false bidding, do not hate one another, do not envy one another, do not turn away from one another, and be brothers as Allah commanded you. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Ibrahim ibn Tahman."
"7028","Muhammad ibn Yusuf ibn Amr ibn Yusuf al-Qumasi narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Isa al-Bistami al-Qumasi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Abi Taybah narrated to us, from Abi Taybah, from al-Amash, from Muslim ibn Subayh, from Masruq, from Abd Allah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If one of them would say: I seek refuge in Allah from Satan, his anger would go — or — his anger would subside. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash, from Abi al-Duha, from Masruq, except Abu Taybah. And people narrated it from al-Amash, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Sulayman ibn Surad."
"7029","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Musa al-Marwazi narrated to us: Mahmud ibn al-Abbas, companion of Ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us: Hushaym narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives four is given four, and its explanation is in the Book of Allah: whoever gives remembrance, Allah remembers him, for Allah says: So remember Me, I will remember you; and whoever gives supplication is given answer, for Allah says: Call upon Me, I will answer you; and whoever gives gratitude is given increase, for Allah says: If you are grateful I will surely increase you; and whoever gives seeking forgiveness is given forgiveness, for Allah says: Seek forgiveness from your Lord, indeed He is Forgiving. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Hushaym; Mahmud ibn al-Abbas alone narrated it."
"7030","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Marwazi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from his father, from Matar al-Warraq, from Ibn Nuhayk, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever frees a share of a slave must free the remainder; if he has no wealth, the slave works to earn his price."
"7031","And with the same chain: from Matar al-Warraq, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the dead is placed in his grave and his companions turn away from him — and he hears the sound of their sandals — two angels come to him, sit him up, and say: What did you used to say about this man? — meaning Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). As for the believer, he says: I bear witness that he is the servant of Allah and His Messenger. It is said to him: Look at your seat in the Fire; Allah has replaced it for you with a seat in Paradise. So he sees both."
"7032","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Harb narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from his father, from Matar, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It will be said to the disbeliever on the Day of Resurrection: What do you think — if you had the earth full of gold, would you ransom yourself with it? He will say: Yes. It will be said to him: You lie; you were asked for what is easier than that and you refused."
"7033","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ali ibn Hujr narrated to us: Manzur ibn Zuhayr al-Sadi narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I only recite qunut so that you supplicate your Lord and ask Him your needs. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Sharik, nor did anyone narrate it from Sharik except Manzur ibn Zuhayr; Ali ibn Hujr alone narrated it."
"7034","Muhammad ibn Ishaq al-Marwazi narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Said al-Darimi narrated to us: Ali ibn al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no divorce before marriage. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Hisham ibn Sad, nor from Hisham except Ali ibn al-Husayn; Ahmad ibn Said al-Darimi alone narrated it."
"7035","And with the same chain: Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Abi al-Aliyah, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his Companions came to Medina and the Ansar sheltered them, the Arabs shot at them from a single bow. Then was revealed: He will surely grant them succession in the land — the verse. This hadith is not narrated from Ubayy ibn Kab except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Said al-Darimi alone narrated it."
"7036","Muhammad ibn Jumuah ibn Khalaf Abu Quraysh al-Quhistani narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Idris al-Harawi narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Hayyaj ibn Bistam narrated to us, from his father, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Khalid ibn Alqamah, from Abd Khayr, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution three times three times. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Hayyaj; his son alone narrated it."
"7037","Muhammad ibn Jumuah Abu Quraysh narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Idris narrated to us: Khalid ibn al-Hayyaj narrated to us, from his father, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Sharik ibn Abd Allah, from Simak ibn Harb who said: I said to Jabir ibn Samurah: Did you sit with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes; he was long silent, and his Companions would recite poetry before him and discuss the accounts of their ancestors, and he would sometimes smile with them. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ishaq except al-Hayyaj ibn Bistam; his son alone narrated it."
"7038","Muhammad ibn Jumuah Abu Quraysh narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Tubbai narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam al-Urani narrated to us: Sallam al-Tawil narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a believer to abandon his brother for more than three days. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Saigh except Sallam al-Tawil; al-Qasim ibn al-Hakam alone narrated it."
"7039","Muhammad ibn Jumuah narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Idris narrated to us: Khalid ibn Hayyaj narrated to us, from his father, from Sufyan, from al-Awzai, from Bab ibn Umayr, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Thabit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) permitted selling araya by its estimated measure. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Hayyaj ibn Bistam; Khalid ibn Hayyaj alone narrated it, and none narrated it from al-Awzai except al-Thawri."
"7040","Muhammad ibn al-Ajam al-Sanani narrated to us: Hariz ibn al-Musallam narrated to us: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from his father, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Zadha n, from Ali, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a hair of his body unwashed, such-and-such will be done to him in the Fire. Ali said: From then I became hostile to my hair, and he used to drag his hair."
"7041","And with the same chain: from Ata ibn al-Saib, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn Amr who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) counting tasbih on his fingers."
"7042","And with the same chain: from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abi Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Abd Allah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah has not sent down a disease except that He sent down a cure for it; whoever knows it knows it, and whoever is ignorant of it is ignorant of it. No one narrated these hadiths from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad except his son; Jarir ibn al-Musallam alone narrated them."
"7043","And with the same chain: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The gates of heaven are opened on Monday and Thursday, and Allah forgives whoever does not associate anything with Him, except the two who have abandoned one another."
"7044","And with the same chain: from Ibn Jurayj, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he ordered cutting off bells. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid; Hariz ibn al-Musallam alone narrated them."
"7045","Muhammad ibn al-Ajam al-Sanani narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abi Ghassan al-Sanani narrated to us: Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Zaidah, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abd Allah ibn Salamah, from Ali who said: Nothing prevented the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from reciting Quran except janabah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyib except Uthman ibn Zaidah, nor from Uthman except Zafir; Ibn Abi Ghassan alone narrated it."
"7046","And with the same chain: Zafir narrated to us, from Israil, from Yunus, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: On buried treasure is the fifth. No one narrated this hadith from Zafir except Abd Allah ibn Abi Ghassan."
"7047","And with the same chain: Zafir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi, from al-Agharr ibn al-Sabbah, from Khalifah ibn Husayn, from Qays ibn Asim, that he embraced Islam and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he ordered him to bathe with water and lote. No one narrated this hadith from Zafir except Abd Allah ibn Abi Ghassan."
"7048","And with the same chain: Zafir narrated to us, from Sufyan al-Thawri, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abd Allah ibn al-Arqam al-Zuhri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When prayer comes and one of you needs the toilet, let him begin with the toilet. No one narrated this hadith from Zafir except Ibn Abi Ghassan."
"7049","And with the same chain: Zafir narrated to us, from Abi Yunus al-Qawi, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he believes in qadar, its good and its evil. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Yunus except Zafir; Ibn Abi Ghassan alone narrated it."
"7050","Muhammad ibn al-Ajam al-Sanani narrated to us: Hariz ibn al-Musallam narrated to us: Abd al-Majid narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Nafi, from al-Jarrah, freedman of Umm Habibah, from Umm Habibah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not accompany a company in which there is a bell. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abd al-Majid; Hariz ibn al-Musallam alone narrated it."
"7051","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti al-Sanani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray while she lay across before him like a bier."
"7052","Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Loyalty of emancipation belongs to whoever frees."
"7053","And with the same chain: from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When supper is served and prayer is established, begin with supper."
"7054","And with the same chain: from Aishah: That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would kiss while fasting."
"7055","And with the same chain: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Sad, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Shoot; may my father and mother be your ransom."
"7056","And with the same chain: from Yahya ibn Said, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Alqamah ibn Waqqas, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Deeds are only by intentions, and each man has only what he intended. Whoever emigrates to Allah and His Messenger, his emigration is to Allah and His Messenger; and whoever emigrates to a worldly gain he attains or a woman he marries, his emigration is to what he emigrated to."
"7057","Muhammad ibn Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Asim ibn al-Ahwal, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made a pact of brotherhood between the Emigrants and the Helpers in the house of Anas. No one narrated these hadiths from al-Qasim ibn Man except Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim ibn Juti alone narrated them."
"7058","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad al-Askari narrated to us: Bishr ibn Hilal al-Sawwaf narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah narrated to us: Abd Allah al-Danaj, Matar al-Warraq and Qatadah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the door of the house heading for the chamber, and heard people disputing about qadar, one saying: Did Allah not say in such-and-such verse? and another saying: Did Allah not say in such-and-such verse? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out of the door of the chamber as if pomegranate seeds had been burst upon his face, and said: Is this what you were commanded — or — is this what you were sent with? Those before you perished by such disputing; they struck parts of the Book of Allah against others. Allah commanded you a command, so accept it, and forbade you something, so refrain from it. People never afterward heard anyone speak about qadar until the days of al-Hajjaj; the first to speak about qadar was Mabad al-Juhani, and al-Hajjaj killed him. No one narrated this hadith from Abd Allah al-Danaj, Matar and Qatadah, from Anas, except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah."
"7059","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl al-Askari narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us: Hammad ibn Isa al-Juhani narrated to us: Hanzalah ibn Abi Sufyan narrated to us, from Salim ibn Abd Allah ibn Umar, from his father, from his grandfather Umar ibn al-Khattab, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that when he extended — or raised — his hands in supplication, he would not return them until he wiped his face with them. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Hammad ibn Isa al-Juhani alone narrated it."
"7060","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Bishr ibn Hilal narrated to us: Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abi Tariq, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who will take these words from me, act upon them, or teach them to one who acts upon them? Abu Hurayrah said: I said: I, O Messenger of Allah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took my hand and counted five therein, and said: Guard against the unlawful and you will be the most devout of people; be content with what Allah apportioned for you and you will be the richest of people; do good to your neighbor and you will be a believer; love for people what you love for yourself and you will be a Muslim; and do not laugh much, for much laughter kills the heart. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Abu Tariq; Jafar ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"7061","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us: Bakr ibn Abd Allah al-Laythi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Abi al-Malih ibn Usamah, from Jabir ibn Abd Allah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a wound and ordered that it be treated and retaliated, and gave a year's respite. No one narrated this hadith from Abi al-Malih except Abd Allah ibn Abi Humayd."
"7062","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abu Jamilah al-Kufi al-Mufaddal ibn Salih narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered Budayl al-Khuzai to announce in the days of Tashriq: Do not fast these days, for they are days of eating and drinking. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except al-Mufaddal ibn Salih."
"7063","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Waki narrated to us, from Abi al-Umays, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away without appointing a successor; had he appointed anyone he would have appointed Abu Bakr. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Mulaykah except Abu al-Umays."
"7064","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl narrated to us: Yazid ibn Hakim narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Yazid ibn Ibrahim al-Tustari and Abu al-Awwam al-Qattan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, may a man pray in one garment? He said: Do all of you find two garments? No one narrated this hadith from Imran al-Qattan except Yahya ibn al-Sakan; Yazid ibn Hakim alone narrated it."
"7065","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl narrated to us: Yazid ibn Hakim narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Hammad ibn Salamah and Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Abi Harun, from Abi Said who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People will come to you seeking knowledge; when they come to you, treat them well. No one narrated this hadith from Imran al-Qattan except Yahya ibn al-Sakan; Yazid ibn Hakim alone narrated it."
"7066","And with the same chain: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, regarding the saying of Allah Almighty: Hajj is well-known months. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dhu al-Qadah and Dhu al-Hijjah. Then: Whoever undertakes Hajj therein. Ibn Umar said: The talbiyah and ihram. Then: No sexual relations. That is intercourse with women. Then: Nor disobedience. That is abuse. Then: Nor dispute. That is argument. No one raised this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Muhajir except Sharik."
"7067","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Uqbah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade spreading a mat at the door of the house, and said: Remove it away from it somewhat. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Uqbah ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"7068","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Jafar narrated to us, from Umar ibn Nafi, from his father, from Ibn Umar who said: Umar ibn Nafi said: I know it only from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When one of you prays, let him pray in two garments; if he has only one garment, let him wrap it round and then pray, and do not wrap yourselves as the Jews wrap, for Allah is most deserving to be adorned for. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Nafi except Abd Allah ibn Jafar; Sahl ibn Uthman alone narrated it."
"7069","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Ali ibn Mushir narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from al-Shabi, from al-Harith, from Ali, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the eater of usury, its giver, its two witnesses, its scribe, the one who marries to make lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful, the tattooing woman and the tattooed woman, and the withholder of charity. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Ali ibn Mushir."
"7070","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Hubayb ibn Habib narrated to us, from Abi Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: Fatimah said to Ali: O son of my uncle, work and the millstone have wearied me, so speak to the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said to her: Yes. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to them next morning while they slept under one blanket, and put his leg between them. Fatimah said: O Prophet of Allah, work has wearied me; will you order a servant for me from what Allah granted you? He said: Shall I not teach you what is better for you than that? Glorify Allah thirty-three times, praise thirty-three times, and magnify thirty-four times; that is one hundred upon the tongue and one thousand in the balance, for Allah says: Whoever comes with a good deed shall have ten like it, up to one hundred thousand. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq except Hubayb ibn Habib — brother of Hamzah al-Zayyat."
"7071","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abbad ibn Bishr narrated to us: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not fear for my ummah a believer or a polytheist; as for the believer, his faith restrains him, and as for the polytheist, his disbelief subdues him. But I fear for them a hypocrite, eloquent of tongue, who says what they know and does what they deny. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Ishaq except Abbad ibn Bishr."
"7072","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Said ibn Maslamah al-Umawi narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cover between the private parts of the sons of Adam and the jinn, when one of them removes his garment, is to say: In the name of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Said ibn Maslamah and Said ibn al-Salt."
"7073","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Abu Kamil al-Jahdari narrated to us: Yazid Abu Khalid al-Baysari narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Umayyah: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: I was at the she-camel of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he entered ihram for the Farewell Hajj, and he said when his mount rose with him: Here I am, with Hajj and Umrah together. No one narrated this hadith from Usamah ibn Zayd except Abu Khalid al-Baysari; Abu Kamil alone narrated it."
"7074","Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Sahl al-Askari narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Mahbub al-Attar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Bazi Abi Khalid, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I had forbidden you joining dates together, but Allah has widened for you, so join them. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except Yazid ibn Bazi."
"7075","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Sahl ibn Uthman narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Muyassar Abu Sad al-Saghani narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas: That a woman came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) complaining that she was married unwillingly, so he removed her from her husband — she was previously married — and she married Abu Lubabah thereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Abu Sad al-Saghani; Sahl alone narrated it."
"7076","Muhammad ibn Yahya narrated to us: Yazid ibn Hakim narrated to us: Yahya ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, from Qays ibn al-Rabi: Habib ibn Abi Thabit narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a black slave girl and said: O Messenger of Allah, I owe a believing neck; will this suffice for me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah? She said: Yes. He said: Free her, for she suffices. No one narrated this hadith from Habib except Qays; and Hunayn is the freedman of al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib, grandfather of Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Hunayn."
"7077","Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Bahmard al-Askari narrated to us: Zunayj Abu Ghassan al-Razi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to us, from Abi Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This son of mine is a master, and Allah will reconcile through him between two groups of Muslims — meaning al-Hasan ibn Ali. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Zuhayr and Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"7078","Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Zunayj narrated to us: Abu Tumaylah Yahya ibn Wadih narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh who said: Ibn Jurmuz came seeking permission to see Ali, and he said: Give glad tidings to the killer of al-Zubayr of the Fire; I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Every prophet has a disciple, and al-Zubayr is my disciple. No one narrated this hadith from al-Husayn ibn Waqid except Abu Tumaylah."
"7079","And with the same chain: Abu Tumaylah narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn Musab, from Khalid al-Hadhdha, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: No man wore sandals nor rode a camel litter like Jafar ibn Abi Talib. No one narrated this hadith from Kharijah except Abu Tumaylah."
"7080","Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Bahmard narrated to us: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us: Nuh ibn Dhakwan Abu Ayyub narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one whose religion and character please you comes to you, marry him; unless you do, there will be trial in the land and widespread corruption. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Maqburi, except Nuh ibn Dhakwan; Amr ibn Asim alone narrated it. And Abd al-Hamid ibn Sulayman narrated it from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Ibn Wathimah al-Nasri."
"7081","Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Bahmard narrated to us: Abu al-Jawza Ahmad ibn Uthman narrated to us: Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us: Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seventy thousand of my ummah will enter Paradise without reckoning; they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, and do not take omens. Imran said: We were cauterized, yet we neither prospered nor succeeded. No one narrated this hadith from Abi Hurrah except Ubayd Allah ibn Abd al-Majid; Abu al-Jawza alone narrated it."
"7082","Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Zunayj narrated to us: Harun ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Muslim, from al-Zuhri, from Abi Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: Evil is the food to which the rich are invited and the poor are barred; and whoever is invited to it and does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger. Then he said: By Allah, I do not say it on my own. And people narrated it from al-Zuhri, from al-Araj."
"7083","Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us: al-Dahhak ibn Makhlad narrated to us: Mastur ibn Abbad Abu Hammam al-Hunai narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I left no need nor desire but I indulged it. He said: And do you bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah? He said: Yes. He said: This covers all that. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except Mastur ibn Abbad."
"7084","Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Raja ibn Muhammad al-Saqati narrated to us: Abd al-Samad ibn Abd al-Warith narrated to us: my father narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Asim ibn Damrah, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs when he has sufficiency amasses thereby embers of Hell. They said: What is sufficiency? He said: A night's supper. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Abi Thabit except al-Hasan ibn Dhakwan; Abd al-Warith alone narrated it."
"7085","Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Imran al-Asbahani narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Muadh al-Dabbi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and I do not know whether he added or omitted; when he finished it was said to him, and he prostrated two prostrations. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Muadh except Abu Dawud; Abd Allah ibn Imran alone narrated it."
"7086","Muhammad ibn Hafs ibn Bahmard narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Harith al-Razi narrated to us: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar al-Fuqaymi narrated to us: Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ashath, Sharik and Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abd Allah ibn al-Harith ibn Nawfal, from al-Muttalib ibn Rabiah who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling on one of his journeys by night, he heard the sound of singing. He said: What is this? He looked and there was a man vying with another man in singing. He said: O Allah, hurl them both into trial headlong, and thrust them into the Fire of Hell thrusting. No one narrated this hadith from Nusayr ibn al-Ashath except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar."
"7087","Muhammad ibn Hafs narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Harith al-Razi narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us: Sallam ibn Abi Muti narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Said ibn Jubayr, that a man asked Ibn Umar about the nabidh of jars, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked it. So Said went to Ibn Abbas and told him what Ibn Umar said, and he said: Ibn Umar spoke truth. No one narrated this hadith from Sallam ibn Abi Muti except Abd Allah ibn Yazid al-Muqri."
"7088","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj al-Askari narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaniyy narrated to us: Umar ibn Harun narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Salim, servant of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would make their heads into four braids; when they bathed they gathered it upon the middle of their heads and did not undo it. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar except Umar ibn Harun, and it is not narrated from Salim except with this chain."
"7089","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mihsan al-Ukkashi narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah narrated to us, from Abd al-Wahid ibn Qays who said: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: A group from Muzaynah, a group from Hudhayl and a group from Juhaynah came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, we set out to Mecca on foot, while people set out riding. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the walker is the reward of seventy Hajjes, and for the rider the reward of thirty Hajjes. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abi Ablah except Muhammad ibn Mihsan."
"7090","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Mansur al-Mashriqi, from al-Shabi, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought cheese in the expedition of Tabuk; he took the knife, cut, and said: Eat in the name of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Mansur except Ibrahim ibn Uyaynah, and none narrated it from al-Shabi except Amr ibn Mansur."
"7091","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Grant respite for the sake of Allah, grant respite; were it not for humble youths, bowing elders, suckling children and grazing beasts, punishment would be poured upon you pouring, then crushed crushing. No one narrated this hadith from Khuthaym except his son; Surayj alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain."
"7092","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: I said to Anas ibn Malik: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye his hair? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had not reached that. But Abu Bakr dyed with henna and katam. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Bishr ibn al-Walid."
"7093","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us: Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith, from al-Qasim, from Abi Umamah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among his Companions and said: Bathe on Friday; whoever bathes on Friday, it is expiation for what is between it and the next Friday plus three days. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn al-Harith except Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"7094","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi Saminah narrated to us: Abu Malik al-Jawdani narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has consumed my wealth? He said: You and your wealth belong to your father. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Jarir ibn Hazim; Abu Malik al-Jawdani alone narrated it."
"7095","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Surayj ibn Yunus narrated to us: Qurran ibn Tammam narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever among you can prostrate, let him prostrate; and whoever cannot, let him not raise anything to his forehead to prostrate upon, but his bowing and prostration is a nod with his head. No one narrated this hadith from Ubayd Allah ibn Umar except Qurran ibn Tammam; Surayj ibn Yunus alone narrated it."
"7096","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Nusayr ibn Abi Nusayr, from Ismail al-Suddi, from Rifaah ibn Shaddad who said: I entered upon al-Mukhtar ibn Abi Ubayd while two cushions were with him, and he said: O slave girl, bring a cushion. I said: Here is a cushion. He said: No; Jibril just rose from this one, and Mikail rose from this one. By Allah, nothing prevented me from striking him with my sword except a hadith Amr ibn al-Hamiq narrated to me. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever grants a man security for his life then kills him is in the Fire, even if the slain one was a disbeliever. No one narrated this hadith from Nusayr — in my view he is Nusayr ibn Abi al-Ashath — except Isa ibn Yunus."
"7097","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Said ibn Salim narrated to us: al-Salt ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying on the tiled floor wearing his sandals; he spat beneath his left foot, then rubbed it into the ground. No one narrated this hadith from al-Salt ibn Dinar except Said ibn Salim; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban alone narrated it."
"7098","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ribi ibn Hirash and Hilal ibn Yasaf, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a gathering of the Ansar in which a group of them sat; he greeted, they returned the greeting, but the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked sitting with them. They said: O Messenger of Allah, it is a gathering our fathers sat in during ignorance, and we loved to keep it alive and sit in it. He said: If you insist on doing so, then return greetings, lower your gazes, and guide the way. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Salih ibn Musa al-Talhi."
"7099","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Umar narrated to us: Wahb ibn Rashid al-Raqqi narrated to us: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: It was said: O Messenger of Allah, so-and-so did not sleep last night. He said: Why? It was said: A scorpion stung him. He said: Had he said when he went to his bed: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah from the evil of what He created, it would not have harmed him. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Wahb ibn Rashid."
"7100","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from Zakariyya ibn Hakim, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salamah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray two rakahs after his witr while sitting. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Zakariyya ibn Hakim and Maymun ibn Musa al-Marai."
"7101","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban narrated to us: Talhah ibn Sinan narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Abd Allah ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Aishah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sometimes call for lunch and not find it, so he would impose fasting upon himself. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Najih except Layth, nor from Layth except Talhah ibn Sinan; Abd Allah ibn Umar ibn Aban alone narrated it."
"7102","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaniyy narrated to us: Amr ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of adultery, for in it are four traits: it removes beauty from the face, cuts off provision, angers the Most Merciful, and brings eternity in the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Amr ibn Jumay."
"7103","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Abi al-Faraj narrated to us: Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata al-Khaffaf narrated to us: Rashid Abu Muhammad al-Himmani narrated to us, from Abi Harun, from Abi Said al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told them on the night he was taken by night: I ascended with Jibril to the lowest heaven, and there I saw an angel called Ismail, keeper of the lowest heaven, with seventy thousand angels before him, each angel accompanied by troops of one hundred thousand. And he recited this verse: And none knows the hosts of your Lord but He. No one narrated this hadith from Rashid al-Himmani except Abd al-Wahhab al-Khaffaf."
"7104","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr al-Sarraj narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumaniyy narrated to us: Shuayb ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, from Aishah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, all your wives have entered the House except me. He said: Go to your kinsman, to Shaybah, and let him open the door for you and enter it. So I sent to him: The Prophet of Allah has permitted me to have the door opened for me so I may enter it. He said: Did the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) command you that? I said: Yes. So he took the keys and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, did you command Aishah to have the door opened for her? He said: Yes. He said: By Allah, I never opened it at night in ignorance or Islam. He said: Do what you used to do and leave what you did not do; and go, O Aishah, and pray two rakahs in the Hijr, for part of it is from the House, and your people fell short in funds so they left part of the House out. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn al-Saib except Shuayb ibn Safwan."
"7105","Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Bakr narrated to us: Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us: al-Mushamil ibn Milhan narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kharraz, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, your saying: Every intoxicant is unlawful — so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Drink, but when it ferments, leave it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Nadr Abi Umar except al-Mushamil."
"7106","7100 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bakr narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Anbasah ibn Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, from al-Dakhil ibn Iyas, from his uncle Hilal ibn Siraj, from Mujjaah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave Mujjaah ibn Murarah of Banu Salma land in al-Yamamah called al-Awzah. He said: And he wrote for him a document to that effect: From Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), to Mujjaah ibn Murarah of Banu Salma, I have given you al-Awzah, so whoever opposes me regarding it, then the Fire. And Yazid wrote it. This hadith is not narrated from Mujjaah except with this chain; Anbasah alone transmitted it."
"7107","7101 - Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bakr narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjadah narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ziyad narrated to us, from Israil, from Simak ibn Harb, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, that it reached Ali that a people in Basra had apostatized from Islam, so he sent for them, and they were brought to him, so he lavished food upon them for two Fridays, then he invited them to Islam, but they refused, so he dug a pit for them, then he stood over it and said: I shall surely fill you with fat and flesh, then he had them brought, struck their necks, threw them into the pit, then threw firewood over them and burned them, then he said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. Suwayd ibn Ghafalah said: When he left, I followed him and said: I heard you saying: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. He said: Woe to you, around me are ignorant people, but when you hear me saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, then for me to fall from the sky is dearer to me than to say about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Israil, and none from Israil except al-Hasan ibn Ziyad al-Lului; al-Hasan ibn Hammad alone transmitted it."
"7108","7102 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb al-Askari narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Hajjaj al-Sami narrated to us, Bashshar ibn al-Hakam narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A righteous quality may be in a man, so Allah sets right all his deeds through it; a man's purification for his prayer expiates his sins through his purification, and his prayer becomes supererogatory."
"7109","7103 - And with the same chain: from Thabit, from Anas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met Abu Dharr and said: O Abu Dharr, shall I not guide you to two qualities which are lighter on the back and heavier in the scale than any others? He said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Upon you be good character and long silence, for by the One in Whose Hand is the soul of Muhammad, no creature has done a deed dearer to Allah than them. No one narrated these two hadiths from Thabit except Bashshar ibn al-Hakam."
"7110","7104 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Dahir ibn Nuh al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Shuayb ibn al-Habhab, from Abu al-Aliyah, that the Mother of the Believers Aishah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us the choice, and it was not a divorce. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aliyah except Shuayb, and none narrated it from Shuayb except Hammad ibn Zayd; Dahir ibn Nuh alone transmitted it."
"7111","7105 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Khalil ibn Said al-Ubulli narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, from Amr ibn Ubayd and Wasil ibn Ata al-Ghazzal, from al-Hasan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Samurah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abd al-Rahman, do not ask for leadership, for if you ask for it you will be left to it, and if you do not ask for it you will be helped with it; and if you swear an oath and then see something else better than it, do what is better and expiate for your oath. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil ibn Ata except Imran ibn Abi Uthman; al-Khalil ibn Said alone transmitted it."
"7112","7106 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, from Abu Burdah, from his father who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed the dawn prayer he would raise his voice until he made his Companions hear, saying: O Allah, set right for me my religion which You have made a protection for me, three times; O Allah, set right my world in which You have placed my livelihood, three times; O Allah, set right for me my Hereafter to which You have made my return, three times; O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, three times; O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pardon from Your punishment, three times; O Allah, I seek refuge in You from You, three times; O Allah, none can withhold what You give, and none can give what You withhold, and the fortune of the fortunate does not avail him against You. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except Ishaq ibn Yahya; Yazid ibn Iyad alone transmitted it."
"7113","7107 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sulayman al-Qaflani narrated to us, Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to me, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not boast of your fathers who died in the Jahiliyyah; do you boast of them? Shall I not tell you? The example of your fathers who died in the Jahiliyyah is like that of a king who built a palace on the roadside, placed food in it, and appointed men over it, and said: Let no one pass except that he partakes of this food of mine. So when a man passed in fine appearance and fine clothes, they would go to him, cling to him, and bring him until he ate of that food; and when a man came in poor appearance and worn clothes, they would prevent him. When that went on for long, Allah sent an angel from among the angels in poor appearance and worn clothes, so he passed by their sides, and they rose against him and pushed him away. He said to them: I am hungry, and food is only made for the hungry. They said: No, the food of the king is eaten only by the righteous. So they pushed him away and he left. Then he came in a handsome form and fine clothes, and passed as if not wanting them, far from them, so they went to him, clung to him, and said: Come, partake of the food of the king. He said: I do not want it. They said: We will not leave you; if it reaches the king that one like you passed and did not partake of his food, it will grieve him, and we fear some punishment from him may befall us. So they compelled him and brought him in until they brought him to the food and presented the food to him, so he did like this with his clothes into the food. They said: What are you doing? He said: I came to you in poor appearance and worn clothes, and I told you I was hungry, but you prevented me; and I came to you in fine appearance and fine clothes, so you compelled me and overcame me. Indeed the food was only earned by these clothes of mine, not by me, so let them eat. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Sulayman al-Qaflani; Shayban alone transmitted it."
"7114","7108 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Attar narrated to us, Yazid ibn Tamim ibn Zayd narrated to us, my father Tamim ibn Zayd narrated to me, Abu Marhum al-Sadi narrated to me, al-Muntasir ibn Umarah narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sells a house and does not replace it, he will not be blessed in its price. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain; Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad alone transmitted it."
"7115","7109 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Bakr ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Said ibn Yazid al-Bajali narrated to us, Amir ibn Sharahil al-Shabi narrated to us that he entered upon Fatimah bint Qays, the sister of al-Dahhak ibn Qays, whose husband was Abu Amr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn al-Mughirah al-Makhzumi, and she said: Abu Amr ibn Hafs sent me my divorce while he was setting out with an army to Yemen, so I asked his guardians for maintenance and lodging, but his guardians said: He sent us nothing about that, nor did he instruct us. So I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, Abu Amr ibn Hafs sent me my divorce, and I sought lodging and maintenance, but his guardians said: He sent us nothing. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Maintenance and lodging are only for a woman when her husband still has the right of return over her; if she is not lawful for him until she marries another husband, then she has neither maintenance nor lodging. No one narrated this hadith from Said ibn Yazid except Bakr ibn Bakkar."
"7116","7110 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Sallam ibn Miskin narrated to us, Ismah Abu Hukaymah narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ubayy ibn Kab who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not teach you what Jibril, peace be upon him, taught me? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, forgive me my mistake and my intent, my jest and my earnestness, and do not deprive me of the blessing of what You have given me, and do not test me in what You have withheld from me. This hadith is not narrated from Ubayy ibn Kab except with this chain; Sallam ibn Miskin alone transmitted it."
"7117","7111 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Israil narrated to us, Waki ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Salih, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay, from Abu Mujahid and Abu Mudillah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: We said: What is with us, O Messenger of Allah, that when we are with you our hearts are in the Hereafter, but when we return that leaves us? He said: If you remained when you return as you are with me, the angels would visit you in your houses and shake hands with you with their palms; and if you did not commit sins, Allah would bring a creation who commit sins, then He would forgive them. I said: O Messenger of Allah, tell us about Paradise, what is its building? He said: A brick of gold and a brick of silver, its mortar is musk, its pebbles are pearls and rubies, and its soil is wars and saffron; whoever enters it will live forever and not die, and enjoy bliss and not suffer; their clothes will not tear, and their youth will not perish. There are three whose supplication is not rejected: the just ruler, the fasting person until he breaks his fast, and the supplication of the oppressed, which Allah raises above the clouds on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Rufay except al-Hasan ibn Salih, and none from al-Hasan except Waki; al-Hasan ibn Israil alone transmitted it."
"7118","7112 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qattan al-Razi narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Razi narrated to us, from his brother Talhah ibn Sulayman, from al-Fayyad ibn Ghazwan, from Zubayd al-Yami, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab passed by Muadh ibn Jabal while he was sitting at the grave of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) weeping, and said: O Muadh, what makes you weep? Perhaps you remembered your brother; if you remembered him, he is indeed worthy of that. He said: No, but something I heard from him in this sitting of mine, or in this place of mine, made me weep; he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says: A little showing off is association; Allah loves the pious, the hidden, the innocent, who when absent are not missed, and when present are not recognized; their hearts are lamps of guidance; they emerge from every black dark tribulation. No one narrated this hadith from Zubayd except al-Fayyad ibn Ghazwan, and none from al-Fayyad except Talhah ibn Sulayman; Ishaq ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"7119","7113 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Taraifi narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik: that when one of his daughters was proposed to, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would sit by the curtain and say: So-and-so proposes; if she remained silent, her silence was her consent, and if she disliked, she would poke at the veil, and that was dislike from her. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit except Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Husayn; Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman alone transmitted it."
"7120","7114 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, Habib ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Ibn Talhah ibn Musarrif narrated to us, from his father, from Murrah al-Tayyib, from Abu Bakr al-Siddiq who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Talhah ibn Musarrif except his son. And thus Habib ibn Farrukh narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Abi Talhah, from his father, from Murrah; and al-Hakam ibn Yala ibn Ata narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Talhah, from his father, from Abu Mamar, from Abu Bakr."
"7121","7115 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi, from Salim, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats anything of this meat, let him wash his hands. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except al-Wazi; al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab alone transmitted it."
"7122","7116 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Wahb ibn Hafs narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid, from Amr ibn Dinar: that he accompanied Ibn Umar on a journey, and whenever Suhayl rose he would say: May Allah curse Suhayl, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He was a tithe-collector who wronged them and seized their wealth unjustly, so Allah transformed him into a shooting star and placed him where you see. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ibrahim ibn Yazid."
"7123","7117 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Judhuyi narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Husayn al-Muallim Abu Bishr narrated to us, narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Buraydah al-Aslami, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about a man praying while sitting, and he said: Whoever prays standing, it is better; and whoever prays sitting has half the reward of the one standing; and whoever prays lying has half the reward of the one sitting."
"7124","7118 - And with the same chain: from Abdillah ibn Buraydah, from Samurah ibn Jundub who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) over a woman who died in childbirth, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for the prayer over her at her middle. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ubayd ibn Husayn al-Muallim except Ibrahim ibn Suwayd."
"7125","7119 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Umar ibn Hafs al-Shaybani narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl becomes obligatory. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except Humayd ibn Hilal, and none from Humayd except Hisham, and none from Hisham except al-Ansari."
"7126","7120 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Munir ibn Maymun al-Basri narrated to us, Abbad ibn Suhayb narrated to us, Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise boasted over the Fire and said: I am better than you. The Fire said: Rather I am better than you. Paradise said to it inquiring: And how? It said: Because in me are the tyrants, and Nimrod, and Pharaoh. So it was silenced, and Allah revealed to it: Do not submit; I shall surely adorn your two corners with al-Hasan and al-Husayn. So it swayed as a bride sways in her chamber. No one narrated this hadith from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful except Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah; Abbad ibn Suhayb alone transmitted it."
"7127","7121 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Aslami narrated to us, from Utbah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah ibn Masud, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Said ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ammar ibn Yasir, that he was afflicted with janabah and had no water with him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: It suffices you to wipe your face and your hands with dust, one strike for the face and one strike for the hands. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Umays Utbah ibn Abdillah except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad."
"7128","7122 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf narrated to us, Said ibn Nuh al-Dubai narrated to us, Khalid ibn Makhlad and Ahmad ibn al-Ashath al-Dubayyan narrated to me, from Husayn ibn Harb ibn Husayn al-Dubai, from Abu Jamrah Nasr ibn Imran al-Dubai, from his grandfather Nuh ibn Makhlad, that he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in Makkah, and he asked him: From whom are you? He said: I am from Banu Dubayah ibn Rabiah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of Rabiah is Abd al-Qays, then the clan you are from; and he sent him with an army to Yemen. This hadith is not narrated from Nuh ibn Makhlad except with this chain; Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaf alone transmitted it."
"7129","7123 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mualla al-Adami narrated to us, Ismail ibn Subayh al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Uways narrated to us, from Thawr ibn Yazid and Musa ibn Maysarah, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about the mustahadah, and he said: That is a kick of Satan in her womb. No one narrated this hadith from Thawr and Musa ibn Maysarah except Abu Uways; Ismail ibn Subayh alone transmitted it."
"7130","7124 - And with the same chain: Ismail ibn Subayh narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Hassan narrated to us, Nafi narrated to me, from Ibn Umar, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O son of Adam, there are two things, neither of which belongs to you: I have made for you a share in your wealth when I seize you by your throat, to purify you with it and cleanse you; and the prayer of My servants upon you after your term ends. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Mubarak ibn Hassan; Ismail ibn Subayh alone transmitted it."
"7131","7125 - And with the same chain: Ismail ibn Subayh narrated to us, from Ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from his father, from Muslim al-Batin, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas who said: How many years do you count for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after his emigration? They said: Ten in Makkah and ten in Madinah. He said: And do you indeed say that? We said: Yes. He said: Yes, and five and seven, in accordance with what Ali ibn Abi Talib said."
"7132","7126 - And with the same chain Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Uthman who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent a delegation to Yemen, and appointed over them a commander from among them, who was the youngest of them. He stayed days without setting out, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met a man from among them and said: O so-and-so, what is with you, have you not set out? He said: O Messenger of Allah, our commander complains of his leg. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to him and blew upon him: In the name of Allah and with Allah, I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power from the evil of what is in it, seven times, so the man was cured. An elder said to him: O Messenger of Allah, do you appoint him over us while he is the youngest of us? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned his recitation of the Quran. The elder said: O Messenger of Allah, were it not that I fear I would take it as a pillow and not uphold it, I would have learned it. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Learn it, for the example of the Quran is like a bag you filled with musk, then tied its mouth; if you open it, the scent of musk spreads, and if you leave it, it remains musk placed aside. Likewise is the example of the Quran when you recite it, or it is in your chest. No one narrated these two hadiths from Salamah ibn Kuhayl except his son Yahya; Ismail ibn Subayh alone transmitted them."
"7133","7127 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Dirham narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some people in Makkah, and they began winking behind his back, saying: This is the one who claims he is a prophet, and with him is Jibril. So Jibril poked with his finger, and something like a fingernail fell upon their bodies, and it became sores, until they stank, and no one could come near them. So Allah sent down: Indeed, We are sufficient for you against the mockers. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Yazid ibn Dirham; Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi alone transmitted it."
"7134","7128 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Rawh ibn Ata ibn Abi Maymunah narrated to us, from his father, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows a funeral and prays over it has a qirat of reward; and if he waits for it until its matter is concluded, he has two qirats. They said: And what is the qirat, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Like Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah except his son."
"7135","7129 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ararah al-Sami narrated to us, Fadalah ibn Husayn al-Attar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When any of you is brought perfume, let him take some of it; and when he is brought sweets, let him take some of it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Fadalah ibn Husayn; Ibrahim ibn Ararah al-Sami alone transmitted it."
"7136","7130 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, al-Salt ibn Masud al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Wazi ibn Nafi al-Uqayli, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Khawlah bint al-Yaman, the sister of Hudhayfah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no good in gatherings of women, except at a dead person, for when they gather they say this and that. This hadith is not narrated from Khawlah bint al-Yaman except with this chain; al-Salt ibn Masud alone transmitted it."
"7137","7131 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah al-Dabbi narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, my uncle Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Abu Hazim al-Ansari who said: On the day of Badr, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought a leather mat of spoils, and it was said: Shade yourself with it, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Would you like that there be shaded between you a shade of Fire on the Day of Resurrection?"
"7138","7132 - And with the same chain: from Abu Hazim al-Ansari who said: On the day of Badr, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in the shade, while his Companions were in the sun fighting, so Jibril came to him and said: Are you in the shade while the Muslims are in the sun fighting? So he stood and moved to the sun. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Amash except Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad, and none narrated them from Mansur except his nephew al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad; Ahmad ibn Abdah alone transmitted them."
"7139","7133 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abdah narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Numan narrated to us, Ali ibn al-Hazawwar narrated to us, from Nufay Abu Dawud, from Imran ibn Husayn and Abu Barzah, they both said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at a funeral, and he saw some people who had thrown off their cloaks walking in shirts, so he said: Do you take up the deed of the Jahiliyyah? Or do you imitate the practice of the Jahiliyyah? I had intended to supplicate against you a supplication by which you would return in other than your forms. So the people took their cloaks and wore them. This hadith is not narrated from Imran ibn al-Husayn and Abu Barzah except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Abdah alone transmitted it."
"7140","7134 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Asim, the companion of Abu Asim, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Humran ibn Abdillah narrated to me, Shuayb ibn Salim narrated to me, from Jafar ibn Abi Musa, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray two rakahs after Asr, and Abu Musa used to pray them. This hadith is not narrated from Jafar ibn Abi Musa except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr alone transmitted it."
"7141","7135 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Ijli narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Uthman al-Wasiti narrated to us, Amr ibn Ubayd narrated to me, from Abu Mashar, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Khuzaymah ibn Thabit who said: I bear witness concerning the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he fixed for the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident a day and a night, wiping over the khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Ubayd except Umar ibn Abi Uthman."
"7142","7136 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Muhammad Abu Wail narrated to us, Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, Isa ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Abdillah al-Ayli, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever gives iftar to a fasting person has the like of his reward, without diminishing anything from his reward; and whatever deed of righteousness he does, his reward is like that of the owner of the food, as much as the strength of the food is in him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Hakam ibn Abdillah al-Ayli, and none from al-Hakam except Isa ibn Ibrahim; Kathir ibn Hisham alone transmitted it."
"7143","7137 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman in ihram shall not wear a face veil, nor a burqa, nor gloves. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi."
"7144","7138 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, Musab ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Dates were gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he distributed them; then I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was eating eagerly, and I saw that only hunger had driven him to that. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Musab ibn Sulaym."
"7145","7139 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Safwan al-Thaqafi narrated to us, Quraysh ibn Anas narrated to us, Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Hazim ibn Hatim Abu Hatim, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: O Allah, I ask You for beneficial knowledge, and I seek refuge in You from knowledge that does not benefit. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Quraysh ibn Anas."
"7146","7140 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Ubayd ibn Waqid al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Umarah al-Azdi, Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril: Which places are best? He said: I do not know. He said: Then ask your Lord about that. He said: So Jibril, peace be upon him, wept, then said: O Muhammad, is it for us to ask Him? He is the One who informs us of what He wills. So he ascended to the heaven, then came to him and said to him: The best of places are the mosques, the houses of Allah on earth. He said: Then which places are worst? So he ascended to the heaven, then came to him and said: The worst of places are the markets. No one narrated this hadith from Ammar ibn Umarah, who is Abu Hashim the companion of saffron, except Ubayd ibn Waqid."
"7147","7141 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Israil narrated to us, Abdillah ibn al-Muttalib al-Kufi narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever hastens to the sneezer with praise will be spared the pain of the flank, and will never complain of his tooth. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Israil, and none narrated it from Israil except Abdillah ibn al-Muttalib; al-Hasan ibn Israil alone transmitted it."
"7148","7142 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Mihran narrated to us, Abu Muti al-Balkhi narrated to us, from Abu Hanifah, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Masud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no cutting except for ten dirhams. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hanifah except Abu Muti al-Hakam ibn Abdillah."
"7149","7143 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Harb ibn Surayj narrated to us, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali: that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the Farewell Hajj, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to relieve himself, returned, performed wudu, and wiped over his khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Sirin except Khalid al-Hadhdha, and none from Khalid except Harb ibn Surayj; Shayban ibn Farrukh alone transmitted it."
"7150","7144 - Muhammad ibn Nuh ibn Harb narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim ibn Hakim al-Ijli narrated to us, Umar ibn Abi Uthman al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Amr ibn Ubayd and Wasil ibn Ata al-Ghazzal, from al-Hasan, from Abu Hurayrah who said: My beloved Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) advised me with three, which I shall not leave until I die: fasting three days of every month, ghusl on Friday, and not sleeping except upon witr. No one narrated this hadith from Wasil al-Ghazzal except Umar ibn Abi Uthman; Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Ijli alone transmitted it."
"7151","7145 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Shayban ibn Farrukh narrated to us, Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The begging of the rich is a disgrace on his face on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ashhab except Shayban, and Waki."
"7152","7146 - Muhammad ibn Nuh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yusuf al-Samti narrated to us, Abd al-Nur ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu al-Shatha, from Buraydah al-Aslami, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Your Lord loves four of your Companions, and commands you to love them. Some of his Companions said: Name them for us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Indeed Ali is among them. Then when the next day came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, the group whom Allah told you that He loves them, and commanded you to love them? He said: Indeed Ali is among them. Then when the third day came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, the group whom Allah told you that He loves them, and commanded you to love them? He said: Indeed Ali is among them. He said: Ali, and Abu Dharr al-Ghifari, and al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad, and Salman al-Farisi. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman except Abd al-Nur ibn Abdillah; Khalid al-Samti alone transmitted it."
"7153","7147 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji al-Tustari narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Salamah ibn Bishr ibn Sayfi narrated to us, Abbad ibn Kathir al-Ramli narrated to us, Abu Iqal narrated to us, he said: I heard Anas ibn Malik saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make tharid even with water. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Dawud ibn Rashid alone transmitted it."
"7154","7148 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab al-Harrani narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Hatim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taken by night, he said: O Jibril, my people accuse me and do not believe me. He said: If your people accuse you, then Abu Bakr believes you. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Thawban except al-Mughirah ibn Siqlab; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal alone transmitted it."
"7155","7149 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Jami al-Sukkari narrated to us, Amr ibn Jarir narrated to us, Ismail ibn Abi Khalid narrated to us, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim who said: I heard Abu al-Darda saying to his son: O my son, let the mosque be your house, for the mosques are the houses of the pious; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever has the mosque as his house, Allah guarantees him rest, mercy, and passage over the Sirat to Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Amr ibn Jarir."
"7156","7150 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Bahr al-Tustari narrated to us, Bashshar ibn Qirat narrated to us, from Abu Muslih, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the end of time, a woman will come to her private chamber and find her husband transformed into an ape, because he did not believe in qadar. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Abu Muslih; Bashshar ibn Qirat alone transmitted it."
"7157","7151 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Muawiyah ibn Hisham narrated to us, Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Riba has seventy-two doors, the least of them is like a man committing adultery with his mother; and the worst of riba is a man prolonging himself in the honor of his brother. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Umar ibn Rashid, and none narrated it from Umar ibn Rashid except Muawiyah ibn Hisham; and it is not narrated from al-Bara except with this chain."
"7158","7152 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Bishr ibn al-Walid al-Kindi narrated to us, Abu Yusuf al-Qadi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq Abu Umayyah, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, from Sad ibn Malik who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The neighbor has more right to his adjoining property. No one narrated this hadith from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah except Abd al-Karim."
"7159","7153 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Hammad ibn Bahr al-Tustari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Muzani narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Abu al-Safar narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi who said: Jarir ibn Abdillah said: Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away when he was sixty-three, and Abu Bakr passed away when he was sixty-three, and Umar was killed when he was sixty-three. Muawiyah said: And this is my day, I am fifty-seven for it, then he lived after that twenty years. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Safar except Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq."
"7160","7154 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ismail ibn Ibrahim al-Tarjumani narrated to us, Hakim ibn Nafi al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The two prostrations of forgetfulness in prayer suffice you for every addition and deficiency. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Hakim ibn Nafi."
"7161","7155 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Abi Khalaf narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), leaving my father to follow me, and he said: There shall now appear a cursed man. So I feared it might be my father, and I kept going out and in, until al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As appeared. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Umamah except Uthman ibn Hakim."
"7162","7156 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Abu Mamar al-Qatii narrated to us, Hushaym narrated to us, from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a thread with which he would remind himself. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Hamid ibn Jafar except Hushaym; Abu Mamar alone transmitted it."
"7163","7157 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Isa al-Misri narrated to us, Dimam ibn Ismail narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Habib and Musa ibn Wardan narrated to me, from Kab ibn Ujrah who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day and saw him changed. He said: I said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, why do I see you changed? He said: Nothing has entered my stomach that enters the stomach of a living creature for three days. He said: So I went, and there was a Jew watering his camels, so I watered for him, for each bucket a date, and I gathered dates and brought them to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: From where is this for you, O Kab? So I told him. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you love me, O Kab? I said: May my father be sacrificed for you, yes. He said: Poverty hastens to one who loves me faster than a flood to its depths; and a trial will befall you, so prepare a shield for it. He said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) missed him and said: What happened to Kab? They said: He is ill. So he went out walking until he entered upon him, and said to him: Receive glad tidings, O Kab. His mother said: Congratulations to you of Paradise, O Kab. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who is this woman swearing upon Allah? He said: She is my mother, O Messenger of Allah. He said: What do you know, O mother of Kab? Perhaps Kab said what does not benefit him, or withheld what would not suffice him. No one narrated this hadith from Kab except Musa ibn Wardan; Dimam alone transmitted it."
"7164","7158 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Dawud ibn Rashid narrated to us, Fuhayr ibn Ziyad narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Remain upon your dwellings; emigration has ended, but there is jihad and intention, and if you are called to march forth, then march forth. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Ibrahim ibn Yazid; Fuhayr ibn Ziyad alone transmitted it."
"7165","7159 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Asfati narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Ibrahim ibn Abi Amr al-Ansari narrated to us, Dawud ibn Mutarrif narrated to us, from his father who said: We were with Anas ibn Malik, then the people met him having returned from Friday, so he entered a house and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is not shy before people is not shy before Allah. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Abdillah ibn Ibrahim alone transmitted it."
"7166","7160 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Shabab al-Usfuri narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fadalah narrated to us, from his father, from Alqamah ibn Abdillah al-Muzani, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A man may free of his slave what he wishes: if he wishes a third, and if he wishes a fourth, and if he wishes a fifth; there is no constraint between him and Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Fadalah except Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad; Shabab alone transmitted it."
"7167","7161 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Sahl ibn Ubayd al-Tustari narrated to us, Suwayd ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that one of the household of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) borrowed silver and lost it, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) guaranteed it. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Suwayd, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"7168","7162 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah narrated to us, from Kurz ibn Wabarah al-Harithi, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi who said: Qadar was mentioned before Abdillah ibn Umar, so Abdillah said: The Qadariyyah were cursed upon the tongues of seventy prophets, among them our Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); and when the Day of Resurrection comes, and Allah gathers the people on one plain, a caller will call, making the first and the last hear: Where are the adversaries of Allah? So the Qadariyyah will rise. No one narrated this hadith from Kurz ibn Wabarah except Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyyah; Muhammad ibn Bakkar alone transmitted it."
"7169","7163 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah Abu al-Mughirah al-Asha, Hakimah bint Ghaylan narrated to me, from her husband Yala ibn Umayyah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me to a woman, either a hairdresser or a perfumer, then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me dyed with saffron and said: Will you not wash this filth off you? Or: Will you not wash this impurity off you? So I came to a river and bathed until the water turned yellow, then I entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with its trace still upon me, so he said: Go and wash it. So I went and washed it, and it did not go until I washed it with dust. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah except Ghaylan, and none from Ghaylan except Yala ibn al-Harith; his son Yahya alone transmitted it."
"7170","7164 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim ibn Suwayd al-Nakhai narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam al-Nakhai narrated to us, from Abu Burdah, from Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Khatmi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The punishment of my ummah is in its worldly life. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn al-Hakam except Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Ibrahim ibn Suwayd; Uthman ibn Abi Shaybah alone transmitted it."
"7171","7165 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Abi Bukayr narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Wasil narrated to us, al-Aswad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Abdi narrated to me, from Hissan ibn Kahil, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No orphan sits with people at their bowl but a devil draws near their bowl. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Yazid ibn Harun alone transmitted it."
"7172","7166 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, Marwan ibn al-Tayyib al-Wasiti narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan al-Wasiti narrated to us, from Nahshal ibn Said, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Wudu before food and after it is among what removes poverty, and it is from the sunnahs of the messengers. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal alone transmitted it."
"7173","7167 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab al-Dallal narrated to us, Jarir ibn Ayyub al-Bajali narrated to us, Abu Ishaq al-Hamdani narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: On the Day the earth will be changed to other than the earth: A white earth as if it were silver, in which no unlawful blood was shed, and in which no sin was committed. No one raised this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Jarir ibn Ayyub; Abu Attab alone transmitted it."
"7174","7168 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mufaddal al-Harrani narrated to us, Sahl ibn Hammad Abu Attab narrated to us, Musa ibn Ubayd Abu Harun al-Kufi narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Silah ibn Zufar who said: When Abu Bakr was mentioned before Ali, he would say: You mention the forerunner, you mention the forerunner; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, we never raced to any good but Abu Bakr preceded us to it."
"7175","7169 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Dibaji narrated to us, Hammad ibn Bahr al-Tustari narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Harun ibn Antarah narrated to us, from his father, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa al-Ashari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah says: O My servants, all of you are astray except whom I guide, and weak except whom I strengthen, and poor except whom I enrich, so ask Me and I shall give you. If the first of you and the last of you, your humans and your jinn, your living and your dead, your moist and your dry, gathered upon the heart of the most pious servant of My servants, they would not increase in My dominion the wing of a gnat; and if the first of you and the last of you, your living and your dead, your moist and your dry, gathered upon the heart of the most wicked servant of My servants belonging to Me, they would not decrease from My dominion the wing of a gnat. That is because I am One; My punishment is a word, and My mercy is a word. So whoever is certain of My power to forgive, it will not seem great in My Self to forgive his sins, even if they are many. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Murrah except Harun ibn Antarah; his son Abd al-Malik alone transmitted it."
"7176","7170 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam al-Tustari narrated to us, Abdillah ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, Ismail ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sad ibn Hisham, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Witr is three like the three of Maghrib. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Ismail ibn Muslim; Abu Bahr alone transmitted it."
"7177","7171 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, Yahya ibn Hammad narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abu Wail, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Some peoples will come to the Hawd, and I shall recognize them, then they will be snatched away from me, so I shall say: From me. Then it will be said: You do not know what they innovated after you. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Abu Awanah, and none from Abu Awanah except Yahya ibn Hammad; Yaqub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi alone transmitted it."
"7178","7172 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Abi al-Nadr narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his head to the ceiling of the house, he would say: Glory be to You, O Allah, and with Your praise; I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. Aishah said: So I asked him about them? He said: I was commanded with them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hakam except Amr ibn Abd al-Jabbar, and none from Amr ibn Abd al-Jabbar except al-Nadr ibn Abi al-Nadr; Abu al-Ashath alone transmitted it."
"7179","7173 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Ishaq ibn Sulayman al-Fulfuli al-Misri narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, from Abu Wahb, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Jibril on the night he was taken by night: My people will not believe me. So Jibril said to him: Abu Bakr will believe you, and he is al-Siddiq. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Yazid ibn Harun; Ishaq ibn Sulayman alone transmitted it."
"7180","7174 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, my father informed me, al-Salt narrated to us, from al-Hasan who said: I heard Jundub narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: How will you be with peoples whose leader enters Paradise, while his followers enter the Fire? They said: O Messenger of Allah, even if they do like their deeds? He said: Even if they do like their deeds. They said: And how can that be, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The leaders enter Paradise for what preceded for them, and the followers enter the Fire for what they innovated. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except al-Salt ibn Mihran; Ali ibn Nasr alone transmitted it."
"7181","7175 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Umar al-Waqidi narrated to us, Yaqub ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Sasaah narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Sasaah, from Abbad ibn Tamim, from Abdillah ibn Zayd who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The key to prayer is purification, its inviolability is the takbir, and its permissibility is the taslim. This hadith is not narrated from Abdillah ibn Zayd except with this chain; al-Waqidi alone transmitted it."
"7182","7176 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Azdi narrated to us, Wahb ibn Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Jamil ibn Murrah narrating, from Abu al-Wadi who said: I saw Ali, and he saw a man wearing a glistening cloak, and said: I suspect there is silk in it. He said: So he joined its two sides and tore it, and said: I have not envied you for it, but I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbidding silk and brocade. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Wadi except Jamil ibn Murrah, and none from Jamil except Jarir ibn Hazim; Wahb ibn Jarir alone transmitted it."
"7183","7177 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Salm ibn Rashid al-Hujaymi narrated to us, Amr ibn Ziyad al-Bahili narrated to us, Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu al-Zara, from Abdillah ibn Masud who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Follow the two after me, Abu Bakr and Umar. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ibn al-Mubarak, and none from Ibn al-Mubarak except Amr ibn Ziyad al-Bahili; Ibrahim ibn Salm ibn Rashid alone transmitted it."
"7184","7178 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, Habban ibn Hilal narrated to us, Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Uthman ibn Khuthaym, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Sahlah bint Suhayl, that Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, used to enter upon her while she had laid aside her garments, so she mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Suckle him, you will become unlawful to him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Khuthaym except Wuhayb ibn Khalid; Habban alone transmitted it."
"7185","7179 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mamar narrated to us, Hammad ibn Masadah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Abi Abdillah, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from Dhakwan, from Aishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray upon a mat. No one narrated this hadith except Hammad ibn Masadah. And the well-known is from the hadith of Hammad ibn Salamah."
"7186","7180 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Raqqam narrated to us, Habib ibn Bishr, the maternal brother of Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi, narrated to us, Said ibn Sufyan al-Jahdari narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Abu al-Malih ibn Usamah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent, during the days of Mina, a man upon a red camel, who called out: O people, these are days of eating and drinking, so do not fast. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Malih, from his father, except Ubaydillah ibn Abi Humayd. And Abu Qilabah narrated it, from Abu al-Malih, from Nubayshah."
"7187","7181 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Daqiqi al-Tustari narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bahr al-Jundaysaburi narrated to us, Amr ibn Mansur al-Qaysi narrated to us, Mubarak ibn Fadalah narrated to us, Amr ibn Dinar, the steward of the family of al-Zubayr, narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abdillah ibn Umar who said: My father narrated to me, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril promised me an appointment, and he was late for me, then he said: What kept me from that was a bell sound or an image in a house. No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak ibn Fadalah except Amr ibn Mansur; Sahl ibn Bahr alone transmitted it."
"7188","7182 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Ishaq al-Daqiqi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Bahr narrated to us, Salm ibn Sulayman al-Dabbi narrated to us, Abu Hurrah narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Sasaa ibn Muawiyah, from Abu Dharr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There are no two Muslims for whom three children die, who have not reached puberty, except that Allah admits them both to Paradise by virtue of His mercy to them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurrah except Salm ibn Sulayman."
"7189","7183 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad al-Tai narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every amusement is disliked except a man playing with his wife, his walking between the two targets, and his training his horse. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad; Hafs ibn Amr al-Rabbali alone transmitted it."
"7190","7184 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Said ibn Anbasah narrated to us, from Faid Abu al-Warqa, from Abdillah ibn Abi Awfa who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prostrating upon the fold of the turban. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abi Awfa except with this chain; Mamar ibn Sahl alone transmitted it."
"7191","7185 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Qasim al-Hashimi narrated to us, al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad al-Tai narrated to us, Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, clothe me. So he turned away from him. He said: O Messenger of Allah, clothe me. He said: Do you not have a neighbor who has two spare garments? He said: Yes, more than one. He said: Then Allah will not join you and him together in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except al-Mundhir ibn Ziyad, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"7192","7186 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Tamam narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, from al-Mughirah ibn Shubah, that he ate garlic and prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then when they finished, the smell of garlic was found from him, so he said: What is this? He said: I complained of my chest, so I ate it. So he did not rebuke him. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Ubaydillah ibn Tamam; Mamar ibn Sahl alone transmitted it."
"7193","7187 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The scholars of this ummah are two men: a man to whom Allah gave knowledge, so he spent it for the people, took no greed upon it, and did not purchase a price with it; so the fish of the sea, the beasts of the land, and the birds in the sky seek forgiveness for him, and he comes to Allah as a noble master until he accompanies the messengers; and a man to whom Allah gave knowledge, but he withheld it from the servants of Allah, took greed upon it, and purchased a price with it; so he will be bridled on the Day of Resurrection with a bridle of Fire, and a caller will call: This is the one to whom Allah gave knowledge but he withheld it from the servants of Allah, took greed upon it, and purchased a price with it; and likewise until the reckoning is finished. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awwam except Abdillah ibn Khirash, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain."
"7194","7188 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us: Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us: Musa ibn Dawud narrated to us, al-Qasim ibn Man narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik that Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a trace of yellow perfume upon him, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: What is this? And that was his expression when he wanted to ask about something. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I married. He said: For how much? He said: For the weight of a date-stone of gold. He said: Give a wedding feast even with a sheep. Anas said: We estimated it as a quarter dinar. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Man except Musa ibn Dawud."
"7195","7189 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Abdillah ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no prayer after Fajr, except the two rakahs before the Fajr prayer. No one narrated this hadith from al-Musayyib except al-Awwam; Abdillah ibn Khirash alone transmitted it."
"7196","7190 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Hudhayfah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Slaughter with anything that severs the jugular veins and sheds blood, except the tooth and the nail. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Taymi except al-Awwam; Abdillah ibn Khirash alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Hudhayfah except with this chain."
"7197","7191 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Jawhari narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Nahwi al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Abu Hammam Muhammad ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Dajjal will emerge from the direction of Isfahan. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Abu Hammam; Ibn Mansur al-Ahwazi alone transmitted it."
"7198","7192 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh al-Ahwazi narrated to us, Mamar ibn Sahl narrated to us, Ubaydillah ibn Tamam narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Walid Abu Bishr, from Ibn Shaghaf, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is more honored before Allah than the believer. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Ubaydillah ibn Tamam; Mamar ibn Sahl alone transmitted it."
"7199","7193 - Muhammad ibn Mahmawayh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam narrated to us, Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man to gather firewood upon his back and sell it is better for him than to ask people. No one narrated this hadith from al-Musayyib ibn Rafi except al-Awwam; Abdillah ibn Khirash alone transmitted it."
"7200","7194 - And with the same chain: from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No man cuts off the right of a Muslim man by his oath except that Allah forbids Paradise to him and makes the Fire obligatory for him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim al-Taymi except al-Awwam; Abdillah ibn Khirash alone transmitted it."
